    <node id="AI">
      <data key="d0">AI</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">AI (Artificial Intelligence) encompasses a rapidly developing family of technologies that enable machines to mimic human intelligence. This includes capabilities such as learning, problem-solving, and performing tasks traditionally requiring human intellect. AI is deployed across various sectors and geographical boundaries, enhancing operations, improving predictions, and personalizing digital solutions. 

As AI evolves, it necessitates regulatory oversight and innovative approaches to ensure its responsible integration, including the implementation of safeguards and risk mitigation measures. Due to its significant societal and environmental impacts, the development of AI should focus on human values and well-being. While AI offers numerous benefits, it also poses potential risks and challenges depending on its application, emphasizing the need for careful management and ethical considerations in its deployment.&lt;SEP&gt;AI, or Artificial Intelligence, refers to the simulation of human intelligence processes by machines, especially computer systems, which are increasingly relevant in various industries.&lt;SEP&gt;AI (Artificial Intelligence) encompasses high-risk systems and general-purpose models that are subject to specific regulatory requirements within the EU.&lt;SEP&gt;AI refers to artificial intelligence, which has beneficial applications but also poses risks of misuse in areas such as manipulation and social control.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-58a25c0dd884625561b248cf275f154e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14f663363e3d8f01aa5c0b361bddc380&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae8bdbb57af24d78fe2313201571bea7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cdf1c7e7ad7fe2c6b1b8f1b0b12db35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a975f3ad5ea339c199a21dd569a7acb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3177468233ec37ad2a71dc38caa17377&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8462fb6c49f462e0c2199ce80842ebde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7114fa80a4a18326b68b2fd61f65c047&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cde8f1eff9bf42001a30603a860556d1</data>
