      <data key="d5">1747657905</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CE Marking">
      <data key="d0">CE Marking</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">CE Marking is a certification mark that signifies that a product, including high-risk AI systems, meets all necessary regulatory compliance requirements established by the European Union (EU). This mark indicates conformity with EU safety, health, and environmental protection standards, which are essential for the marketability of such systems within the European Economic Area. By obtaining CE Marking, high-risk AI systems demonstrate that they comply with the required regulatory standards, thereby allowing them to be sold in the market. Overall, CE Marking is crucial for ensuring that products adhere to EU regulations, contributing to consumer safety and environmental protection.&lt;SEP&gt;CE marking is a certification indicating that a product conforms to safety, health, and environmental protection standards within the European Economic Area.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-43942ba7283893ebf128acb858a20c58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fc356102e8bbeed5152b8bb0cda2ff6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73fd7e801c2d8d41361f6b16b45c6ed0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c237e1a0b42db9afb10cc8a045dbb751&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddb5ca2a2f12bb39286916d398b70ed9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68d6983d829937a84d37118dacc3e39c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29241e99bddf5af77eca441d2d8dbc1b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_48.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_23.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_24.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_16.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_129.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_83.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747658049</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation">
      <data key="d0">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation encompasses a comprehensive legal framework designed to govern the deployment and use of various systems, particularly high-risk artificial intelligence (AI) technologies, alongside addressing the implications for individual rights. Specifically highlighted in Regulation (EU) 2019/1020, this framework is instituted by the European Union (EU) to ensure effective market surveillance and compliance within multiple sectors, including civilian applications, law enforcement, military, defense, and national security.

The Regulation aims to foster a thriving internal market while prioritizing health, safety, and the protection of fundamental rights. It mandates uniform execution by all EU member states, emphasizing compliance with specific operational obligations directed at high-risk AI technologies. Essential to this framework is its focus on promoting transparency and ethical practices in AI applications through legal guidelines that facilitate oversight. National competent authorities are appointed to maintain impartiality and enforce these regulations effectively, while member states are compelled to systematically monitor compliance and designate appropriate authorities for this purpose.

Furthermore, the Regulation outlines detailed compliance standards necessary for the operation of AI systems within the EU marketplace, placing significant obligations on AI providers to adhere to strict quality management systems. It addresses critical matters surrounding biometric data, advocating for rigorous measures to ensure safety and mitigate systemic risks linked to AI technologies. 

In the context of law enforcement, the Regulation requires individuals to disclose their identities in relevant situations to enhance accountability in AI technology deployment. It sets forth parameters governing AI's use in content generation and manipulation, reinforcing non-discriminatory practices. Employers also bear explicit responsibilities under this regulation regarding worker information and consultation, particularly concerning the implementation of high-risk AI systems in workplace settings.

In summary, the Regulation functions as a pivotal framework for the compliance, assessment, and ethical oversight of AI technologies across the EU, devoted to safeguarding individual rights and managing law enforcement implications while clearly delineating the responsibilities of all stakeholders involved in its implementation.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulations include requirements and obligations related to the evaluation and compliance of AI systems, specifically addressing high-risk classifications.&lt;SEP&gt;The Regulation refers to legislation aimed at ensuring compliance and facilitating expertise for SMEs and other providers in the market.&lt;SEP&gt;The Regulation refers to the legal framework guiding the assessment and compliance procedures for high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation outlines the authoritative guidelines and compliance requirements that high-risk AI systems must follow to ensure safety and proper functioning.</data>
