    <node id="Union">
      <data key="d0">Union</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">The Union primarily signifies the European Union (EU), a significant political and economic coalition comprised of member states predominantly located in Europe. As a collective entity, it operates within a structured legal framework aimed at fostering collaboration among its members through a series of agreed laws and regulations. The Union focuses on key areas such as law enforcement, migration, border control, and is pivotal in adhering to international trade agreements, including those established by the World Trade Organization, enhancing its influence in global trade dynamics.

The Union enacts a diverse array of laws and regulations that affect several domains, including data protection, non-discrimination, consumer protection, and competition law. These measures ensure consistent governance across its jurisdiction, ultimately aiming to safeguard individual rights, uphold democracy, promote the rule of law, and enhance environmental protection. It emphasizes cooperative governance and regulatory policies among its member states to address common challenges and further shared interests, particularly surrounding consumer protection and disability rights.

A particularly notable focus of the Union is on the governance and regulation of artificial intelligence (AI). It has developed a comprehensive framework intended to harmonize regulations regarding AI technologies, with specific provisions for high-risk AI systems and public interest considerations. This framework mandates compliance with common legal standards for AI system providers, extending accountability to entities outside its jurisdiction, thereby reinforcing the EU's centralized authority over regulations and standards related to general-purpose AI models. Overall, the Union represents a cohesive alliance dedicated to creating harmonized legislation and regulations that both protect rights and improve market operations within its framework, particularly concerning the regulation of AI systems and ensuring compliance with applicable laws.</data>
