    <node id="SMEs">
      <data key="d0">SMEs</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">SMEs (Small and Medium-sized Enterprises) encompass businesses of varying sizes that are considered smaller than large corporations, often pivotal in innovation and economic development.&lt;SEP&gt;SMEs (Small and Medium-sized Enterprises) represent a category of commercial interests that must be included in the advisory forum for balanced representation.&lt;SEP&gt;SMEs, or Small and Medium-sized Enterprises, are a key focus for national competent authorities regarding legislation on AI systems and compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;Small and Medium Enterprises (SMEs) are defined as businesses that have a limited number of employees and revenue, typically falling below certain thresholds established by regulations. These enterprises, which encompass a wide range of organizations with registered offices or branches within the European Union, play a vital role in the economy, particularly in innovation and technological development. SMEs are significantly smaller in scale compared to larger corporations and operate within the AI ecosystem, where their specific interests and needs are increasingly considered in the development of codes of conduct for AI governance.

SMEs face unique challenges, including the need for regulatory compliance and the drive for innovation, which can considerably impact their growth and sustainability. Recognizing these challenges, regulatory frameworks have been established to prioritize SMEs, particularly in providing access to AI regulatory sandboxes. These sandboxes create supportive environments that allow SMEs to develop and test innovative technologies without incurring prohibitive costs, thus facilitating their advancement in the market.

Moreover, SMEs are subjected to tailored compliance requirements designed to support their technological growth while ensuring adherence to regulatory standards. Compliance is closely monitored to maintain their economic viability and promote standards and compliance development within the broader entrepreneurial ecosystem. Overall, SMEs are essential stakeholders in the economic landscape, receiving targeted measures to enhance their success and enable them to thrive in a competitive environment, while their contribution to innovation positions them as crucial players in shaping the future of technology.&lt;SEP&gt;SMEs stands for small and medium-sized enterprises, which are significant stakeholders considered in the guidelines for AI regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-40f3761e589fb7702938fd4fbbecfdcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7365f713d09e74d49090cb78cb3e19b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36cb0fd5abf1b169a8aa13021f58c7b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e24261c10195e33e965bd7e966c33337&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0271020749ae70ce56cbd607a6f6662a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-184360d53ae652d7f48a919e168f375a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-712b56cbfc73c46eacde9204fa4e5c49&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d42aaf56c15be020feabced14d2409d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-064e3e5273a81cd8d9a47da9a3f51240&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f76666cf495bb0f0810313fe42e2c882&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65c79a1c0cb37c10df906970d376029d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b235644744fa597c94328afbeaa7e56b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d6ed86abb2e8f0e12897e923d1e9964&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc97d8ad7f3aa0522d885f92ee323822&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e76c1f88e5810a7e79cf9527486831e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de5a0c7f560be7dcbe4301aed20bcb98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aca56f82b70892874784bcec5c2bb2c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95424b9dff57302628c496570b4baff4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e7b8a0eb1cb8c27dfd822da15429870&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5928be36056ac91865bd3e4d596159e</data>
