    <node id="Public Authorities">
      <data key="d0">Public Authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Public Authorities are government entities that operate within the public sector and are responsible for the deployment of high-risk artificial intelligence (AI) systems. These authorities are required to register their use of such systems in a designated EU database, as mandated by regulatory frameworks. Their role includes ensuring compliance with relevant regulations governing the use of high-risk AI technologies. Additionally, Public Authorities may implement quality management rules for the use of these AI systems across various levels of government. It is important to note that Public Authorities in third countries may be exempt from certain regulations due to cooperative agreements with the European Union. Overall, they face specific compliance requirements under the Regulation when utilizing high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Public Authorities are government entities that receive notifications of serious incidents and coordinate responses at the national level.&lt;SEP&gt;Public Authorities are governmental entities that may engage in the use of AI systems and are subjected to Union regulations in their operations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-44eafa4c222bb60e722eca942751cf7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b8c1122e1044e4445aa96d7fa6d5b6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b0c31436f0e7ce27ce5952aa2bf9ae5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8e23760d52ebfb589b4de63afe8ab83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2806e288e0b71013209c4ad85ecaa38b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3105f8ed20ed5608a4571fe7b1d8f942&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f116a95954c59b63ce3149e6283ed8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e78bce1eaa5df9c186492b5e1482218</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_22.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_81.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_73.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_177.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_131.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_111.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_2.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_49.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747464661</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Quality Management System">
      <data key="d0">Quality Management System</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A Quality Management System is a structured set of policies, procedures, and processes that organizations implement to ensure product quality and regulatory compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;Quality management systems are frameworks established by providers to ensure compliance with regulations and standards for high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The Quality Management System is a structured system that organizations implement to ensure consistent quality in their products and services, including AI technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;The Quality Management System is a structured system that organizations implement to ensure quality compliance and improvement.&lt;SEP&gt;A Quality Management System is a structured system which ensures that an organization's products or services meet customer quality requirements and regulatory compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9b7fd511ed97ef1a87c9783c3425b7d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68d6983d829937a84d37118dacc3e39c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac68c725e087cb7c659f2dd75f0a6e34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44eafa4c222bb60e722eca942751cf7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e4f07f79ad3c90c82b86c0a02d0fae9</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_17.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_81.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_16.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_63.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_173.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657861</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Sectoral Union Law">
      <data key="d0">Sectoral Union Law</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Sectoral Union law refers to specific regulations governing various sectors, including those related to the quality management of high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-44eafa4c222bb60e722eca942751cf7d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_81.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Post-Market Monitoring System">
      <data key="d0">Post-Market Monitoring System</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A Post-Market Monitoring System involves activities carried out by providers to gather and analyze data from the use of AI systems in the market.&lt;SEP&gt;The Post-Market Monitoring System is a legislative framework designed to ensure the ongoing safety, compliance, and performance assessment of high-risk artificial intelligence (AI) systems following their market introduction. This system is referenced in Article 72 and involves the collection of data to analyze potential risks associated with these AI technologies once they are deployed. It mandates ongoing evaluation and reporting procedures to monitor the behavior of high-risk AI systems, ensuring they continue to meet established safety and performance standards. Providers are responsible for implementing this system to oversee the compliance of their AI products, thereby safeguarding users and enhancing public trust in technology.&lt;SEP&gt;A post-market monitoring system is a crucial component where providers must analyze interactions between AI systems to address risks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c237e1a0b42db9afb10cc8a045dbb751&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f56b40e98f8949a37c3ab283b01f7050&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44eafa4c222bb60e722eca942751cf7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ca7c773df7242c37f506b8ad3db475b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99c78ffcf815fa82f05dcb7dc5871e1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac68c725e087cb7c659f2dd75f0a6e34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54948128ea5a4b84a219d7dbaa346a50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c32bc5fa5cdfa35a393a42535dc4fdfb</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_17.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_9.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_72.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_81.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_155.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657278</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Obligations">
      <data key="d0">Obligations</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Obligations encompass the range of responsibilities and legal requirements that AI model providers are mandated to fulfill. These obligations are designed to ensure compliance with copyright law and other regulatory frameworks established by governing bodies, such as the Commission. They particularly emphasize the duties of providers of high-risk AI systems, ensuring that they operate within relevant legal parameters. Additionally, obligations include specific requirements for detecting and labeling artificially generated or manipulated content, as well as adherence to the stipulations set forth to avoid penalties. Overall, obligations signify the comprehensive responsibilities that AI providers must uphold to align with existing laws and regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3034aa8ff1b6d41ac6e0b8ff655b76ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af991f85166d6ddfbbf84e4a73207d3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32556db3a80f72f1db354810bba21be7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae3ab8a3b5c5d0c61e8b99fa718913b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c087216cbefba4022c0cdbe838e30f19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44eafa4c222bb60e722eca942751cf7d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_108.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_162.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_112.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_50.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_81.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_169.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657430</data>
    </node>
    <node id="National or Regional Level">
      <data key="d0">National or Regional Level</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">National or regional levels refer to the different administrative divisions where public authorities may establish rules for quality management systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-44eafa4c222bb60e722eca942751cf7d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_81.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union Law">
      <data key="d0">Union Law</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Union Law refers to the body of laws that guide the member states of the European Union, particularly regarding the implementation of directives like 2016/680.&lt;SEP&gt;Union Law refers to the comprehensive body of legislation and regulations established by the European Union (EU) that governs various areas, including artificial intelligence (AI) compliance, safety standards, and the use and processing of biometric data. It encompasses legal frameworks that integrate with AI regulation, significantly impacting its enforcement and applicability across EU member states.

A core aspect of Union Law is its commitment to safeguarding individual rights and freedoms, particularly in contexts where AI systems are involved in decision-making processes. The legislation mandates transparency regarding how personal data is managed, ensuring compliance with legal standards, especially when individuals are affected by AI outcomes. Union Law distinguishes between high-risk and low-risk AI applications, providing specific guidelines for their deployment, management, and oversight, which includes introducing administrative fines and enforcement measures to ensure adherence to these regulations.

Moreover, Union Law plays a crucial role in the lawful processing and classification of biometric data, contributing to enhanced safety standards throughout the EU. It also governs legal metrology, ensuring the accuracy of measurements used in commercial transactions, thus upholding the integrity of commerce within the region. The framework enhances governance and accountability among member states by ensuring conformity to established treaties and regulations, fortifying the protection of fundamental rights, non-discrimination, consumer protection, and competitive practices.

In addition, Union Law addresses public interests and access to public spaces, thereby balancing innovation and the protection of rights across the EU. It includes provisions relevant to copyright and data protection rights, particularly concerning AI training, reflecting its comprehensive scope in addressing contemporary legal challenges in technology and commerce. Overall, Union Law establishes a robust regulatory environment that seeks to protect citizens' rights while fostering innovation within the EU.&lt;SEP&gt;Union law refers to regulations and legal frameworks established by the European Union to ensure compliance in various sectors, including data protection and AI governance.&lt;SEP&gt;Union Law refers to the body of regulations that govern the functioning of the European Union, particularly in relation to digital services and AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-737358b61293029e1a6d7326160654fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b31c82fb046f107cbfab945a92431bbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb0291da832d9defa94aaf2262ad3761&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72cfde8a7c3c94fdf1dc93c4253bec9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbcf833252ce65fd6a1d8bd1f5a6efc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe76292b9a553c383dab6b0a4a67cee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c4d08c48923bc3e8bff8968fd67a799&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e853663a3f2d06a9cfea8582e10f089&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c28a81721b7de3ef4442495cc499b1cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4988a00689afb1245e0f0ce4ceef5921&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7114fa80a4a18326b68b2fd61f65c047&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28efea7f8fe5945cce5b7be57e88efe7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8833999c9ef9aa31a007f2e77ffea02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ffd8df9d8eb9625dca23bc5f974e025&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-727225adfedcad573a12c2ed92e8ee1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0044fdddd0a21caecd46a12639588d98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3105f8ed20ed5608a4571fe7b1d8f942&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f1adc61864fb9c4d0f971c9290506f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-445327adc051facf545b6358f6f01466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-431ae031d4ead528e84df75526b0f1dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6adb64ff4e7b459fa1df815eac98b096&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85bb41c1db2d2e1883172e505d5f7b71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50be48c46c67191e901c756873069fcb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71f538bc77dea56a19150de3c7514990&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-599d61ad7be34e2603c3fef13f2ff8dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1ab686ea2085e0bf2cc7ea2cb5eb270&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19ac689968d1b5ce1db014f781096bd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a68b9cb2eff595118d2af9313b6c89f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08ef4cc90d0e3e23ebc122fef44151a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fde742696dfc1372a034cc9cadcb58d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b65e9562dd645622f1390ba1863fee19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b235644744fa597c94328afbeaa7e56b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d08b537f9a5bb2b4f4bbdf442ba39bdd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a350089bbf860c041d514aa2041d9455&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2315cd7abb88dee440f081de5430a32f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1eea61d03ab615ac5f518e77cd220c1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15eee417af0ebe299ed66be76a0b845a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20ac675fffdeba0fbc242b392d3af8da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ed67e673a6fe0a3c79a41bb9102d44b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50beca99a2207706ee9f0ad17a4205ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc662d7e26079b23ad5010b8671bfb7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-800752b66b6fe0cd70bb0290efc2fbbe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3070277451614bdc67954ec8735dd80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad1a115533e7d3b3ced9ea8e2e87b0e2</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_10.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_9.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_94.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_119.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_59.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_67.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_171.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_31.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_63.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_45.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_10.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_30.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_17.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_2.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_57.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_5.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_9.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_54.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_96.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_77.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_157.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_107.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_19.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_73.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_25.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_74.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_59.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_86.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_141.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_58.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_5.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_7.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_60.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_137.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_70.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747658082</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Charter">
      <data key="d0">Charter</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Charter enshrines fundamental rights, including nondiscrimination, data protection, privacy, and rights of the child.&lt;SEP&gt;The Charter, specifically referring to the Charter of Fundamental Rights of the European Union, enshrines essential rights and fundamental freedoms that are crucial for governance, particularly in the context of AI systems. It outlines key principles including democracy and the rule of law, and explicitly addresses rights related to data protection, dignity, privacy, and non-discrimination. The Charter serves as a foundational document, guiding the actions and regulations of the Union concerning rights and freedoms, while also ensuring the protection of rights associated with freedom of expression and the arts. Overall, it represents a comprehensive framework that aims to safeguard fundamental rights in the increasingly significant realm of artificial intelligence technologies and their applications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4acea71d2f59038573b7ec13db4ad10b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e284955c1d36330bd14d117bb417611&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0455405f9e173535e78c4ea589745cf4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41cdee30f8345bc3690d876d77e6845c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14f663363e3d8f01aa5c0b361bddc380&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ded1c99cfd152513a4ef07b96a9c5de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1eea61d03ab615ac5f518e77cd220c1d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_63.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_134.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_28.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_176.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_48.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_2.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_7.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747658099</data>
    </node>
    <node id="National Law">
      <data key="d0">National Law</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">National Law refers to the comprehensive legal framework established by individual Member States, governing various aspects of law enforcement and the use of biometric systems. It encompasses legal statutes and regulations that ensure compliance with fundamental rights while effectively interacting with or aligning with Union law related to artificial intelligence and data protection. Additionally, National Law sets the legal standards concerning the use of biometric data and embodies frameworks designed to protect the rights and freedoms of individuals and entities. Furthermore, it pertains to the legal frameworks enacted by individual countries that influence the accessibility of various spaces.&lt;SEP&gt;National law complements Union law by addressing the specific regulations surrounding biometric data use within individual countries.&lt;SEP&gt;National Law refers to the legal framework and statutes enacted by a Member State to govern its territory and activities.&lt;SEP&gt;National Law refers to the legislative framework that governs activities at the country level, ensuring regulations are compliant with local statutes.&lt;SEP&gt;National Law refers to the legal frameworks that govern activities within individual member states of the European Union, complementing Union Law.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-13b35a74627bd926656242d6545e09a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19ac689968d1b5ce1db014f781096bd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc0db03f57b007cfc458657e88e273ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffc59c087d680631c2a594779449f195&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b65e9562dd645622f1390ba1863fee19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb040a8b4e6e3fa6f26776f560b6591c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3070277451614bdc67954ec8735dd80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67ecee9ae9852fb675f5c9c9cb2f2de6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d08b537f9a5bb2b4f4bbdf442ba39bdd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1eea61d03ab615ac5f518e77cd220c1d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_167.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_35.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_170.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_57.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_5.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_54.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_63.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_37.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_19.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_30.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657689</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Personal Data">
      <data key="d0">Personal Data</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Personal Data refers to any information relating to an identified or identifiable person, which is critical in the context of biometric identification and data protection laws.&lt;SEP&gt;Personal data refers to any information relating to an identified or identifiable individual, which market surveillance authorities can access to perform their duties.&lt;SEP&gt;Personal data refers to any information that relates to an identified or identifiable individual. This type of data is critical in the context of data protection regulations, and it encompasses any information capable of identifying a person. Personal data is subject to strict regulations, particularly under frameworks such as the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and other related directives, which are designed to safeguard users' privacy and rights. Additionally, personal data requires careful handling in compliance with legal frameworks, especially in the context of artificial intelligence systems, highlighting the importance of its governance and processing to ensure the security and privacy of individuals.&lt;SEP&gt;Personal data refers to any information that relates to an identified or identifiable natural person, as defined under the GDPR.&lt;SEP&gt;Personal data refers to information that can be used to identify individuals, which may be used ethically or otherwise in AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7ef570a9dfbda3c55d0d5bcc36fd77c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-699b82035d71a633a86a67090e5a61e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a46250ea72037444e96653239f2893b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fde742696dfc1372a034cc9cadcb58d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe76292b9a553c383dab6b0a4a67cee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-800752b66b6fe0cd70bb0290efc2fbbe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f736e1ff707eaba05079b0f194d8a123&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4988a00689afb1245e0f0ce4ceef5921&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0639a0bd62e8b0bbe41bc1bee4a3098&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1eea61d03ab615ac5f518e77cd220c1d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_159.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_103.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_59.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_63.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_140.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_10.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657969</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Polygraphs">
      <data key="d0">Polygraphs</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Polygraphs are tools used to assess the physiological responses of individuals, often utilized in the context of evaluating the credibility of evidence in investigations.&lt;SEP&gt;Polygraphs are tools used to detect physiological responses, often utilized in assessing the emotional states of individuals.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-77ba8e0dd4981bd71dedb04a86b45601&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1eea61d03ab615ac5f518e77cd220c1d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_63.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_59.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747464730</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Emotional State Detection Systems">
      <data key="d0">Emotional State Detection Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">These systems aim to assess the emotional states of individuals, often raising ethical and legal concerns related to privacy and consent.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1eea61d03ab615ac5f518e77cd220c1d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_63.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="High-risk AI systems">
      <data key="d0">High-risk AI systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">High-risk AI systems are categorized based on their intended purpose and compliance with regulations to ensure safety and reliability.&lt;SEP&gt;High-risk AI systems refer to artificial intelligence technologies that require significant oversight and regulatory measures to ensure safe and intended usage.&lt;SEP&gt;High-risk AI systems refer to artificial intelligence systems that require stringent guidelines for design, operation, and transparency to ensure safe and appropriate use by deployers.&lt;SEP&gt;High-risk AI systems refer to advanced artificial intelligence systems that carry significant risks and must comply with strict specifications and regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1952e0d35566561db978f8ee1ebdbd3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2f186d6b95e69680f63fabb65ad924a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ded7b0ac022304fae10651966b33d18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0695d12d62d4fd15a528842231db1850</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_73.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_41.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_8.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_13.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747658160</data>
    </node>
    <node id="natural persons">
      <data key="d0">natural persons</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Natural persons are individual human beings, particularly in the context of legal rights and responsibilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Natural persons are individuals assigned to oversee the functioning of AI systems, ensuring their proper use and addressing impacts.&lt;SEP&gt;Natural persons refer to individual human beings, particularly in legal contexts regarding rights and protection.&lt;SEP&gt;Natural persons refer to individual human beings whose personal data can be collected and processed under various regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Natural persons refer to individual human beings who can initiate legal challenges regarding the functioning of certain systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7110d3511298db6faf629e1d559dc5ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a23e03a78af2035b69e69bd4fc65a435&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ded7b0ac022304fae10651966b33d18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0073df6368131f4f385a66430ef1c4f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0373d38f7600f51def3b5e5cb5061d17</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_33.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_5.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_59.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_50.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_73.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747464730</data>
    </node>
    <node id="biometric identification systems">
      <data key="d0">biometric identification systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Biometric identification systems are technologies that identify individuals based on unique physical characteristics, necessitating robust oversight due to their potential risks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ded7b0ac022304fae10651966b33d18c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_73.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="law enforcement">
      <data key="d0">law enforcement</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Activities conducted by law enforcement authorities aimed at preventing and investigating crimes and ensuring public security.&lt;SEP&gt;Law enforcement encompasses the actions taken by authorities to prevent, investigate, and prosecute criminal activities and enforce penalties.&lt;SEP&gt;Law enforcement refers to a system of governmental agencies and officials tasked with maintaining public order, enforcing laws, and ensuring safety within society. This includes the responsibilities of preventing and investigating crimes. Law enforcement may utilize various technologies, including biometric identification systems and artificial intelligence, to aid in their efforts to identify individuals and streamline operations. Overall, law enforcement encompasses a range of processes and resources dedicated to the effective enforcement of laws and the maintenance of public safety.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a94885e0b736d24263914e9a9d565900&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfc036b3a79fdcd1eb36c0af6aafbb4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ded7b0ac022304fae10651966b33d18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27c28ab4482e4bec149657c656192c46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-239d42cf353b4be7fdeade1f3fced85d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0073df6368131f4f385a66430ef1c4f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4249f491e5466803d0f267a67c5cb39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de40ca48bf7dafc1db86f4d8a18d2bba</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_5.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_73.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_34.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_95.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657195</data>
    </node>
    <node id="migration">
      <data key="d0">migration</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Migration involves the movement of individuals from one country or region to another, which can intersect with AI technologies for identification and processing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ded7b0ac022304fae10651966b33d18c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_73.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="border control">
      <data key="d0">border control</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Border control encompasses measures implemented by governments to monitor and regulate the movement of people across national boundaries, often incorporating AI technologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ded7b0ac022304fae10651966b33d18c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_73.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="asylum">
      <data key="d0">asylum</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Asylum is a form of international protection given to individuals fleeing persecution or serious harm in their home countries, potentially involving AI for processing claims.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ded7b0ac022304fae10651966b33d18c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_73.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="human oversight measures">
      <data key="d0">human oversight measures</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Human oversight measures are protocols and guidelines determined by providers of AI systems to ensure that technology operates within safe and intended parameters, concerning human operators.&lt;SEP&gt;Human oversight measures involve procedures and techniques put in place to ensure that high-risk AI outputs are interpreted correctly and addressed properly by the deployers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0d2cf289e7ae9939fc7fe1d189daf51f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ded7b0ac022304fae10651966b33d18c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_13.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_73.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747464135</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union law">
      <data key="d0">Union law</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Union law encompasses regulations and directives established within a political or economic union that govern member states' policies and practices regarding AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Union law refers to the comprehensive legal framework and regulations established by the European Union (EU) that govern the rights and obligations of its member states. This body of law is crucial for ensuring the protection of individual rights and responsibilities across various domains, including but not limited to data protection, migration, asylum, and copyright. It plays a significant role in the regulation of technology, particularly concerning the processing of personal data within artificial intelligence (AI) systems, thereby safeguarding individual rights. Union law comprises regulations and directives that affect diverse aspects of law, ensuring cohesive and consistent legal standards within the EU member states.&lt;SEP&gt;Union law encompasses regulations and legal frameworks relevant to the governance of AI systems across Member States.&lt;SEP&gt;Union law refers to regulations established by the European Union governing various legal matters, including data acquisition and protection.&lt;SEP&gt;Union law refers to the legal framework within the European Union that governs the rights and obligations of its member states and citizens.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4dc89de2edca5d2bfe0d5e9e7c99665b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4c7e75432b8ffa8e0b96687dc4dd380&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8721c261d628c538814f61ffe3cec22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74c582b50b1dcae6565f7384ebbe5e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1ae06c8c76fc5976313d75e4ffabdfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-071372b252509d0e29e64264c0511359&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2612abd3c26dca69a0acec30add3ef15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ded7b0ac022304fae10651966b33d18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0373d38f7600f51def3b5e5cb5061d17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de40ca48bf7dafc1db86f4d8a18d2bba</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_59.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_35.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_91.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_106.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_50.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_53.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_172.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_73.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_95.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_46.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747464578</data>
    </node>
    <node id="training and authority">
      <data key="d0">training and authority</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Training and authority pertain to the skills and level of control that natural persons must possess to effectively oversee high-risk AI systems and ensure their proper function.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ded7b0ac022304fae10651966b33d18c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_73.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Persons">
      <data key="d0">Persons</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Natural persons are individuals who are involved in the operation or use of a system, which might include verification and logging duties.&lt;SEP&gt;Persons in this context refer to individuals who may be subjected to manipulation and influencing by AI systems, especially vulnerable groups.&lt;SEP&gt;Persons refer to individuals whose health and safety is a concern in various contexts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7a0ae2ebdd7c0c6e56069b878ca85c78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ed67e673a6fe0a3c79a41bb9102d44b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9e17b101216d20a500f79a31d9a0d7b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_48.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_29.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_73.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Law Enforcement">
      <data key="d0">Law Enforcement</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Law Enforcement encompasses a variety of agencies and authorities dedicated to maintaining public order and enforcing the law. This includes police forces and border control, along with a wide range of governmental agencies and personnel whose primary responsibility is upholding laws and ensuring public safety. Law enforcement activities involve systems and practices designed to enforce laws, which may include the application of high-risk artificial intelligence (AI) and biometric systems for identification and criminal investigations.

The role of law enforcement is critical in the structure of society, as it employs advanced technologies to enhance capabilities in policing and public safety measures. Law enforcement involves not only traditional methods but also the integration of AI systems focused on maintaining safety and order, which are distinct from military applications. Ultimately, law enforcement encapsulates the various entities and processes engaged in the ongoing effort to uphold laws and facilitate public order, utilizing lawful categorization of biometric data as part of their operational strategies.&lt;SEP&gt;Law enforcement includes government agencies responsible for ensuring compliance with laws and regulations, often involving the use of investigative powers.&lt;SEP&gt;Law Enforcement refers to agencies that may have specific needs when interacting with AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Law enforcement refers to governmental agencies that enforce laws and can utilize AI for biometric identification, raising concerns about privacy and rights.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1be166c61f466e23c3d8c143f6efd3bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d91755cda6acde2b40257e6d4cef1695&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ffa7662f1a996e8ed97ec3caf0ae564&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab148daacc5693b15ec462635a5502a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ed67e673a6fe0a3c79a41bb9102d44b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2035e81a92cf42f945220e637e40591a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee1f186f5aed070bc8e6e813caed9967&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5981afe4b9fb547c64f49e76b1d9c0a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f736e1ff707eaba05079b0f194d8a123&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3070277451614bdc67954ec8735dd80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-166a35f517674f4ceba2754c65f88c5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb43ec5a01dc502046ab6ffbe3a25504&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50be48c46c67191e901c756873069fcb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f116a95954c59b63ce3149e6283ed8e</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_132.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_33.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_5.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_73.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_159.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_131.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_24.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_38.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_32.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_49.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_30.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657468</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Migration">
      <data key="d0">Migration</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Migration involves the movement of individuals from one area to another, often in the context of border control and legal processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Migration refers to the movement of people, often regulated by national or international laws, particularly regarding rights and protections.&lt;SEP&gt;Migration involves the movement of people, which can be monitored or managed through high-risk AI systems in compliance with EU regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Migration refers to the movement of individuals from one country to another, often regulated by laws and policies that ensure their rights and protections.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-166a35f517674f4ceba2754c65f88c5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ed67e673a6fe0a3c79a41bb9102d44b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5644d48de211c02e29152f909c69640b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f736e1ff707eaba05079b0f194d8a123</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_131.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_73.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_14.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_159.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747464919</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Border Control">
      <data key="d0">Border Control</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">Border Control involves measures and systems put in place to regulate and monitor the movement of people across national borders, often employing high-risk AI systems for surveillance.&lt;SEP&gt;Border control involves measures and processes taken by governments to regulate entry and exit at their borders, including security checks and documentation.&lt;SEP&gt;Border control refers to measures and activities aimed at regulating the movement of people across national borders.&lt;SEP&gt;Border control refers to areas governing entry and exit between regions, typically not publicly accessible to general citizens.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2ed67e673a6fe0a3c79a41bb9102d44b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4013941d0b165f5643b927164f2ffd1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f116a95954c59b63ce3149e6283ed8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5644d48de211c02e29152f909c69640b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_73.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_19.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_14.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_49.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747464751</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Asylum">
      <data key="d0">Asylum</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Asylum is a form of international protection granted to individuals in need of safety from persecution in their home countries.&lt;SEP&gt;Asylum is a legal status granted to individuals fleeing persecution or danger in their home countries.&lt;SEP&gt;Asylum is a protection granted to individuals in foreign countries due to fear of persecution based on race, religion, nationality, or membership in a particular social group.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2ed67e673a6fe0a3c79a41bb9102d44b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5644d48de211c02e29152f909c69640b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f736e1ff707eaba05079b0f194d8a123</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_73.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_14.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_159.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747464919</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Natural Persons">
      <data key="d0">Natural Persons</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Natural Persons are defined as individual human beings recognized by law, endowed with specific legal rights and obligations. They play a critical role in the framework of high-risk AI systems, serving as recipients of information or recommendations generated by these technologies. Their decisions can be significantly influenced by the outputs of these systems, which underscores the importance of verifying results to ensure accuracy and reliability. Additionally, Natural Persons may act as human operators who oversee the proper functioning and safety of high-risk AI systems.

These individuals are often subject to data collection during AI system testing and are required to provide informed consent to participate. They are involved in various legal contexts, such as evaluations of criminal conduct and behavioral assessments, where their actions are analyzed under the law. In the domain of AI, the emotions and intentions of Natural Persons can be identified or inferred by these systems, raising substantial concerns regarding privacy and ethical treatment, particularly in work or educational scenarios.

Natural Persons include those who may utilize AI systems for personal, non-professional purposes, often seeking essential public services and benefits, thereby frequently facing risks of discrimination or exclusion. Their access to financial resources can also be affected by AI systems, highlighting the necessity of careful consideration of their rights and protections. Furthermore, they are integral to the interaction and oversight of high-risk AI technologies, positioning them centrally within the legal and ethical discussions surrounding these systems, and distinguishing them from organizations or corporations.

Moreover, Natural Persons are responsible for registering systems within the EU Database and possess legal representation authority. They are also subject to transparency obligations when engaging with AI systems. Their rights and freedoms are protected under various regulations, including those pertaining to migration and asylum processes, as well as social scoring practices, reinforcing their significance in relation to AI-generated content and evaluation.

In summary, Natural Persons are pivotal to the deployment and usage of high-risk AI systems, reflecting both their potential impacts and the critical need for protections concerning their rights and privacy. They are individuals whose biometric data may be collected and processed through real-time and remote biometric identification systems, revealing the thorough intersection between human rights and emerging AI technologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b31c82fb046f107cbfab945a92431bbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d44e4d07784e334a8ded2c1da49b969e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5644d48de211c02e29152f909c69640b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63ef16386f45c7bc364061cc094254fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50cb89ed7d0d818018d373ebefa65267&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aff0d16c0510c298943e3daa75fd581b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b4348ad8873ef2041aca94abc9297ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bccefc944ad0794c75bc69b977c88a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d1a48b7c6d78e001878383cb0acaf58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28efea7f8fe5945cce5b7be57e88efe7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac04e8bc9dd9ff3998ce3c08f3800f57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-602b68fe088482c0037845fc0b520c30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-431ae031d4ead528e84df75526b0f1dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-671e76af4a78aebc96c988f0504bfa99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb43ec5a01dc502046ab6ffbe3a25504&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61cbf514bcfe4869e269c00a2dc9e712&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18e4ea35b819263359794e3a968f44ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2118453abd880b63eddb91fa3806c3f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83317eda1161cf5d13ef9aa07297c98b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b65e9562dd645622f1390ba1863fee19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f62cf38e10f73dd06a997571902c1ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee04f6104a24650416810ede28f3790b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de3f18a6d766d2baa57ae891b9da7741&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d91755cda6acde2b40257e6d4cef1695&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41cdee30f8345bc3690d876d77e6845c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c4d127e5313d415dd94f6b6761da956&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab148daacc5693b15ec462635a5502a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4274f38f6b4aeff6dc2959e9e1a87f1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ed67e673a6fe0a3c79a41bb9102d44b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dead6db59d178a53a4fc03ed67a92e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ef0a2a22402771842f4d35bbf4be08d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-498834b2d84eaf9afe4e5fb0df15933c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8022b105f5e7e2d0ba74bbe75f31f87</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_14.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_44.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_2.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_31.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_16.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_17.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_60.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_96.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_2.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_33.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_12.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_18.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_5.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_93.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_54.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_70.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_32.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_132.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_73.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_50.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_141.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_58.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_14.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_15.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_42.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_6.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_71.json</data>
