    <node id="Regulation (EU) 2024/1689">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) 2024/1689</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 is a legislative act established by the European Parliament and the Council that sets forth harmonized rules pertaining to artificial intelligence (AI) systems. It aims to enhance safety by outlining requirements for safety components and introduces amendments to several previous regulations and directives. This regulation represents a comprehensive framework for governing AI, ensuring that standards are consistent across the EU to promote safe and reliable AI deployment. The focus on safety components is a key aspect of this regulation, reinforcing the commitment to protecting users and stakeholders involved in the development and application of AI technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 is a legislative document by the European Parliament focusing on harmonised rules regarding artificial intelligence and amending previous regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 is a legislative act that establishes rules on artificial intelligence and amends several existing regulations and directives.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 is a new regulation set by the European Parliament and Council outlining harmonized rules on artificial intelligence, affecting multiple previous regulations and directives.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7eb5283f4e280f1ec77650d624699286&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7805654ce0fe0d8d9b6ba008562d2aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6485ea34e7fea16b2f5a59242c8ef2a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3acb107043f5850a72cf1b047a443296&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a84d660603389dd91dcd96134d5bb46e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9e2499910b26136c66e6e7a013d8f0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4219a2a10d85ddd82f98b8d6267cb9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c472ba24566e25512f738275d98a9e3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0b46b9cdd1723562953df9638581250&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a5a3ae528d10c9d38e017d520ab6719</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_107.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_105.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_103.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_109.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_106.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_110.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_104.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_102.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_108.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657990</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Artificial Intelligence Act">
      <data key="d0">Artificial Intelligence Act</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Artificial Intelligence Act comprises a comprehensive legal framework established by the European Union, designed to regulate the use, approval, and governance of artificial intelligence (AI) technologies within its member states. Officially referenced as Regulation (EU) 2024/1689, the Act sets forth standards aimed at ensuring the safe development and implementation of AI systems throughout the EU. It addresses critical safety and regulatory aspects to foster harmonized rules on AI systems, thereby facilitating a structured and responsible approach to technological advancement in the field of artificial intelligence.&lt;SEP&gt;The Artificial Intelligence Act is a legal framework for the regulation of AI technologies in the EU, focusing on safety and ethical standards.&lt;SEP&gt;The Artificial Intelligence Act is a classification of regulations pertaining to artificial intelligence technology, focusing on governance, safety, and ethical use in the EU.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0a68b7c657291244b183bd644e6df395&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7eb5283f4e280f1ec77650d624699286&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6485ea34e7fea16b2f5a59242c8ef2a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a84d660603389dd91dcd96134d5bb46e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4219a2a10d85ddd82f98b8d6267cb9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c472ba24566e25512f738275d98a9e3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0b46b9cdd1723562953df9638581250&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a5a3ae528d10c9d38e017d520ab6719</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_107.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_103.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_106.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_110.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_104.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_102.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_108.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657997</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulations (EC) No 300/2008">
      <data key="d0">Regulations (EC) No 300/2008</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EC) No 300/2008 addresses European security standards and is amended by Regulation (EU) 2024/1689.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EC) No 300/2008 is a European regulation concerning rules related to aviation security.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulations (EC) No 300/2008 focuses on establishing rules for airport security and is one of the regulations amended by the AI Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b9e2499910b26136c66e6e7a013d8f0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6485ea34e7fea16b2f5a59242c8ef2a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c472ba24566e25512f738275d98a9e3b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_109.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_107.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_110.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657623</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EU) No 167/2013">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) No 167/2013</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) No 167/2013 deals with the type-approval of agricultural and forestry vehicles, amended by Regulation (EU) 2024/1689.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) No 167/2013 is a legislative act of the European Union that sets out rules regarding certain directives, particularly concerning artificial intelligence systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) No 167/2013 lays down rules on the approval and market surveillance of agricultural vehicles.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) No 167/2013 pertains to the approval and market surveillance of agricultural and forestry vehicles, impacting the use of AI systems in these sectors.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) No 167/2013 relates to the approval and market surveillance of agricultural and forestry vehicles.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e86452bf9fab5e4da73d81e6eadabb30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a84d660603389dd91dcd96134d5bb46e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9e2499910b26136c66e6e7a013d8f0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4ba1d5ee9be6a9378df917d6a467f31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c472ba24566e25512f738275d98a9e3b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_109.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_49.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_107.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_103.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657295</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EU) No 168/2013">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) No 168/2013</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) No 168/2013 concerns the type-approval of two- or three-wheel motor vehicles, also amended by Regulation (EU) 2024/1689.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) No 168/2013 outlines rules concerning the approval of two or three-wheeled vehicles and quadricycles.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) No 168/2013 is a legislative act of the European Union concerning the regulation of certain standards and requirements, particularly related to safety components in Artificial Intelligence systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) No 168/2013 pertains to the approval and market surveillance of two- or three-wheel vehicles and quadricycles.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) No 168/2013 relates to the approval and market surveillance of two- or three-wheel vehicles and quadricycles, influencing AI safety assessment in these vehicles.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7eb5283f4e280f1ec77650d624699286&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e86452bf9fab5e4da73d81e6eadabb30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9e2499910b26136c66e6e7a013d8f0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4ba1d5ee9be6a9378df917d6a467f31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c472ba24566e25512f738275d98a9e3b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_109.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_49.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_107.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_104.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657295</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EU) 2018/1139">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) 2018/1139</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) 2018/1139 addresses the aviation domain within the European Union, establishing a comprehensive framework for safety standards in civil aviation. This regulation sets out common rules pertinent to the field of civil aviation and serves to establish the European Union Aviation Safety Agency (EASA). Furthermore, it includes provisions related to the implementation of Artificial Intelligence (AI) systems within the aviation sector, outlining specific safety rules and guidelines for their operation. Additionally, Regulation (EU) 2018/1139 has amendments introduced by Regulation (EU) 2024/1689, which further refine and enhance the existing safety standards within this regulatory framework. Overall, this regulation plays a crucial role in ensuring safety and uniformity in civil aviation practices across the European Union.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e86452bf9fab5e4da73d81e6eadabb30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7805654ce0fe0d8d9b6ba008562d2aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9e2499910b26136c66e6e7a013d8f0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4ba1d5ee9be6a9378df917d6a467f31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c472ba24566e25512f738275d98a9e3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2af15b193dbeb2497919d2971657871e</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_109.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_49.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_107.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_108.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657302</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive 2014/90/EU">
      <data key="d0">Directive 2014/90/EU</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive 2014/90/EU is a European Union legislative document that focuses on the regulation of marine equipment, ensuring safety and compliance in maritime transport. It serves to update previous directives related to this area and lays down specific requirements aimed at enhancing safety standards. Additionally, the directive addresses the regulation of high-risk artificial intelligence systems used in maritime contexts, reflecting the evolving technological landscape. It is part of the amendments made by the AI Regulation and establishes standards for vessel traffic monitoring and information systems, thereby integrating these components within the EU's maritime policies. Overall, Directive 2014/90/EU plays a crucial role in ensuring that marine equipment meets necessary safety standards and effectively supports the safe navigation and operation of vessels in European waters.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e86452bf9fab5e4da73d81e6eadabb30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6485ea34e7fea16b2f5a59242c8ef2a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3acb107043f5850a72cf1b047a443296&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4ba1d5ee9be6a9378df917d6a467f31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c472ba24566e25512f738275d98a9e3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0b46b9cdd1723562953df9638581250</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_107.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_105.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_106.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_110.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_49.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657997</data>
    </node>
