    <node id="Regulation (EU) 2022/2065">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) 2022/2065</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) 2022/2065 is a comprehensive legislative framework established by the European Parliament and Council that addresses the obligations related to AI systems within the European Union. It aims to ensure transparency in the generation of content, particularly to mitigate risks associated with misinformation and artificially generated content. The regulation focuses on the responsibilities of AI system providers, outlining their obligations to guarantee transparency and to manage the risks that come with the deployment of AI systems and models.

Additionally, Regulation (EU) 2022/2065 provides clear provisions regarding the liability of intermediary service providers in the EU, establishing a legal framework that governs the application and use of AI systems. This regulatory act is essential for defining how market actors must operate when deploying AI technologies, thereby promoting accountability and safety in the digital services landscape.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2022/2065 outlines the legal framework for AI systems within the EU, focusing on technology neutrality and intermediary services.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b1ab686ea2085e0bf2cc7ea2cb5eb270&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8833999c9ef9aa31a007f2e77ffea02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cac929d0048fe34377179e8ecde4a5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7570653f66cb58454b80be2046705a29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74def3a33d9c60f3c11227adf7704a09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3105f8ed20ed5608a4571fe7b1d8f942&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7e1bc352c7c8d3a7ba58b9b1a4f9f37</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_2.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_136.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_120.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_11.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_119.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_118.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747658082</data>
    </node>
