    </node>
    <node id="very large online platforms">
      <data key="d0">very large online platforms</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Very large online platforms are defined as major digital services that provide a range of online services to end users, subject to regulatory requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Very large online platforms are required under this regulation to identify and mitigate systemic risks related to content dissemination.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9cac929d0048fe34377179e8ecde4a5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7570653f66cb58454b80be2046705a29</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_120.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_118.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657250</data>
    </node>
    <node id="very large online search engines">
      <data key="d0">very large online search engines</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Very large online search engines are included in the regulation's scope to manage risks associated with manipulated content.&lt;SEP&gt;Very large online search engines are significant digital platforms that facilitate information retrieval over the internet, regulated under specific EU laws.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9cac929d0048fe34377179e8ecde4a5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7570653f66cb58454b80be2046705a29</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_120.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_118.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657250</data>
    </node>
    <node id="democratic processes">
      <data key="d0">democratic processes</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Democratic processes refer to the systems and methods that facilitate fair elections and civic participation, which may be influenced by misinformation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7570653f66cb58454b80be2046705a29</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_120.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="civic discourse">
      <data key="d0">civic discourse</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Civic discourse encompasses public discussions and debates that are vital for democracy and community engagement, and can be affected by misleading information.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7570653f66cb58454b80be2046705a29</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_120.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Systemic Risks">
      <data key="d0">Systemic Risks</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Systemic Risks encompass a range of potential threats that could undermine the stability and integrity of online platforms, democratic processes, and the functioning of AI models. These risks primarily arise from the widespread deployment and usage of powerful general-purpose AI models, which can lead to negative impacts across various users, markets, and industries. The potential consequences and vulnerabilities linked to these AI models must be carefully assessed and managed to identify and mitigate risks. Systemic Risks pose potential dangers to security, privacy, and safety, reflecting the overarching threats that AI technologies can introduce to critical sectors and societal functions.

Addressing Systemic Risks is crucial, as it emphasizes the necessity for risk mitigation measures and regulatory frameworks designed to safeguard against possible hazards that could affect a large number of users or lead to significant consequences. Overall, ensuring the effective operation and safety of AI technologies, alongside their integration into society, hinges on recognizing and managing these systemic risks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1fb0ee5d200ca5b71eb6d9f53ad070ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90efb8f063f236753e4794005afa2a0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bee8a141261944c2193bcb00b304b768&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7570653f66cb58454b80be2046705a29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1ef1c9ca92c002cf6ad36264fe1292c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c259012a2ff719418b0deb6cbd52130&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3f46abe104a1bdb0fae1c25094db36d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fcd3af92cad1d85ebf561f059acb114&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4dc0271c68856282748506ff58069b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69b5f24963810305f2a7846d54923bf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-447d51c65bac6d28fd62c36c3e70e08b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_110.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_52.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_120.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_112.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_114.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_116.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_164.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_56.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_111.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_115.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657459</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Very Large Online Platforms">
      <data key="d0">Very Large Online Platforms</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Very Large Online Platforms are internet-based services that host vast amounts of user-generated content and are subject to specific regulatory obligations.&lt;SEP&gt;Very large online platforms are major digital services that facilitate user interactions and content dissemination, subject to specific regulatory obligations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7570653f66cb58454b80be2046705a29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7e1bc352c7c8d3a7ba58b9b1a4f9f37</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_136.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_120.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Very Large Online Search Engines">
      <data key="d0">Very Large Online Search Engines</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Very Large Online Search Engines provide search functionalities over a vast amount of data and face requirements to mitigate harmful content.&lt;SEP&gt;Very large online search engines are services that index the web and return user queries, also subject to regulatory requirements regarding content management.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7570653f66cb58454b80be2046705a29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7e1bc352c7c8d3a7ba58b9b1a4f9f37</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_136.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_120.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Disinformation">
      <data key="d0">Disinformation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Disinformation refers to false information spread intentionally to deceive, particularly relevant in the context of democratic processes and civic discourse.&lt;SEP&gt;Disinformation refers to misinformation that is deliberately spread to mislead or manipulate public opinion, particularly in democratic processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Disinformation refers to false or misleading information that can be spread through models, jeopardizing democratic values and personal privacy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e7e1bc352c7c8d3a7ba58b9b1a4f9f37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-392a0705db576351b9cbccd6dcfdf33f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7570653f66cb58454b80be2046705a29</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_110.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_136.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_120.json</data>
