ocs/recital_148.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_153.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_151.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_176.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_88.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_24.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_137.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_160.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_71.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_112.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_173.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_79.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_70.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747658106</data>
    </node>
    <node id="providers of general-purpose AI models">
      <data key="d0">providers of general-purpose AI models</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Providers of general-purpose AI models are companies or organizations that develop and offer AI systems capable of performing a wide range of tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;Providers of general-purpose AI models are organizations or businesses that develop and offer AI models for various applications, requiring compliance with specific obligations based on their type and size.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0c8a6b92fbe8d93eb878957c5ed60aa0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65c79a1c0cb37c10df906970d376029d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_109.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_117.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657432</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union copyright law">
      <data key="d0">Union copyright law</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Union copyright law encompasses legal regulations governing the use and protection of copyrighted material within the Union.&lt;SEP&gt;Union copyright law refers to the legal framework governing copyright within the European Union, influencing compliance obligations for AI model providers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-32556db3a80f72f1db354810bba21be7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65c79a1c0cb37c10df906970d376029d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_109.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_108.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657426</data>
    </node>
    <node id="start-ups">
      <data key="d0">start-ups</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Start-ups are new businesses that fall under the category of SMEs and are similarly considered in the regulatory context.&lt;SEP&gt;Start-ups are newly established companies often looking to innovate, particularly in technology, and are granted simplified compliance measures to promote their development.&lt;SEP&gt;Start-ups are newly established businesses that are often focused on innovation and developing technology, such as AI systems, and typically seek to rapidly grow their market presence.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3d6ed86abb2e8f0e12897e923d1e9964&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65c79a1c0cb37c10df906970d376029d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7365f713d09e74d49090cb78cb3e19b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_143.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_109.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747464772</data>
    </node>
    <node id="general-purpose AI models">
      <data key="d0">general-purpose AI models</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">General-purpose AI models are advanced artificial intelligence systems engineered to perform a diverse array of tasks across various applications. These models are designed for broad use, demonstrating versatility and flexibility in their deployment. They have the capability to learn and adapt based on the data they are trained on, which enables them to handle a wide range of functions beyond predetermined, specific roles.

In addition to their multifaceted applications, general-purpose AI models must comply with various standards and regulations, including those established by the European Union. This compliance involves adherence to necessary codes for safety, performance, and copyright laws. While many of these models are accessible to the public under free and open-source licenses, allowing for broad dissemination and use, they are also subject to specific regulatory constraints that aim to manage potential systemic risks associated with their deployment.

Overall, general-purpose AI models represent a significant advancement in artificial intelligence technology, necessitating responsible governance to address their capabilities and the associated dangers they may pose.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-010f171cc1a7f217689efe00fd8cb656&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c408a5b914a49af8b42e7e84ad02be6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cc37264ee8f2a814b7b6f98953de48c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6de18717bcb0167956be85a15dd210f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0695d12d62d4fd15a528842231db1850&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c4d08c48923bc3e8bff8968fd67a799&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65c79a1c0cb37c10df906970d376029d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c8a6b92fbe8d93eb878957c5ed60aa0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2739984aae71aa27a0af867bc197b730&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1ae06c8c76fc5976313d75e4ffabdfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f3c3fe390cb5d40b199e1bcc024928f</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_109.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_106.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_40.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_117.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_41.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_25.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_56.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_107.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_68.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747658160</data>
    </node>
    <node id="obligations">
      <data key="d0">obligations</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Obligations refer to the legal responsibilities that entities must adhere to in relation to AI models and their compliance with regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Obligations refer to the requirements that AI model providers must comply with to ensure ethical standards and regulatory compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b567607dbb431b0d294cd02679760039&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65c79a1c0cb37c10df906970d376029d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_109.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_54.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="nonprofessional or scientific research purposes">
      <data key="d0">nonprofessional or scientific research purposes</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Nonprofessional or scientific research purposes denote activities conducted without financial or commercial intent, focusing instead on discovery or academic contributions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-65c79a1c0cb37c10df906970d376029d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_109.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Notified Body">
      <data key="d0">Notified Body</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A Notified Body is a specific type of organization recognized under relevant Union legislation, primarily within the European Union (EU), and is responsible for assessing the conformity of products, particularly high-risk AI systems, before they can be marketed. Designated by national authorities in EU member states, Notified Bodies operate under national law and possess legal personality, which enables them to carry out conformity assessments in accordance with various regulatory standards and requirements.

These organizations play a crucial role in ensuring that products meet necessary regulations prior to their release into the market. Notified Bodies assess compliance, issue certifications, and maintain oversight to guarantee adherence to applicable requirements. They are specifically tasked with evaluating high-risk products and systems, ensuring that they conform to essential regulations for safety and effectiveness.

Due to the nature of their work, Notified Bodies are subject to investigation regarding their competence in executing these assessments. This oversight is vital for maintaining high operational standards within the industry and ensuring consumer safety. Overall, Notified Bodies are integral to the regulatory framework that governs the marketing of AI systems and other high-risk products in the EU.&lt;SEP&gt;Notified bodies are organizations designated to assess whether a high-risk AI system conforms to relevant regulations and issue compliance certificates.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9f55b689ece7aa049c38fdc38018dba8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c237e1a0b42db9afb10cc8a045dbb751&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-785d0dafc3a62a1aee53267d076b7533&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-397d6e2474c4f45e883f265653f2e715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46418d497e0c090818a97380d173293d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34f79a9fca1518856b24fdcb7e59f040&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97182f6b8815d40f51faf3e8eaeb7c7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb8e27222ad9e21f792d1e7ee0a1e255&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-595952fa3e7e47cb312adaaad303b73c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b0c31436f0e7ce27ce5952aa2bf9ae5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8caee37338a6383c30fe06ea2b3e4761&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ad9c740a10a5c1577e578a593bd61fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e978e96ac6d99cf448b53260c07dded</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_36.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_33.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_37.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_44.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_35.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_31.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_18.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_20.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_73.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_79.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747658119</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Conformity Assessment Activities">
      <data key="d0">Conformity Assessment Activities</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Conformity Assessment Activities are tasks conducted by Notified Bodies to evaluate the compliance of high-risk AI systems with necessary regulations and standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Conformity Assessment Activities are the procedures conducted by notified bodies to verify that products, processes, or services meet specified standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Conformity assessment activities refer to the procedures and evaluations conducted by notified bodies to ensure compliance with regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Conformity Assessment Activities refer to the processes followed by Conformity Assessment Bodies to ensure AI systems meet required standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-34f79a9fca1518856b24fdcb7e59f040&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f94df6da4de89cee24b1bd8f504c377&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb8e27222ad9e21f792d1e7ee0a1e255&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2a5e7031602556ef7d57e2811f58992</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_30.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_36.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_45.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_31.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657935</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Conformity Assessment Body">
      <data key="d0">Conformity Assessment Body</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A Conformity Assessment Body is a third-party organization responsible for the testing, certification, and inspection of artificial intelligence (AI) systems. This body evaluates whether high-risk AI systems comply with established legal standards and requirements, ensuring their adherence to relevant legislation. Conformity Assessment Bodies perform third-party assessments to validate that AI systems meet regulatory requirements, conducting evaluations to certify compliance with specific standards and regulations relevant to their respective fields. As part of its responsibilities, a Conformity Assessment Body also plays a role in the evaluation process that informs the Commission's decisions regarding the compliance of AI systems with established standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ff611ee371ea780574e9c16859c31f2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-244204be180c4ed9731f434ed67ee99b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f5fc2b531499a81e154196ee1e86ac6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c237e1a0b42db9afb10cc8a045dbb751&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f94df6da4de89cee24b1bd8f504c377&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb8e27222ad9e21f792d1e7ee0a1e255&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c712c6235ebe0b7ee5102919bbe87d08</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_30.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_28.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_31.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_29.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657930</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Top-Level Management">
      <data key="d0">Top-Level Management</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Top-Level Management refers to the leadership hierarchy within a Conformity Assessment Body that oversees operations and decision-making processes related to conformity assessments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fb8e27222ad9e21f792d1e7ee0a1e255</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_31.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Personnel">
      <data key="d0">Personnel</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Personnel in a Conformity Assessment Body are the staff responsible for conducting conformity assessment tasks and ensuring compliance with regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Personnel refers to the staff, committees, and individuals that work within the notified bodies and are crucial for maintaining standards and assessment integrity.&lt;SEP&gt;Personnel refers to the group of individuals engaged in performing tasks in a given organization, emphasizing the need for competent expertise in various fields.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-58a25c0dd884625561b248cf275f154e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb8e27222ad9e21f792d1e7ee0a1e255&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be2e0f993ca9c4e593e5fcbdd8fc03fe</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_28.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_31.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657604</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Confidentiality Procedures">
      <data key="d0">Confidentiality Procedures</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Confidentiality Procedures are documented processes that safeguard sensitive information obtained during conformity assessment activities, mandated for Conformity Assessment Bodies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fb8e27222ad9e21f792d1e7ee0a1e255</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_31.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Cybersecurity Requirements">
      <data key="d0">Cybersecurity Requirements</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Cybersecurity Requirements encompass the necessary security measures that Conformity Assessment Bodies must implement to protect the integrity of their assessment processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Cybersecurity Requirements refer to the essential standards and measures that must be met by products with digital elements to ensure their security and compliance with EU legislation.&lt;SEP&gt;Cybersecurity requirements are standards that organizations must meet to protect systems and data during the conformity assessment process.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fb8e27222ad9e21f792d1e7ee0a1e255&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97ee5867d3c03f24001b650ad752686d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6370e960da03a6bbdee69f64993cdae6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_31.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_77.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_126.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Liability Insurance">
      <data key="d0">Liability Insurance</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Liability Insurance is protection that Notified Bodies must procure to cover potential legal claims arising from their conformity assessment activities or decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;Liability insurance is a form of coverage that notified bodies must take out for their conformity assessment activities unless covered by the Member State.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-be2e0f993ca9c4e593e5fcbdd8fc03fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb8e27222ad9e21f792d1e7ee0a1e255</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_31.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Notified Bodies">
      <data key="d0">Notified Bodies</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Notified Bodies are independent organizations designated by national authorities and Member States within the European Union to assess the conformity of high-risk AI systems and other regulated products against established regulatory standards. Their primary responsibilities encompass assessing, approving, and monitoring technical documentation and quality management systems in alignment with Union regulations. 

These organizations are tasked with carrying out thorough conformity assessments while ensuring high professional integrity, competence, and adherence to principles of independence, objectivity, and impartiality. The activities conducted by Notified Bodies are essential for maintaining confidentiality and ensuring all assessment procedures are well-documented.

In addition to their assessment duties, Notified Bodies play a crucial role in verifying compliance with specific standards and regulations, thus contributing to the safety and reliability of high-risk AI systems and other products before they can be marketed within the EU. They are responsible for ensuring that products meet the necessary standards established for market entry, highlighting their importance in the regulatory landscape of high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Notified Bodies are organizations designated to conduct conformity assessments and ensure that specific compliance standards are met for products and systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Notified Bodies are independent organizations designated to evaluate and certify the compliance of high-risk AI systems with regulatory standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d1d974005cd87fc21678c732472ee11a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc97d8ad7f3aa0522d885f92ee323822&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28717558f1bb8bd2fd8b9542f8e2a99c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69838403e8b59bb122436a0d25a9fc1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a57bbcc3ccf00f26352f12c36036aedf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a310ed4ba9b96c860daae9a944f07fce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97ee5867d3c03f24001b650ad752686d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be2e0f993ca9c4e593e5fcbdd8fc03fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2a5e7031602556ef7d57e2811f58992&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29241e99bddf5af77eca441d2d8dbc1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c32bc5fa5cdfa35a393a42535dc4fdfb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c72b31b17ef0accd3df4ab25a063163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e978e96ac6d99cf448b53260c07dded</data>
