      <data key="d5">1747658129</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Judgement or Integrity">
      <data key="d0">Judgement or Integrity</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Judgement or integrity refers to the principles and standards that guide the operations and assessments made by notified bodies in conformity assessment activities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-be2e0f993ca9c4e593e5fcbdd8fc03fe</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_31.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Consultancy Services">
      <data key="d0">Consultancy Services</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Consultancy services provided by notified bodies involve offering expertise and guidance in relation to conformity assessments and regulatory compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-be2e0f993ca9c4e593e5fcbdd8fc03fe</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_31.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 78">
      <data key="d0">Article 78</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 78 outlines confidentiality obligations for the national competent authorities in the performance of their tasks under the regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 78 outlines confidentiality obligations that national competent authorities must follow while performing their regulatory tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 78 refers to a specific provision within Union regulations that governs confidentiality obligations concerning information obtained by various competent authorities during compliance and conformity assessment activities. It outlines requirements for maintaining the confidentiality of sensitive information and trade secrets, particularly in accordance with AI regulations. This article establishes guidelines for ensuring that information obtained by Notified Bodies and national public authorities during assessments and investigations remains protected and handled appropriately.

Moreover, Article 78 specifies confidentiality safeguards for information acquired by market surveillance authorities and mandates confidentiality obligations related to sensitive information gathered during investigations by the Commission. The provisions outlined in Article 78 are set to take effect starting from 2 August 2025. Overall, Article 78 emphasizes the critical importance of confidentiality in the context of regulatory compliance and the safeguarding of sensitive data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-22275ba6343521309923fef233affa2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc0fa7bd172fb09094c2d62c87957967&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fce1cda52753ec9e5183762f5b2c81b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97182f6b8815d40f51faf3e8eaeb7c7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d42aaf56c15be020feabced14d2409d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5abff9e94aff7675c473268fd21bf551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e93fbd1f7fc7cbb860b708f989987b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be2e0f993ca9c4e593e5fcbdd8fc03fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa2b7ae4447e7d43e6030d6793c59ef7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e853663a3f2d06a9cfea8582e10f089&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cfbca03bf6afb99c3326dc8b02d083b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c49e78c25e30ed3a2557915010f14f3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a310ed4ba9b96c860daae9a944f07fce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8512760339eb776d946a91a28089b34</data>
