    <node id="conformity assessment body">
      <data key="d0">conformity assessment body</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A conformity assessment body evaluates the compliance of products or services with established standards, ensuring that they meet specific criteria defined by relevant regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9db4c15b43d1b7a1a1138d5a7403b240</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_32.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Official Journal of the European Union">
      <data key="d0">Official Journal of the European Union</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Official Journal of the European Union is a publication that disseminates legal texts and regulations adopted by European Union institutions.&lt;SEP&gt;The Official Journal of the European Union is the official publication of the European Union that serves as the formal record of EU regulations, legislation, and other significant documents. It is the designated platform for publishing EU legislation, decisions, notices, and references related to harmonised standards and relevant legislative documents applicable across EU member states. Additionally, it publishes references for certified high-risk AI systems under the pertinent regulations, including their compliance statements. This publication plays a critical role in ensuring transparency and accessibility of EU legislative processes and standards.&lt;SEP&gt;The Official Journal of the European Union publishes legal documents, including regulations and standards that affect all member states, specifically in compliance with Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012.&lt;SEP&gt;The Official Journal of the European Union is the publication through which the European Union publishes its legal acts, including regulations and standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-762d138929f27b0266d948c0aad50daa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9db4c15b43d1b7a1a1138d5a7403b240&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e93fbd1f7fc7cbb860b708f989987b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0695d12d62d4fd15a528842231db1850&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07b79b1855840c81b5d9079a82c7e9fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d423f15a7cbd742a57795f884434b60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f41337092de45470ab838aff17309ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2739984aae71aa27a0af867bc197b730&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da5fbf959baa6ee8e86278864a9144cc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_122.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_40.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_42.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_41.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_32.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_97.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_113.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747658160</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 31">
      <data key="d0">Article 31</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 31 establishes a comprehensive framework for the requirements and obligations that notified bodies must fulfill to maintain their notification status within the regulatory landscape of the European Union. This article specifies the criteria that these conformity assessment bodies must meet in order to be recognized as competent, ensuring effective oversight of conformity assessment processes as mandated by relevant regulations. It also details the regulatory requirements that govern compliance oversight, which is crucial for maintaining standards in compliance and regulatory practices related to conformity assessment in the EU.

Additionally, Article 31 addresses the specific obligations of notifying authorities and notified bodies regarding market surveillance and compliance assessment of high-risk AI systems. It outlines the conditions that conformity assessment bodies must satisfy before receiving notification, underscoring its significance as a critical component of the legal framework for ensuring rigorous compliance with established standards. Through these provisions, Article 31 plays an essential role in fortifying the integrity of conformity assessment processes across the European market.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ff611ee371ea780574e9c16859c31f2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9db4c15b43d1b7a1a1138d5a7403b240&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f94df6da4de89cee24b1bd8f504c377&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41e5d20a8e9427a4698b84f758676994&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7365f713d09e74d49090cb78cb3e19b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34f79a9fca1518856b24fdcb7e59f040&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b479c56b927c79a74d3a19d8470ff1da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97182f6b8815d40f51faf3e8eaeb7c7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e7b8a0eb1cb8c27dfd822da15429870&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8caee37338a6383c30fe06ea2b3e4761&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21da71f798625922669f14e575cb5dcd</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_30.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_36.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_39.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_37.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_43.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_32.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_29.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657935</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Harmonised Standards">
      <data key="d0">Harmonised Standards</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Harmonised Standards are technical specifications and standards established within the European Union (EU) to ensure that products and services meet necessary regulatory, safety, and compliance requirements. These standards are developed and recognized by designated organizations, serving as a framework that allows providers to demonstrate conformity with EU legislation. They cover a diverse range of sectors, including those related to artificial intelligence (AI), ensuring that products not only meet specific regulatory mandates but also adhere to safety and effectiveness criteria. Harmonised Standards are crucial in fostering cooperation and consistency across the EU, enabling products and services to achieve compliance with various regulations effectively.&lt;SEP&gt;Harmonised standards provide guidelines that ensure compliance with regulatory requirements for high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Harmonised standards are technical standards that comply with European regulations, facilitating the meeting of legal requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-010f171cc1a7f217689efe00fd8cb656&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9db4c15b43d1b7a1a1138d5a7403b240&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69838403e8b59bb122436a0d25a9fc1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cc9a7191827dda78eda5924876e5f7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07b79b1855840c81b5d9079a82c7e9fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00e7606a0fa9d588f18d67d02cfcf654&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac68c725e087cb7c659f2dd75f0a6e34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e24261c10195e33e965bd7e966c33337</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_17.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_122.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_41.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_43.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_32.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_66.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_81.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_121.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747658156</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 31 Requirements">
      <data key="d0">Article 31 Requirements</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 31 Requirements are specific stipulations that entities must meet to demonstrate conformity with EU standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9db4c15b43d1b7a1a1138d5a7403b240</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_32.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Office">
      <data key="d0">AI Office</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The AI Office is a dedicated body established to develop expertise and capabilities in AI and to support the implementation of AI regulations within the Union.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI Office is a designated authority within the Union that plays a vital role in overseeing and regulating artificial intelligence (AI) systems, with a particular emphasis on general-purpose AI models. It is tasked with monitoring compliance with established regulations, assessing risks associated with AI technologies, and ensuring adherence to safety standards while protecting individual rights.

One of the core responsibilities of the AI Office is the development and implementation of codes of practice for general-purpose AI models. These codes are designed to reflect international standards and incorporate diverse perspectives, ensuring alignment with Union-level regulations. The Office regularly reviews these codes to maintain compliance and effectiveness in the face of evolving AI technologies.

Functioning as the secretariat for the Board, the AI Office organizes meetings, prepares agendas, and develops methodologies crucial for evaluating AI systems. This evaluation process is essential for verifying that AI technologies meet safety standards and for identifying potential risks within the information society. In addition, the Office coordinates investigations into high-risk AI systems to ensure compliance with EU regulations and engages in collaborative inquiries as necessary.

Collaboration is a fundamental aspect of the AI Office's approach. It actively engages with a broad range of stakeholders, including representatives from the scientific community, industry experts, and civil society, to assess the capabilities and risks posed by AI technologies. This engagement facilitates the establishment of operational thresholds essential for the safe and compliant functioning of AI systems.

Moreover, the AI Office oversees classification rules and compliance procedures related to AI technologies. It develops and recommends model terms for contracts involving high-risk AI systems and contractual terms for providers and third parties involved in compliance efforts. The Office also supports national competent authorities in establishing regulatory frameworks and facilitating regulatory sandboxes, thereby enhancing the effectiveness of AI regulation across various jurisdictions.

Recognizing the complexity of its functions, the AI Office acknowledges the need for additional powers and resources. This acknowledgment underscores its commitment to promoting safety and competence within the regulatory landscape. Through its multifaceted roles, the AI Office diligently works to ensure the safe and responsible use of AI systems, making it a pivotal entity in the governance and oversight of AI technology, particularly in relation to regulations set to take effect from January 24, 2024.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI Office is an organizational entity responsible for overseeing or managing initiatives related to artificial intelligence.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI Office is tasked with overseeing the implementation and compliance related to AI regulations and may request updates to guidelines.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI Office is an entity that may initiate structured dialogue with providers of AI models for information requests.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a94885e0b736d24263914e9a9d565900&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfc036b3a79fdcd1eb36c0af6aafbb4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c49e78c25e30ed3a2557915010f14f3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e6a5cc59273abbe42c743808026477c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50cb89ed7d0d818018d373ebefa65267&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82b1b08be1175d2e6d49ab5a294ef86a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b567607dbb431b0d294cd02679760039&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3f4621c3d73dca675e991da5d0c9317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c4d08c48923bc3e8bff8968fd67a799&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0efde0679d72a2d51e7acdaf09979bfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40f3761e589fb7702938fd4fbbecfdcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00e7606a0fa9d588f18d67d02cfcf654&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40a9e2a0fc4601f4b3d4f583384b6a06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0373d38f7600f51def3b5e5cb5061d17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c9021d6cb53dceeddd1e648d3e37fbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f892644f7a3eab6b024d8a386777f23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21c742eff7a2b610bb01c8c0ec233b62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c408a5b914a49af8b42e7e84ad02be6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4dc89de2edca5d2bfe0d5e9e7c99665b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fb0ee5d200ca5b71eb6d9f53ad070ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbcc9707fb1611da88a5526a5558a165&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af991f85166d6ddfbbf84e4a73207d3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec7c9ce58b650afe456517c2483e56c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-873c3732f26f3ace86c77cfec67991ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90efb8f063f236753e4794005afa2a0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-184360d53ae652d7f48a919e168f375a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3d60cf6cbe0ae91a9793cb5c98a4a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34333cde7ca701413cb4d0a0ef1129e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85bb41c1db2d2e1883172e505d5f7b71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23ab4f338bfa06297d4c996d7d54dc70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4dc0271c68856282748506ff58069b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a69b68c9998277692ac6c6341fcdcac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83ca16d466deaa751e3b9dc390e91e2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-064e3e5273a81cd8d9a47da9a3f51240&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c553a0db4b39033e7fcfeddeb912aac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32556db3a80f72f1db354810bba21be7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11bdaa862215570a86eed137e3092ea6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6579442a2f027e643cf907006333003a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6de18717bcb0167956be85a15dd210f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b71cdb20a8fa5befb7c30c90163cd416&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-577494efd5ce842563e6974b0da9707b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c259012a2ff719418b0deb6cbd52130&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b235644744fa597c94328afbeaa7e56b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a0c1908573a7d6a832a6b35befbd7ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbe4515f5aa3b0876e436a8a0dffc23e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f3c3fe390cb5d40b199e1bcc024928f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cc37264ee8f2a814b7b6f98953de48c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b90abf0636c26d546e9b6724e3224ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-140dff8b8263721e25ea86a4104c273d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b837dd750c95d041180fa3d735328672&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e76c1f88e5810a7e79cf9527486831e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea1514e01d99729cb280141a24250142&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de5a0c7f560be7dcbe4301aed20bcb98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc8a3a685818e1a12850434d4ddcb5cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e28e08bfb7b1ae3208e2c91ea6f1e4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cfbca03bf6afb99c3326dc8b02d083b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc0fa7bd172fb09094c2d62c87957967&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18d33fd192f06f727ac6bb21becbaa57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-daa2a9a43bd7a2482ad876b406b9e9c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fcd3af92cad1d85ebf561f059acb114&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a0bef2c1dcc3d7b428c7611732f7ffc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c8a6b92fbe8d93eb878957c5ed60aa0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69b5f24963810305f2a7846d54923bf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-075ecb5835777e6044264a23ca0cb20a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4ac0ccf9bd954306cee6efbfd342416</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_91.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_108.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_92.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_74.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_112.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_90.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_111.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_25.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_27.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_57.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_75.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_96.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_62.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_164.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_65.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_56.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_107.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_93.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_53.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_162.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_95.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_101.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_50.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_89.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_116.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_161.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_179.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_163.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_68.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_148.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_117.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_54.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_151.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_88.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_55.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_160.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_66.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_113.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_112.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_64.json</data>
