    </node>
    <node id="Article 77">
      <data key="d0">Article 77</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 77 refers to the regulatory framework involving consultations with national authorities regarding risks associated with AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2440fb0070f3198e96bd1ad753ae3e0a</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_82.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Health and Safety">
      <data key="d0">Health and Safety</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Health and Safety are fundamental rights that may be endangered by high-risk AI systems, influencing their regulatory classification.&lt;SEP&gt;Health and Safety involves measures and regulations aimed at protecting individuals from harm, which are relevant in the deployment of AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Health and Safety refers to the frameworks and considerations that must be adhered to in the usage of AI systems to prevent risks and ensure the well-being of individuals. It encompasses measures, standards, and protocols designed to protect people's safety in various environments, particularly in relation to technological advancements. Health and safety are fundamental public interests protected under the Union’s regulations, underscoring the importance of safeguarding citizens against potential threats. This is especially pertinent in the evaluation of high-risk AI systems, where health and safety considerations are critical to mitigating risks that could adversely affect individuals and communities. The overarching concern is the potential impacts of AI systems on individuals' well-being and fundamental rights, highlighting the necessity for robust regulations to address these issues effectively.&lt;SEP&gt;Health and Safety encompasses the principles and measures taken to safeguard individuals and property from risks associated with AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Health and Safety encompasses regulations and measures that ensure the well-being of individuals, potentially utilizing AI for enhancement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4a65ec6b0fbd17afe47587686523a725&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f5fc2b531499a81e154196ee1e86ac6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe49d95d50900e82a706b2766339562f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2440fb0070f3198e96bd1ad753ae3e0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37d88f95110db00bbf8230a2632a2035&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21acb22d994b8f65ea3709a99eb85032&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b4348ad8873ef2041aca94abc9297ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8f21b63428a38759e45ffcb10bac3d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-878d589bc7b69ae2d9c3a44284a1badc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9e17b101216d20a500f79a31d9a0d7b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_52.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_130.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_7.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_82.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_6.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_48.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_72.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_8.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_20.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657660</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union Market">
      <data key="d0">Union Market</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">The Union Market refers to the economic zone comprising the European Union, where businesses aim to enter and operate under harmonized regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Union market refers to the collective market of EU Member States where AI systems are made available to consumers and businesses.&lt;SEP&gt;The Union market refers to the economic marketplace within the jurisdiction of a group of nations or states, where the impacts of AI may significantly affect commerce and regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Union Market refers to the marketplace within the European Union where high-risk AI systems may be placed into service or used, subject to compliance with regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ca3e6894a9009f1db207c0ec639d8a39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34333cde7ca701413cb4d0a0ef1129e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2440fb0070f3198e96bd1ad753ae3e0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afea58b87ff95e4731bff6457b0b57c5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_46.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_57.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_82.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747658177</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Member States concerned">
      <data key="d0">Member States concerned</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Member States concerned are the countries that are involved in the consultation regarding national measures evaluated by the Commission.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0789803641ff590acdf82b97e7d4afbd</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_82.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="relevant operators">
      <data key="d0">relevant operators</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Relevant operators refer to the entities or organizations that are stakeholders in the national measures being evaluated by the Commission.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0789803641ff590acdf82b97e7d4afbd</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_82.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="High-Level Expert Group on Artificial Intelligence">
      <data key="d0">High-Level Expert Group on Artificial Intelligence</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The High-Level Expert Group on Artificial Intelligence (AI HLEG) is a body that develops guidelines for trustworthy AI, ensuring adherence to ethical standards and principles.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3ded1c99cfd152513a4ef07b96a9c5de</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_7.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European Declaration on Digital Rights and Principles for the Digital Decade">
      <data key="d0">European Declaration on Digital Rights and Principles for the Digital Decade</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The European Declaration on Digital Rights and Principles for the Digital Decade outlines key commitments and values regarding digital technology and rights in the European Union.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3ded1c99cfd152513a4ef07b96a9c5de</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_7.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="common rules for high-risk AI systems">
      <data key="d0">common rules for high-risk AI systems</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The common rules for high-risk AI systems are a framework aimed at protecting public interests related to health, safety, and fundamental rights in AI deployment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3ded1c99cfd152513a4ef07b96a9c5de</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_7.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Ethics Guidelines for Trustworthy AI">
      <data key="d0">Ethics Guidelines for Trustworthy AI</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Ethics Guidelines for Trustworthy AI outline the principles and requirements for AI systems to ensure ethical usage and societal trust.&lt;SEP&gt;The Ethics Guidelines for Trustworthy AI set forth standards and principles for developing and implementing AI technologies responsibly and ethically.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3ded1c99cfd152513a4ef07b96a9c5de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c14e1756e1d8d71ac3ba07125f122da</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_7.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_165.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657067</data>
    </node>
    <node id="general-purpose AI model">
      <data key="d0">general-purpose AI model</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A general-purpose AI model is an advanced artificial intelligence system trained to perform a broad array of tasks through the use of large datasets and self-supervision techniques. These models are designed to be adaptable and versatile, allowing for integration across various sectors and applications. They demonstrate significant applicability and can fulfill multiple functions, making them suitable for a diverse range of uses. However, general-purpose AI models also present potential systemic risks depending on their capabilities and deployment strategies. As such, they are subject to specific compliance regulations and evaluations concerning safety and efficacy, which are crucial for mitigating risks, particularly at the Union level. Overall, general-purpose AI models exemplify the intersection of innovation and responsibility in the rapidly evolving field of artificial intelligence.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9575387945b55e197ecb0c955ef00f65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afea58b87ff95e4731bff6457b0b57c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec7c9ce58b650afe456517c2483e56c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3266d68b5262e6852cabbe36178dec96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b567607dbb431b0d294cd02679760039&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a0c1908573a7d6a832a6b35befbd7ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-075ecb5835777e6044264a23ca0cb20a</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_100.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_92.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_54.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_113.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_163.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657226</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI system">
      <data key="d0">AI system</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An AI system is a complex software entity capable of making predictions, recommendations, or decisions based on data, characterized by its ability to learn and adapt.&lt;SEP&gt;An AI system is a technology framework that utilizes AI models to perform a variety of tasks, potentially including general-purpose functionalities.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI system represents a technological entity whose use is governed by specific obligations and intended uses, requiring proper understanding and documentation for users.&lt;SEP&gt;An AI system refers to software and technologies that enable machines to perform tasks usually requiring human intelligence, such as identifying individuals through biometric data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0f62cf38e10f73dd06a997571902c1ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07e8d113bd66975dbb8053a37cc427fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd27f4cf61449e217b2273c0cf67adfa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9575387945b55e197ecb0c955ef00f65</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_72.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_12.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_17.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_100.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747658025</data>
    </node>
    <node id="general-purpose AI system">
      <data key="d0">general-purpose AI system</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A general-purpose AI system is a type of AI that can perform a variety of functions due to the integration of general-purpose models into its architecture.&lt;SEP&gt;A general-purpose AI system utilizes a general-purpose AI model to serve multiple purposes, allowing for direct use and integration with other systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9575387945b55e197ecb0c955ef00f65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afea58b87ff95e4731bff6457b0b57c5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_100.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657226</data>
    </node>
    <node id="integration">
      <data key="d0">integration</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Integration is the process of combining a general-purpose AI model into an AI system to enhance its functionality.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9575387945b55e197ecb0c955ef00f65</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_100.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="capability">
      <data key="d0">capability</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Capability refers to the ability of the AI system to perform diverse tasks, enabled by the integration of AI models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9575387945b55e197ecb0c955ef00f65</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_100.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="purposes">
      <data key="d0">purposes</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Purposes represent the various functions or uses that a general-purpose AI system can provide.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9575387945b55e197ecb0c955ef00f65</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_100.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Human-Machine Interface Tools">
      <data key="d0">Human-Machine Interface Tools</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Human-machine interface tools are designed to facilitate effective interaction between humans and AI systems, crucial for oversight.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4c4d127e5313d415dd94f6b6761da956</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_14.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Automation Bias">
      <data key="d0">Automation Bias</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Automation Bias refers to the tendency for individuals to over-rely on AI system outputs, potentially leading to misguided decisions in critical areas such as law enforcement or healthcare.&lt;SEP&gt;Automation bias is a phenomenon where users overly rely on the output of automated systems, posing risks in critical decision-making contexts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4c4d127e5313d415dd94f6b6761da956&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2118453abd880b63eddb91fa3806c3f3</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_14.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Monitoring Measures">
      <data key="d0">Monitoring Measures</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Monitoring measures are defined actions or tools that help track and ensure the safe operation of high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4c4d127e5313d415dd94f6b6761da956</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_14.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Deployment Measures">
      <data key="d0">Deployment Measures</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Deployment measures are strategies or techniques implemented before an AI system is used to ensure its safety and compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4c4d127e5313d415dd94f6b6761da956</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_14.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="High-Risk AI System Output">
      <data key="d0">High-Risk AI System Output</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">High-risk AI system output refers to the results or recommendations produced by AI systems, requiring careful interpretation by users.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4c4d127e5313d415dd94f6b6761da956</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_14.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="high-risk AI system">
      <data key="d0">high-risk AI system</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A high-risk AI system is defined as an artificial intelligence application that poses significant risks, particularly concerning its deployment and use. These systems require a thorough assessment of their impact on fundamental rights, health, and safety prior to their deployment. High-risk AI systems necessitate strict compliance with rigorous regulations and oversight to ensure safety and adherence to legal standards. They are categorized based on their potential impact on natural persons, thereby requiring careful monitoring and certification.

Moreover, the deployment of high-risk AI systems mandates the identification of a responsible party to ensure accountability and compliance with necessary checks and authorizations. These systems involve technical capabilities that must be evaluated for their implications on individual rights, and specific compliance obligations must be met according to relevant regulations before they can be placed in the market. Overall, high-risk AI systems demand a meticulous approach to regulation and oversight to mitigate their associated risks effectively.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8af2de29a8b78dd2b512b6eb64d912a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2118453abd880b63eddb91fa3806c3f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cdf6e3e080867f88ec52fa9fabbeafd6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4c7e75432b8ffa8e0b96687dc4dd380&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d2cf289e7ae9939fc7fe1d189daf51f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85fb9638473c0974347ccab540b99b7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77a0a99b47c288a96d7474c796efb766&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19283d37b8085eb0b86aff77d85558de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c17bf6e803eec807c9fc7299d71d51d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36cb0fd5abf1b169a8aa13021f58c7b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cc37264ee8f2a814b7b6f98953de48c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_36.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_22.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_27.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_23.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_46.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_16.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_14.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_13.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_25.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_79.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_11.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657871</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union or National Law">
      <data key="d0">Union or National Law</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Union or National Law refers to the legal frameworks that govern the use of high-risk AI systems, including provisions related to verification and operation.&lt;SEP&gt;Union or national law refers to the legal frameworks established at the European level or within individual member states which govern the exchange and protection of sensitive information.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2118453abd880b63eddb91fa3806c3f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75ec68339f2da8ef06976767a0d5b494</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_78.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_14.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747464120</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Measures for High-Risk AI Systems">
      <data key="d0">Measures for High-Risk AI Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Measures for High-Risk AI Systems consist of protocols and requirements instituted to monitor the operation and effectiveness of AI systems that pose significant risks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2118453abd880b63eddb91fa3806c3f3</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_14.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Identification">
      <data key="d0">Identification</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Identification refers to the process of recognizing and confirming the characteristics or identity of an entity, particularly in contexts requiring accuracy and verification.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5644d48de211c02e29152f909c69640b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_14.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="System">
      <data key="d0">System</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A system is a set of connected elements or components that work together to achieve a particular outcome, often utilized in technology or bureaucratic processes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5644d48de211c02e29152f909c69640b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_14.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Verification">
      <data key="d0">Verification</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Verification is the process of checking and validating the authenticity or accuracy of information or identification, ensuring it meets certain standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5644d48de211c02e29152f909c69640b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_14.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Natural Person Competence">
      <data key="d0">Natural Person Competence</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Natural person competence refers to the qualifications, knowledge, and authority held by individuals to make informed decisions or validations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5644d48de211c02e29152f909c69640b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_14.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="High-Risk AI Systems in Law Enforcement">
      <data key="d0">High-Risk AI Systems in Law Enforcement</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">High-risk AI systems in law enforcement are advanced technologies that pose significant implications for justice and safety and are regulated differently due to their sensitivity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5644d48de211c02e29152f909c69640b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_14.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="high-risk AI systems">
      <data key="d0">high-risk AI systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">High-risk AI systems are artificial intelligence systems that pose significant risks to safety or rights, subject to stringent compliance requirements under EU regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;High-risk AI systems are defined as artificial intelligence technologies that present significant potential risks to health, safety, and fundamental rights. Due to their potential impact on public safety, national security, and ethical considerations, these systems are subject to strict regulatory frameworks. High-risk AI systems must conform to specific regulations that mandate thorough evaluations to ensure their trustworthiness prior to being marketed or used.

The deployment of high-risk AI systems raises substantial concerns regarding safety and compliance, necessitating extensive regulatory oversight to manage these risks effectively. As such, they undergo stringent conformity assessment procedures aimed at ensuring safety and adherence to regulatory standards. These compliance obligations are particularly important when high-risk AI systems are integral to safety components within various products.

Overall, the thorough testing and comprehensive governance of high-risk AI systems are essential for guaranteeing that they operate safely, comply with established regulations, and uphold fundamental rights. Their potential to cause significant harm or risks underscores the need for careful supervision and oversight by market authorities to mitigate safety and compliance risks effectively.&lt;SEP&gt;High-risk AI systems are defined as those AI technologies subject to specific requirements under European regulations to ensure safety and compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-82b1b08be1175d2e6d49ab5a294ef86a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8eae051373e28d701c4893438950556b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0461b38c664574f634a78148bfce0336&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdf8a675497acfbeb420b95621b7cb31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c9021d6cb53dceeddd1e648d3e37fbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-010f171cc1a7f217689efe00fd8cb656&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-675b49fdde07175ec9a1afb693d1d877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5ee58307a02a795e806984f0ff4abe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83f37d4143e19486af167d7acee5bee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78dcdae0f5d22df28405d8ae03e038d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e978e96ac6d99cf448b53260c07dded&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad25bfaa86145b8556e5d82696b8bab4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a57bbcc3ccf00f26352f12c36036aedf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0bd7056742f766183c11176d91fb1e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b837dd750c95d041180fa3d735328672&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75ec68339f2da8ef06976767a0d5b494&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0695d12d62d4fd15a528842231db1850&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2739984aae71aa27a0af867bc197b730&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-759ef1bca08a56dec0192e47771d9820</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_68.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_146.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_60.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_125.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_10.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_40.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_123.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_41.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_160.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_38.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_174.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_20.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_112.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_25.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_78.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747658156</data>
    </node>
    <node id="conformity assessment">
      <data key="d0">conformity assessment</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6c9021d6cb53dceeddd1e648d3e37fbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-759ef1bca08a56dec0192e47771d9820</data>
      <data key="d2">Conformity assessment is the process by which high-risk AI systems are evaluated for compliance with relevant regulations, particularly in safety and performance.&lt;SEP&gt;High-risk AI systems must undergo conformity assessments to establish trustworthiness before being placed on the market.</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_123.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_25.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657107</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union AI testing support structures">
      <data key="d0">Union AI testing support structures</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Union AI testing support structures are proposed entities aimed at supporting the enforcement of AI systems and enhancing capacities of Member States.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9c76dd7edbc6dcf218d6558d18116d52</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_152.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI systems">
      <data key="d0">AI systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">AI systems are advanced computer technologies designed to perform tasks that typically require human intelligence, such as learning, reasoning, monitoring, decision-making, and problem-solving. These intelligent technologies encompass a broad spectrum of frameworks and applications that utilize artificial intelligence, highlighting their capacity to simulate human cognitive abilities.

The operation of AI systems varies widely, ranging from low-risk applications to those with significant implications for health, safety, and fundamental rights. Given the diverse levels of risk associated with these technologies, there is a pressing need for a robust regulatory framework to ensure compliance and safeguard the rights and freedoms of individuals. This regulatory framework is particularly important within the context of European Union compliance standards, where AI systems must adhere to specific regulations regarding data protection, especially since many of these systems process personal data.

AI systems can also influence various aspects of life, including political campaigning and voting behaviors, particularly in the context of elections. Their growing importance extends to accessibility considerations, as they play a role in improving various services and technologies for individuals with different needs.

Overall, AI systems represent a significant technological advancement that holds the potential for both positive impact and considerable ethical considerations. Their integration into various applications emphasizes the necessity for adequate enforcement measures to uphold established standards and regulations, ensuring that the benefits of AI technologies are realized while mitigating potential risks.&lt;SEP&gt;AI systems refer to technologies and models that utilize artificial intelligence for various applications, subject to governance and regulatory scrutiny.&lt;SEP&gt;AI systems are technologies designed to perform tasks that typically require human intelligence, including learning, reasoning, and self-correction.&lt;SEP&gt;AI systems are technologies that use artificial intelligence algorithms to perform tasks that typically require human intelligence.&lt;SEP&gt;AI systems encompass various technologies and applications that utilize artificial intelligence, subject to specific regulations and market evaluations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cfc036b3a79fdcd1eb36c0af6aafbb4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-714d9f621f6eee9273625419653b083c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b567607dbb431b0d294cd02679760039&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-610573a7c194ad780ed97782200a740c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5ee58307a02a795e806984f0ff4abe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3105f8ed20ed5608a4571fe7b1d8f942&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78dcdae0f5d22df28405d8ae03e038d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb040a8b4e6e3fa6f26776f560b6591c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a69b68c9998277692ac6c6341fcdcac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33366c5df404f37775ccbf3ec455b578&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c76dd7edbc6dcf218d6558d18116d52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-649ac2acd7b1a3b0b6a81ce20aa799f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bedecbbbba0ded6846e6dc97756b7de5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85605aee8aaac2bf4ad29d80d902148f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0bd7056742f766183c11176d91fb1e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2315cd7abb88dee440f081de5430a32f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d6ed86abb2e8f0e12897e923d1e9964&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b837dd750c95d041180fa3d735328672&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8721c261d628c538814f61ffe3cec22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e4f07f79ad3c90c82b86c0a02d0fae9</data>
