    <node id="Article 34(4)">
      <data key="d0">Article 34(4)</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 34(4) defines reporting obligations for market surveillance authorities under Regulation (EU) 2019/1020.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-53fb2685a38836a165fa7637bbbadce2</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_74.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union Competition Rules">
      <data key="d0">Union Competition Rules</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Union competition rules are legal frameworks established to maintain fair competition within the EU market.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-53fb2685a38836a165fa7637bbbadce2</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_74.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Legal Acts">
      <data key="d0">Legal Acts</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Legal Acts are formal statutes that outline the regulatory framework governing high-risk AI systems and compliance requirements for manufacturers.&lt;SEP&gt;Legal Acts refer to the formal statutory regulations and guidelines that govern compliance and legal requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Legal acts encompass all formal legislations and regulations that define permissible actions and obligations in the EU.&lt;SEP&gt;Legal acts refer to formal statutes and regulations that provide the framework for the operational standards of AI systems as specified in the aforementioned Regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Legal acts refer to legislation that governs the conformity assessment procedures for high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-41e5d20a8e9427a4698b84f758676994&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55bfb9287798720e37fcd8bae961e88b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b8c1122e1044e4445aa96d7fa6d5b6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c72b31b17ef0accd3df4ab25a063163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53fb2685a38836a165fa7637bbbadce2</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_43.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_177.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_74.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_11.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657902</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Relevant National Authority">
      <data key="d0">Relevant National Authority</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Relevant national authority refers to the specific governmental body responsible for overseeing compliance in financial services.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-53fb2685a38836a165fa7637bbbadce2</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_74.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Financial Institutions">
      <data key="d0">Financial Institutions</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Financial Institutions are organizations such as banks and insurance companies that must adhere to stringent internal governance and risk management requirements under Union financial services law.&lt;SEP&gt;Financial Institutions are organizations that provide a range of financial services, including those offered by banks, insurers, and investment firms. These entities operate within the financial services sector and are required to adhere to various regulations designed to ensure stability and consumer protection. Specifically, Financial Institutions are subject to rigorous compliance with both AI regulations and internal governance standards. They must follow specific requirements set forth by Union financial services law, which not only impacts their operational practices but also influences their documentation processes, particularly in relation to AI systems. Overall, Financial Institutions play a crucial role in managing money, investments, and credit services while conforming to established regulatory frameworks.&lt;SEP&gt;Financial Institutions are organizations that must adhere to specific internal governance rules regarding AI monitoring obligations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c852bda35515c8d5385ef007c8140254&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f12c01099dadb1fc1008ce18c7d800e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18f422febe10e4293aaf989ea5e3d3e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc662d7e26079b23ad5010b8671bfb7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46418d497e0c090818a97380d173293d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99c78ffcf815fa82f05dcb7dc5871e1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8c5a915dca180e1c423cefa27ea6cd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c32bc5fa5cdfa35a393a42535dc4fdfb</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_19.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_17.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_74.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_72.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_158.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_18.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657948</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European Central Bank">
      <data key="d0">European Central Bank</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The European Central Bank (ECB) is an essential institution responsible for managing the euro and overseeing monetary policy within the Eurozone. It plays a crucial role in ensuring financial stability while supervising regulated credit institutions that participate in the Single Supervisory Mechanism. As the central bank for the euro, the ECB is tasked with maintaining the monetary policy of the Eurozone, which encompasses the prudential regulation and supervision of banks to promote a stable financial system in Europe. Overall, the European Central Bank's key functions include the implementation of monetary policies and the oversight of banking institutions to safeguard the integrity and stability of the Eurozone's financial landscape.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bfa4c0995d224333f53196e26a30156b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8da189e7622be67a80b2e12945a657cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f12c01099dadb1fc1008ce18c7d800e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b0054dbaea0e7f90c303fe7d7a824d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af24a9a67de887431d611cc88e6df8c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711f6ce0c9e8f119b1813ffe001673da</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_74.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_158.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive 2013/36/EU">
      <data key="d0">Directive 2013/36/EU</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive 2013/36/EU focuses on the access and prudential supervision of credit institutions and investment firms, establishing rules for financial regulation in the EU.&lt;SEP&gt;Directive 2013/36/EU is a regulation by the European Parliament regarding access to the activity of credit institutions and the prudential supervision of these institutions.&lt;SEP&gt;Directive 2013/36/EU is a regulation that establishes capital requirements for banks in the European Union, promoting financial stability and consumer protection.&lt;SEP&gt;Directive 2013/36/EU outlines the authorization and supervisory requirements for credit institutions in the EU.&lt;SEP&gt;Directive 2013/36/EU outlines the regulatory framework for credit institutions and investment firms within the EU, focusing on the prudential supervision and risk management.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-18f422febe10e4293aaf989ea5e3d3e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8da189e7622be67a80b2e12945a657cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b0054dbaea0e7f90c303fe7d7a824d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af24a9a67de887431d611cc88e6df8c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711f6ce0c9e8f119b1813ffe001673da</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_74.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_158.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Single Supervisory Mechanism">
      <data key="d0">Single Supervisory Mechanism</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Single Supervisory Mechanism is a system for banking supervision in the Eurozone, allowing the European Central Bank to oversee banks to ensure compliance with EU laws.&lt;SEP&gt;The Single Supervisory Mechanism is a system whereby the European Central Bank oversees significant banks to ensure safety and soundness across the Eurozone.&lt;SEP&gt;The Single Supervisory Mechanism is the system set up to oversee banking institutions in the Eurozone to ensure their safety and soundness.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-711f6ce0c9e8f119b1813ffe001673da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8da189e7622be67a80b2e12945a657cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af24a9a67de887431d611cc88e6df8c6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_74.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_158.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EU) No 1024/2013">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) No 1024/2013</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) No 1024/2013 covers the establishment of the European Central Bank's responsibilities in the banking supervision under the Single Supervisory Mechanism.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) No 1024/2013 pertains to the establishment of the European Central Bank's supervisory role over credit institutions in the Eurozone.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8da189e7622be67a80b2e12945a657cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af24a9a67de887431d611cc88e6df8c6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_74.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_158.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive (EU) 2016/679">
      <data key="d0">Directive (EU) 2016/679</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive (EU) 2016/679 is the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) that aims to protect personal data and privacy in the European Union.&lt;SEP&gt;Directive (EU) 2016/679, also known as the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), sets guidelines for the collection and processing of personal information.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-68df7ac042ba1913236779113868f934&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8da189e7622be67a80b2e12945a657cb</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_10.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_74.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive (EU) 2016/680">
      <data key="d0">Directive (EU) 2016/680</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive (EU) 2016/680 is a comprehensive legislative framework established by the European Union that focuses on the protection of personal data processed for law enforcement purposes. It is aimed at ensuring the safeguarding of individuals' rights while their personal data is handled by competent authorities involved in preventing, investigating, detecting, or prosecuting criminal offenses. 

The directive emphasizes the necessity for responsible management of personal data within law enforcement activities and establishes regulations designed to protect private life and communications. It specifically addresses the processing of personal data and sets forth rules regarding the handling of biometric data, aiming to enhance the rights of natural persons and prevent potential misuse of their personal data by law enforcement agencies. 

Overall, Directive (EU) 2016/680 serves as a crucial legal framework for regulating the processing of personal data in the context of law enforcement and criminal investigations, ensuring that the individual's privacy is adequately protected throughout these processes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-737358b61293029e1a6d7326160654fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8da189e7622be67a80b2e12945a657cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0efde0679d72a2d51e7acdaf09979bfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bccefc944ad0794c75bc69b977c88a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc038db2f25d511bf84cccc9550e10c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4988a00689afb1245e0f0ce4ceef5921&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0373d38f7600f51def3b5e5cb5061d17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c1d05b847c03fe702172f787883fc33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68df7ac042ba1913236779113868f934&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-602b68fe088482c0037845fc0b520c30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bece07e296fce9647a40a0dde904fe4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3cb5eb81289d4fb565bd824bdc63506&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77a0a99b47c288a96d7474c796efb766&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85605aee8aaac2bf4ad29d80d902148f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de3f18a6d766d2baa57ae891b9da7741&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc8a3a685818e1a12850434d4ddcb5cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15eee417af0ebe299ed66be76a0b845a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77093970e26d1be04734ed16ea88f777&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a46250ea72037444e96653239f2893b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee1f186f5aed070bc8e6e813caed9967&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4882abf1dd869d3dff00b8d88ee946a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-498834b2d84eaf9afe4e5fb0df15933c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de40ca48bf7dafc1db86f4d8a18d2bba</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_27.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_10.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_74.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_53.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_94.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_14.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_50.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_93.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_70.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_38.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_39.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_140.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_10.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_95.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657969</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Annex III to this Regulation">
      <data key="d0">Annex III to this Regulation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Annex III to this Regulation lists the high-risk AI systems and the requirements for their oversight and governance by relevant authorities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8da189e7622be67a80b2e12945a657cb</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_74.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Court of Justice of the European Union">
      <data key="d0">Court of Justice of the European Union</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Court of Justice is the judicial authority in the EU, acting independently in legal matters without interference.&lt;SEP&gt;The Court of Justice of the European Union is the judicial authority that reviews decisions related to the imposition of fines by the Commission.&lt;SEP&gt;The Court of Justice of the European Union is the judicial institution that reviews decisions made by the Commission regarding the imposition of fines.&lt;SEP&gt;The Court of Justice of the European Union oversees the review of decisions made by the Commission and has unlimited jurisdiction regarding penalties under specific articles of the TFEU.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bc8a3a685818e1a12850434d4ddcb5cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae3ab8a3b5c5d0c61e8b99fa718913b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de6a0d59bb86cca6093fbb52cf156b4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b16c22014fb75795531a9a187b8fc81</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_169.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_101.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_74.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Annex I">
      <data key="d0">Annex I</data>
      <data key="d1">document</data>
      <data key="d2">Annex I is a comprehensive document that contains a list of Union harmonisation legislation pertaining to the regulation of artificial intelligence (AI). It ensures consistency and compliance across various sectors and outlines specific legislative frameworks related to high-risk AI systems. The annex serves as a regulatory reference for market surveillance and compliance activities, detailing the necessary conformity assessments that must be conducted for high-risk AI systems.

Furthermore, Annex I specifies the requirements for post-market monitoring systems associated with certain products, particularly those categorized as high-risk AI systems. It also establishes the conditions under which AI system certificates remain valid, which is for a maximum of five years, providing clear compliance requirements for stakeholders involved in the development and deployment of such systems. Overall, Annex I plays a crucial role in promoting regulatory clarity and ensuring that high-risk AI systems meet established safety and compliance standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex I lists legal acts that enable product manufacturers to opt out of third-party conformity assessments under certain conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex I lists the Union harmonisation legislation governing high-risk AI systems and the applicable conformity assessment procedures.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bc8a3a685818e1a12850434d4ddcb5cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f56b40e98f8949a37c3ab283b01f7050&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41e5d20a8e9427a4698b84f758676994&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-397d6e2474c4f45e883f265653f2e715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99c78ffcf815fa82f05dcb7dc5871e1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b4348ad8873ef2041aca94abc9297ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b235644744fa597c94328afbeaa7e56b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c72b31b17ef0accd3df4ab25a063163</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_74.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_72.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_44.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_6.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_43.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_96.json</data>
