      <data key="d5">1747657792</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Validation Data Sets">
      <data key="d0">Validation Data Sets</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Validation Data Sets are used to evaluate the performance of AI systems against regulatory expectations and standards in high-risk AI development.&lt;SEP&gt;Validation data sets are utilized to assess the performance of AI models and ensure they meet quality and applicability standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2fde742696dfc1372a034cc9cadcb58d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbe4515f5aa3b0876e436a8a0dffc23e</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_10.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_74.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Documentation">
      <data key="d0">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Documentation encompasses a comprehensive range of written materials that are essential for understanding the use, limitations, and intended applications of AI systems. It is designed to ensure accessibility for users, providing them with the necessary information to effectively engage with the technology. This body of work includes all relevant files, instruction manuals, and records related to the development and functioning of high-risk AI systems.

Furthermore, documentation refers to writings prepared to outline the assessment of AI systems, ensuring compliance with applicable regulations prior to their market entry. It also encompasses written policies, procedures, and instructions that delineate how providers manage regulatory compliance for high-risk AI systems. Additionally, any records or materials created or maintained under Union law that are essential for enforcing compliance and oversight of these AI systems fall under the domain of documentation. Ultimately, it includes all records and evidence supporting adherence to regulatory standards and operational procedures for high-risk AI systems, thereby playing a critical role in promoting accountability and transparency within the field.&lt;SEP&gt;Documentation refers to the collection of information that the provider must submit for compliance with regulations governing AI models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7c553a0db4b39033e7fcfeddeb912aac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e853663a3f2d06a9cfea8582e10f089&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4672fd3df7077626af67d20e46d3fcb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07e8d113bd66975dbb8053a37cc427fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbe4515f5aa3b0876e436a8a0dffc23e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68d6983d829937a84d37118dacc3e39c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac68c725e087cb7c659f2dd75f0a6e34</data>
