    <node id="Third Country">
      <data key="d0">Third Country</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">A third country is any nation that is not part of the Union, particularly as it relates to the deployment and regulation of AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;A third country refers to any nation that is not part of the Union but is involved in trade agreements with the Union as per the regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Third country refers to any country that is not part of a specific legal or political agreement involving the Union.&lt;SEP&gt;Third Country refers to nations not part of the Union but may interact with its regulations concerning AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b4337a268de724c492ca11805622faf1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13991bdab077b3114e8913f89a1371e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21da71f798625922669f14e575cb5dcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e78bce1eaa5df9c186492b5e1482218</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_22.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_39.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_2.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_127.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747464649</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Conformity Assessment Bodies">
      <data key="d0">Conformity Assessment Bodies</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Conformity Assessment Bodies are organizations responsible for assessing the conformity of products and services to relevant standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Conformity Assessment Bodies are organizations that assess whether a product meets required standards and regulations in compliance with international trade laws.&lt;SEP&gt;Conformity assessment bodies are organizations authorized to ensure compliance with specific regulations and standards under agreements with the Union.&lt;SEP&gt;Conformity assessment bodies are organizations that submit applications for notification to the notifying authority in their Member State, claiming competence in conformity assessment activities for AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-21da71f798625922669f14e575cb5dcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4337a268de724c492ca11805622faf1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff611ee371ea780574e9c16859c31f2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c712c6235ebe0b7ee5102919bbe87d08</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_28.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_127.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_29.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_39.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657604</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Mutual Recognition Agreements">
      <data key="d0">Mutual Recognition Agreements</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Mutual Recognition Agreements are treaties or agreements that allow for the recognition of regulatory measures and compliance across different countries.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b4337a268de724c492ca11805622faf1</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_127.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 8">
      <data key="d0">Article 8</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 8 refers to a specific section of Directive 2014/90/EU that introduces a paragraph regarding artificial intelligence systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3acb107043f5850a72cf1b047a443296</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_105.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Chapter III">
      <data key="d0">Chapter III</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Chapter III of Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 outlines safety requirements for artificial intelligence systems applicable to Article 8.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3acb107043f5850a72cf1b047a443296</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_105.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Section 2">
      <data key="d0">Section 2</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Section 2 of Chapter III is a critical component of the regulatory framework governing artificial intelligence systems, particularly those classified as high-risk. This section outlines detailed requirements and standards that these AI systems must fulfill to ensure compliance and safety within the market. Specifically, Section 2 delineates the safety components that high-risk AI systems are required to incorporate, establishing a clear set of criteria for authorization and compliance. Providers of such systems must adhere to these regulatory requirements as part of the broader EU regulatory framework designed to enhance the safety and reliability of AI technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;Section 2 refers to specific requirements set in the regulation that AI systems must meet to ensure safety and compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f13d730755b7535c59eb130d6f7ac62e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4c7e75432b8ffa8e0b96687dc4dd380&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3acb107043f5850a72cf1b047a443296&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa2b7ae4447e7d43e6030d6793c59ef7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a21678b36bef336bf18e091bdfdb68f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2739984aae71aa27a0af867bc197b730&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdd0ab3aadbdd5226fa3661ea9057181</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_47.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_105.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_40.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_46.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_24.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_21.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747658017</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EU Legislative Document 2024/1689">
      <data key="d0">EU Legislative Document 2024/1689</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The EU Legislative Document 2024/1689 is a legal document related to regulations issued by the European Union in 2024.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ec3aceb64afa671f57d404e61126379b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_105.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data from Europe">
      <data key="d0">Data from Europe</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Data from Europe refers to datasets and information released by the European Union pertaining to laws, regulations, and directives.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ec3aceb64afa671f57d404e61126379b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_105.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Value Chain">
      <data key="d0">AI Value Chain</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The AI Value Chain refers to the various stages and parties involved in creating AI systems, tools, and services along with the integration and development processes.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI value chain refers to the various stages and roles that contribute to the development, implementation, and management of AI technologies across industries.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI value chain encompasses various stages and responsibilities in the development and deployment of AI technologies, particularly regarding compliance and implementation practices.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI value chain refers to the entire process involved in the development, deployment, and management of AI systems, emphasizing the importance of cooperation among stakeholders.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI value chain encompasses all the stages involved in the development, deployment, and monitoring of AI systems, including cooperation among various stakeholders.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-778cb9e68fcb25e3f810e3cea927f7b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7963b30391bfa3d5e28ecd9a95b61010&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bee8a141261944c2193bcb00b304b768&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11bdaa862215570a86eed137e3092ea6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a67563c32c3414ab14ce22666bed23dc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_88.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_114.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_101.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_89.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_85.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Providers">
      <data key="d0">Providers</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Providers are entities or individuals responsible for the development, management, and supply of artificial intelligence (AI) systems and components, particularly those classified as high-risk. They play a vital role in ensuring that AI systems meet the mandatory requirements set forth by legislation before being offered in the market. This includes a commitment to compliance with regulatory standards, which is crucial for both high-risk and general-purpose AI systems.

Providers must demonstrate conformity to applicable regulations, which may be requested by competent authorities, and they are accountable for the accurate and appropriate use of AI systems. This accountability extends to the creation and distribution of necessary documentation that is accessible and understandable to users. Providers may also operate in specific sectors, such as financial services, where they must adhere to particular governance and quality management standards.

Furthermore, providers are responsible for establishing and documenting post-market monitoring systems for high-risk AI technologies, which involves ensuring compliance and conducting performance evaluations. Overall, providers are integral to the development and integration of AI technologies, ensuring that they operate within the framework of regulatory compliance while addressing market needs.&lt;SEP&gt;Providers are organizations or entities that develop and supply general-purpose AI models for various uses and applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Providers are entities or individuals that develop high-risk AI systems and are subject to conformity assessments by notified bodies.&lt;SEP&gt;Providers of high-risk AI systems are responsible for ensuring compliance with regulations and taking corrective actions as necessary.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d1d974005cd87fc21678c732472ee11a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90efb8f063f236753e4794005afa2a0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a65ec6b0fbd17afe47587686523a725&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-873c3732f26f3ace86c77cfec67991ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73fd7e801c2d8d41361f6b16b45c6ed0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32556db3a80f72f1db354810bba21be7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f56b40e98f8949a37c3ab283b01f7050&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc662d7e26079b23ad5010b8671bfb7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a67563c32c3414ab14ce22666bed23dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa2b7ae4447e7d43e6030d6793c59ef7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7963b30391bfa3d5e28ecd9a95b61010&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bf82c08e44c3a6e12c9472e052df840&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac68c725e087cb7c659f2dd75f0a6e34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07e8d113bd66975dbb8053a37cc427fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e978e96ac6d99cf448b53260c07dded</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_108.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_17.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_72.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_64.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_24.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_54.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_85.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_21.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_88.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_72.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_20.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_34.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_111.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747658119</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Tools and Services">
      <data key="d0">Tools and Services</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Tools and services in the context of AI are software applications and support systems that help in the development, training, and deployment of AI models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7963b30391bfa3d5e28ecd9a95b61010</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_88.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Model Training">
      <data key="d0">Model Training</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Model Training is the process of teaching an AI model using data sets to enable it to make predictions or decisions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7963b30391bfa3d5e28ecd9a95b61010</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_88.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Model Testing">
      <data key="d0">Model Testing</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Model Testing evaluates the performance and accuracy of an AI model by running it against test data and measuring outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7963b30391bfa3d5e28ecd9a95b61010</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_88.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Integration into Software">
      <data key="d0">Integration into Software</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Integration into Software refers to the process of incorporating AI components into existing software systems for enhanced functionality.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7963b30391bfa3d5e28ecd9a95b61010</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_88.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Written Agreement">
      <data key="d0">Written Agreement</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A written agreement defines the roles and responsibilities of different parties involved in the testing of AI systems, ensuring accountability and clarity.&lt;SEP&gt;Written Agreement is a formal document outlining the terms and conditions between parties involved in the AI value chain, ensuring clarity and commitment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f8022b105f5e7e2d0ba74bbe75f31f87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7963b30391bfa3d5e28ecd9a95b61010</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_88.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_141.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Intellectual Property Rights">
      <data key="d0">Intellectual Property Rights</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Intellectual Property Rights protect the creations of the mind, including inventions, literary and artistic works, and symbols.&lt;SEP&gt;Intellectual Property Rights refer to legal protections for creations of the mind, crucial for safeguarding technological innovations and inventions.&lt;SEP&gt;Intellectual property rights encompass the legal rights that protect the creations of the mind, including inventions, literary and artistic works, designs, and symbols, names, and images used in commerce.&lt;SEP&gt;Intellectual property rights protect creations of the mind, such as inventions and trade secrets, which must be considered when publishing lists of AI models.&lt;SEP&gt;Intellectual property rights are legal rights that provide creators protection over their inventions, designs, and artistic works, significant in the context of confidentiality.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-13b35a74627bd926656242d6545e09a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e284955c1d36330bd14d117bb417611&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe4d7c8b1c65cb7b9f5021681b13c271&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7963b30391bfa3d5e28ecd9a95b61010&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1ef1c9ca92c002cf6ad36264fe1292c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_48.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_167.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_52.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_88.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657436</data>
    </node>
    <node id="The Commission">
      <data key="d0">The Commission</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Commission is a governing and authoritative body within the European Union responsible for the regulation of artificial intelligence (AI) systems, with a particular emphasis on high-risk applications affecting health, safety, and fundamental rights. It designates general-purpose AI models as presenting systemic risks and is empowered to adopt delegated acts, thereby ensuring proper coordination and collaboration among notified bodies that oversee high-risk AI.

In its regulatory role, the Commission is tasked with assigning identification numbers to these notified bodies and maintaining a public list of them. It plays a critical function in monitoring and regulating emerging technologies, which includes the publication of annual reports concerning biometric identification systems used for law enforcement purposes. The Commission also develops guidance for compliance related to obligations for reporting serious incidents involving AI systems.

Moreover, the Commission is heavily involved in implementing and overseeing regulations concerning content practices, while also fostering initiatives that encourage AI development and data exchange. As the executive branch of the European Union, it is integral to proposing legislation and executing decisions that form the regulatory framework for AI systems. The Commission continuously assesses and amends regulations to uphold transparency and compliance within the sector, ensuring that the guidelines address the needs of various stakeholders, including small and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs) and public authorities. Overall, the Commission serves as a crucial regulatory entity, overseeing compliance with legal obligations and shaping the landscape for AI technologies in the EU.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0dc307b8b7cb1f0e39aa9b4b1839c408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a811acaf13b6420a717f6aa21a6ed331&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cb1edc11e8b8d0e952b15617a80f379&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3034aa8ff1b6d41ac6e0b8ff655b76ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe49d95d50900e82a706b2766339562f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de5a0c7f560be7dcbe4301aed20bcb98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40e75ee11aa912f1497b2a91ae655e7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c553a0db4b39033e7fcfeddeb912aac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb0291da832d9defa94aaf2262ad3761&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-785d0dafc3a62a1aee53267d076b7533&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c4d62babb1c5a144faeae6ac2f13628&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3177468233ec37ad2a71dc38caa17377&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1ef1c9ca92c002cf6ad36264fe1292c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-911571ee28a1070a8fcc503dd5d91e14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0461b38c664574f634a78148bfce0336&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6adb64ff4e7b459fa1df815eac98b096&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b235644744fa597c94328afbeaa7e56b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_91.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_57.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_52.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_53.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_40.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_5.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_35.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_50.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_6.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_165.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_43.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_96.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_38.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_7.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_112.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_73.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747658139</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 5">
      <data key="d0">Article 5</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 5 is a crucial component of the regulatory framework concerning artificial intelligence (AI), establishing clear prohibitions related to non-compliant AI practices that must be followed within the market. This article specifically addresses the prohibition of unacceptable AI practices, ensuring that AI systems are developed and operated in a manner that is both safe and ethical.

The provisions outlined in Article 5 detail specific practices that are not permitted under the established regulations, highlighting the need for regular assessments by the Commission to evaluate compliance. Moreover, Article 5 includes stipulations regarding the testing and use of high-risk AI systems, reinforcing the necessity of adhering to safety and ethical standards.

It emphasizes the importance of compliance and accountability in the development and operation of AI systems, making it clear that violations of these regulations are subject to penalties. Furthermore, it mandates that Member States align their practices with these regulations to uphold the integrity of the AI regulatory landscape. Overall, Article 5 serves as a foundational element within this framework, ensuring that ethical standards are maintained in the use of artificial intelligence.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ff61ec794793cf787d4a0473487a06f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de5a0c7f560be7dcbe4301aed20bcb98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a69b68c9998277692ac6c6341fcdcac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-345a8ba89ed0ea3325462384d5e16aaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7365f713d09e74d49090cb78cb3e19b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b71cdb20a8fa5befb7c30c90163cd416&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b235644744fa597c94328afbeaa7e56b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee6d94a5f64203f09d02387acbdb39c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-111c71f234a0f2d1b26490907acae6eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ad9c740a10a5c1577e578a593bd61fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8e23760d52ebfb589b4de63afe8ab83</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_100.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_60.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_111.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_96.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_81.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_112.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_79.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657789</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 50">
      <data key="d0">Article 50</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 50 outlines essential transparency obligations that must be fulfilled by providers and deployers of artificial intelligence (AI) systems. It establishes clear requirements for these transparency measures, ensuring that the implementation of AI systems adheres to accountability and ethical standards. Specifically, Article 50 applies to AI systems that require additional transparency measures and is subject to amendments based on evaluations of compliance and effectiveness. Furthermore, it addresses specific compliance requirements and enforcement measures under the broader framework of EU regulations. Organizations implementing AI systems are mandated to comply with these outlined transparency obligations to promote responsible and ethical use of AI technology.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 50 refers to a specific provision of the Regulation concerning high-risk AI systems and their use in decision-making processes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2c1d05b847c03fe702172f787883fc33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de5a0c7f560be7dcbe4301aed20bcb98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-345a8ba89ed0ea3325462384d5e16aaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7365f713d09e74d49090cb78cb3e19b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b71cdb20a8fa5befb7c30c90163cd416&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b235644744fa597c94328afbeaa7e56b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a69b68c9998277692ac6c6341fcdcac</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_96.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_112.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_79.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657985</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 99">
      <data key="d0">Article 99</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 99 refers to a provision within EU regulations that outlines the penalties for non-compliance by providers regarding AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 99 refers to the penalties related to infringements of the regulation, particularly administrative fines applied by Member States.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 99 stipulates the penalties for providers that fail to comply with the regulatory requirements, emphasizing accountability.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a64bfb94635a0df2f808b2f8a494bd3e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-610573a7c194ad780ed97782200a740c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de5a0c7f560be7dcbe4301aed20bcb98</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_112.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_80.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747658087</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union agency">
      <data key="d0">Union agency</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A proposed body that may be created to address identified shortcomings in the enforcement of AI regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-de5a0c7f560be7dcbe4301aed20bcb98</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_112.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="energy-efficient development of AI models">
      <data key="d0">energy-efficient development of AI models</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Energy-efficient development of AI models refers to practices aimed at optimizing AI system performance while minimizing their environmental impact.&lt;SEP&gt;This refers to the regulatory focus on developing AI models in an energy-efficient manner as part of standardisation deliverables.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-83f37d4143e19486af167d7acee5bee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b837dd750c95d041180fa3d735328672</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_174.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_112.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747464320</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 99(1)">
      <data key="d0">Article 99(1)</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 99(1) outlines specific administrative fines applied by Member States for regulatory infringements concerning AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b837dd750c95d041180fa3d735328672</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_112.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="evaluation">
      <data key="d0">evaluation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Evaluation refers to the process undertaken by the Commission to assess the functions and effectiveness of the AI Office and other regulatory measures.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b837dd750c95d041180fa3d735328672</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_112.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="standardisation deliverables">
