      <data key="d5">1747658106</data>
    </node>
    <node id="notifying authority">
      <data key="d0">notifying authority</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Notifying authorities are responsible for ensuring that bodies they notify participate in sector groups and assessments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0461b38c664574f634a78148bfce0336</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_38.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Regulatory Sandboxes">
      <data key="d0">AI Regulatory Sandboxes</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">AI Regulatory Sandboxes are controlled environments designed to facilitate the testing and experimentation of artificial intelligence (AI) systems and applications. They enable small and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs), start-ups, and other innovators to develop and validate their AI technologies while ensuring compliance with pertinent regulations and data protection laws. These frameworks promote innovation and cooperation among relevant stakeholders by allowing for regulatory supervision during the testing phases. By providing a structured setting for AI development, AI Regulatory Sandboxes not only help innovators navigate complex regulatory landscapes but also support the responsible advancement of AI technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;AI Regulatory Sandboxes are controlled environments established to foster innovation and facilitate the development, testing, and validation of innovative AI systems before they are placed on the market.&lt;SEP&gt;AI Regulatory Sandboxes are frameworks established to facilitate the development and testing of AI systems while ensuring compliance with regulations and fostering innovation.&lt;SEP&gt;AI regulatory sandboxes are controlled environments created to test innovative AI technologies under regulatory supervision to foster compliance and innovation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e76c1f88e5810a7e79cf9527486831e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc97d8ad7f3aa0522d885f92ee323822&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7859a0c655f74761757b416c3b50bf36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aca56f82b70892874784bcec5c2bb2c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-800752b66b6fe0cd70bb0290efc2fbbe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34333cde7ca701413cb4d0a0ef1129e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95424b9dff57302628c496570b4baff4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85bb41c1db2d2e1883172e505d5f7b71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d08b537f9a5bb2b4f4bbdf442ba39bdd</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_139.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_57.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_58.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_59.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_62.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657689</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Start-ups">
      <data key="d0">Start-ups</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Start-ups are a subset of SMEs that are new or emerging businesses, often characterized by innovation and growth potential.&lt;SEP&gt;Start-ups are newly established businesses, often in the technology sector, focused on innovation and growth.&lt;SEP&gt;Start-ups are newly established companies that often focus on innovative ideas and technologies, which can greatly benefit from AI regulatory sandboxes to ensure compliance and accelerate market access.&lt;SEP&gt;Start-ups are new businesses represented in the advisory forum, contributing innovative perspectives to the implementation of the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f76666cf495bb0f0810313fe42e2c882&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95424b9dff57302628c496570b4baff4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e76c1f88e5810a7e79cf9527486831e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0271020749ae70ce56cbd607a6f6662a</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_139.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_58.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_150.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_62.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657281</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Deployers">
      <data key="d0">Deployers</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Deployers are entities or individuals responsible for implementing and using AI systems in various contexts while adhering to the specified instructions.&lt;SEP&gt;Deployers are entities, which can be individuals or organizations, responsible for implementing artificial intelligence (AI) systems in practical applications. They often handle high-risk AI systems and are tasked with understanding their operational context to ensure compliance with relevant regulations. Deployers may partner with AI system providers to participate in regulatory initiatives known as AI regulatory sandboxes. Additionally, they have the responsibility of conducting impact assessments on these systems. Overall, Deployers play a crucial role in the deployment and regulation of AI technology, ensuring that it is used safely and effectively in various capacities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e76c1f88e5810a7e79cf9527486831e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a65ec6b0fbd17afe47587686523a725&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a68b9cb2eff595118d2af9313b6c89f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f5fc2b531499a81e154196ee1e86ac6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63ef16386f45c7bc364061cc094254fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0efde0679d72a2d51e7acdaf09979bfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aca56f82b70892874784bcec5c2bb2c3</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_2.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_27.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_9.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_58.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_62.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_72.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657170</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Local Public Authorities">
      <data key="d0">Local Public Authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Local Public Authorities are governmental entities at the municipal or regional levels considered in the guidelines for AI regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Local public authorities are government bodies at the municipal level that may provide assistance and resources to SMEs and start-ups regarding the AI regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b235644744fa597c94328afbeaa7e56b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e76c1f88e5810a7e79cf9527486831e5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_96.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_62.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657747</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Standardisation Development Process">
      <data key="d0">Standardisation Development Process</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The standardisation development process involves creating guidelines and standards for the implementation and operation of AI systems within the regulatory framework.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e76c1f88e5810a7e79cf9527486831e5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_62.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Board">
      <data key="d0">Board</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Board is a governing body dedicated to overseeing the regulation of artificial intelligence (AI) within the framework established by Member States. It plays a vital role in coordinating activities among national competent authorities regarding AI regulations and works closely with the AI Office to ensure the effective implementation of codes of practice and adherence to relevant regulations concerning AI.

Composed of representatives from various Member States, the Board promotes cooperation and regulatory compliance among market surveillance authorities. It is recognized as the European Artificial Intelligence Board and is committed to fostering a cohesive regulatory landscape across Member States. The Board not only monitors and evaluates the effectiveness of codes of practice but also ensures accountability among all participants involved in AI development and deployment. It solicits independent technical and scientific advice from the Union AI Testing Support Structures and other entities as required, enabling informed compliance decisions related to AI.

Additionally, the Board provides guidance and support to national competent authorities and the European Commission, ensuring adherence to best practices in the regulation of AI. It is involved in preparing agendas that align with existing regulations and procedural rules, and it oversees the activities of the Advisory Forum, from which it may solicit written contributions and opinions.

Through its comprehensive approach—including the processing of information on fines imposed under legal articles and insights from market surveillance authorities—the Board is an essential entity in the regulatory and advisory landscape, guiding the development of standardized templates and regulations while also playing a key role in the evaluation and assessment of AI models. Overall, the Board is instrumental in ensuring compliance with regulatory practices for AI and in coordinating collaboration among multiple stakeholders within the AI ecosystem.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d4058e2567f154203a2d9dacec4bdf7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d58805118916ede230a82a4ec3f60b3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad86065dee426d0a1db7444552c4a385&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-184360d53ae652d7f48a919e168f375a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3d60cf6cbe0ae91a9793cb5c98a4a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72498ec90c19419f10373dde7e7b51b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-712b56cbfc73c46eacde9204fa4e5c49&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85bb41c1db2d2e1883172e505d5f7b71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23ab4f338bfa06297d4c996d7d54dc70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-699c5fa3a4d8d093e6a599637df82443&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4dc0271c68856282748506ff58069b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d42aaf56c15be020feabced14d2409d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83ca16d466deaa751e3b9dc390e91e2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f76666cf495bb0f0810313fe42e2c882&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6de18717bcb0167956be85a15dd210f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85d8b1632746db5110bcd9632c1ace58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de6a0d59bb86cca6093fbb52cf156b4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e28e08bfb7b1ae3208e2c91ea6f1e4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aacbea1ddddc58fbf14c882b36d9a6b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4ac0ccf9bd954306cee6efbfd342416</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_92.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_149.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_57.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_84.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_101.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_75.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_67.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_143.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_71.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_65.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_56.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_62.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_150.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_70.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657728</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Operators">
      <data key="d0">Operators</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Operators are defined as individuals or entities that bear the responsibility for adhering to regulations governing various applications of artificial intelligence (AI) systems within the Union. These operators can include those who manage or utilize high-risk AI systems, providing digital products or services, and must remain compliant with relevant regulatory obligations. They play a crucial role in the value chain, encompassing various stakeholders such as importers, distributors, and others involved in ensuring compliance.

As part of their responsibilities, operators can be subject to fines and other penalties for any non-compliance with these regulations. This underscores the necessity for operators to maintain a comprehensive awareness and understanding of the legal framework governing AI systems to effectively manage compliance and mitigate risks associated with regulatory violations. In summary, operators are key players in the AI landscape, tasked with both the operational and legal aspects of utilizing technology within regulated environments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5b8c1122e1044e4445aa96d7fa6d5b6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-197c7357cf5fefe6ca4e08f847ff6a75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fc29985a43f3bd521b3a1c9eb9ba756&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3d60cf6cbe0ae91a9793cb5c98a4a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e7b8a0eb1cb8c27dfd822da15429870&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c32bc5fa5cdfa35a393a42535dc4fdfb</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_17.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_177.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_62.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_82.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_83.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657853</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Communication Campaigns">
      <data key="d0">Communication Campaigns</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Communication campaigns are organized efforts aiming to raise awareness about the obligations arising from the Regulation for operators.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e3d60cf6cbe0ae91a9793cb5c98a4a92</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_62.json</data>
    </node>
