    <node id="Workplace">
      <data key="d0">Workplace</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">The workplace is a context where the use of AI systems to detect emotional states may lead to detrimental treatment of individuals due to the imbalance of power.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8dead6db59d178a53a4fc03ed67a92e7</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_44.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Education">
      <data key="d0">Education</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Education is another context where AI systems could be implemented to assess emotional states, necessitating careful consideration of ethical implications.&lt;SEP&gt;Education refers to the systematic process of acquiring knowledge, skills, and competences necessary for individual and societal development.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7df88d0d68bb9e14cc05c3f581da8399&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dead6db59d178a53a4fc03ed67a92e7</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_44.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_56.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747658164</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Therapeutical Use">
      <data key="d0">Therapeutical Use</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Therapeutical use refers to the application of AI systems in medical settings, which is considered acceptable and not covered by the proposed prohibitions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8dead6db59d178a53a4fc03ed67a92e7</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_44.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Intrusive Technologies">
      <data key="d0">Intrusive Technologies</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Intrusive technologies refer to tools or systems that encroach on personal rights and freedoms, particularly with respect to identifying personal emotions and intentions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8dead6db59d178a53a4fc03ed67a92e7</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_44.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Discriminatory Outcomes">
      <data key="d0">Discriminatory Outcomes</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Discriminatory Outcomes relate to negative consequences faced by individuals or groups as a result of biased social scoring practices by AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Discriminatory outcomes are negative consequences that may arise from using AI systems to assess emotions, impacting certain groups or individuals unfavorably.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-28efea7f8fe5945cce5b7be57e88efe7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dead6db59d178a53a4fc03ed67a92e7</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_44.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_31.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Rights and Freedoms">
      <data key="d0">Rights and Freedoms</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Rights and freedoms encompass the basic entitlements of individuals, potentially compromised by intrusive technologies like AI biometric identification.&lt;SEP&gt;Rights and freedoms refer to the entitlements individuals have regarding personal privacy, autonomy, and protection from discrimination.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ab148daacc5693b15ec462635a5502a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dead6db59d178a53a4fc03ed67a92e7</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_32.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_44.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657468</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 60">
      <data key="d0">Article 60</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 60 is a comprehensive regulatory provision that governs the deployment and operation of artificial intelligence (AI) systems, with a particular focus on ensuring public safety. It outlines specific requirements and guidelines for testing high-risk AI systems in real-world conditions, ensuring that these systems comply with established safety standards. The article details testing procedures that must be followed to achieve compliance, emphasizing the importance of safety in the operation of such technologies.

Additionally, Article 60 addresses the issue of informed consent, establishing guidelines for obtaining consent from subjects involved in the testing process under real-world conditions. This provision ensures that ethical considerations are upheld while testing AI systems. Furthermore, Article 60 encompasses requirements related to information management and access pertaining to the EU Database, thereby providing a comprehensive framework for the responsible deployment of AI technologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-18e4ea35b819263359794e3a968f44ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a68b9cb2eff595118d2af9313b6c89f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c9405f93ec3e0ccf6209ed15ef0263f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35a30c75209c0fbb0ca1bb4afe44c77d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba5a4fee300868ea16940c9ea15f534a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43a1516ad8d48077af0d59fc01578f33</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_9.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_61.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_71.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_76.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657223</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union-wide Unique Single Identification Number">
      <data key="d0">Union-wide Unique Single Identification Number</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">This refers to a specific identification number assigned to the testing under Article 60, ensuring traceability and accountability.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ba5a4fee300868ea16940c9ea15f534a</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_61.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Subjects of Testing">
      <data key="d0">Subjects of Testing</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Subjects of testing refer to individuals who participate in the testing process and must provide informed consent before involvement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ba5a4fee300868ea16940c9ea15f534a</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_61.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Legal Representative">
      <data key="d0">Legal Representative</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A legal representative is an entity or individual appointed by a provider of AI systems to ensure compliance with EU regulations and to act on their behalf.&lt;SEP&gt;The legal representative refers to an individual who may act on behalf of the subjects of testing, particularly in matters related to informed consent.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-675b49fdde07175ec9a1afb693d1d877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba5a4fee300868ea16940c9ea15f534a</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_61.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_60.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657561</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Real World Conditions">
      <data key="d0">Real World Conditions</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Real World Conditions refer to the practical environment in which AI system testing occurs, focusing on realistic usage and impact assessment.&lt;SEP&gt;Real world conditions pertain to the actual circumstances under which the testing is conducted, emphasizing practical applicability and realism in the testing scenario.&lt;SEP&gt;Real World Conditions refer to the practical environments in which AI systems are tested for efficacy and compliance before deployment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-475967c83e624bc711a9ff13e8150163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f6e14583352886a741ac1d51eada03a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba5a4fee300868ea16940c9ea15f534a</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_61.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_60.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_57.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657689</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Informed Consent">
      <data key="d0">Informed Consent</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Informed Consent is a crucial principle in AI testing that mandates participants to voluntarily agree to the testing protocols after being fully educated about the implications of their participation. It encompasses a legal acknowledgment from subjects, allowing them to partake in the testing while retaining the right to withdraw their consent at any time. The process involves informing participants about various aspects of the testing, including associated risks and objectives, ensuring that they understand what their involvement entails.

Informed Consent emphasizes the importance of clear communication and understanding, particularly when it comes to the handling of personal data. It is especially relevant in contexts involving vulnerable populations, where participants must be adequately prepared to make informed decisions about their participation. Overall, Informed Consent is designed to protect the rights and autonomy of individuals by ensuring they are well-informed and agree willingly to participate in AI system testing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6f6e14583352886a741ac1d51eada03a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-675b49fdde07175ec9a1afb693d1d877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c9405f93ec3e0ccf6209ed15ef0263f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe76292b9a553c383dab6b0a4a67cee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4518ca313d8493e277775e1a9267b84d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba5a4fee300868ea16940c9ea15f534a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8022b105f5e7e2d0ba74bbe75f31f87</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_61.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_60.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_141.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657561</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Testing Arrangements">
      <data key="d0">Testing Arrangements</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Testing arrangements refer to the organizational and procedural aspects that govern how testing in real world conditions will be performed.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ba5a4fee300868ea16940c9ea15f534a</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_61.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 94">
      <data key="d0">Article 94</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 94 outlines procedural guarantees relevant to the Commission's powers and enforcement mechanisms.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ea1514e01d99729cb280141a24250142</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_88.json</data>
