    <node id="Article 75(3)">
      <data key="d0">Article 75(3)</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 75(3) pertains to provisions regarding market surveillance authorities and their relationship with the Commission.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ea1514e01d99729cb280141a24250142</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_88.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Chapter V">
      <data key="d0">Chapter V</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Chapter V discusses the powers and responsibilities of the Commission in relation to implementing regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Chapter V is a section of the Regulation, set to apply starting on 2 August 2025.&lt;SEP&gt;Chapter V of Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012 sets out obligations for standardisation, particularly regarding high-risk AI systems and general-purpose AI models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e93fbd1f7fc7cbb860b708f989987b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2739984aae71aa27a0af867bc197b730&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea1514e01d99729cb280141a24250142</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_40.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_88.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_113.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747658017</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Regulatory Sandbox">
      <data key="d0">AI Regulatory Sandbox</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The AI Regulatory Sandbox is a structured framework established by competent authorities to create a controlled environment for the development, testing, and validation of artificial intelligence (AI) systems. This environment is specifically designed to facilitate innovation in AI technologies while ensuring compliance with relevant legal and regulatory requirements. By allowing businesses and developers to experiment with high-risk AI applications under regulatory supervision, the sandbox promotes a balanced approach to exploring AI's capabilities while protecting personal data rights and public interests.

In this controlled setting, the AI Regulatory Sandbox enables stakeholders to effectively evaluate and manage potential risks associated with AI systems before their full deployment. The initiative serves as a crucial tool for both policymakers and developers, as it fosters collaborative exploration and provides valuable insights into implementation and best practices. By maintaining focus on regulatory adherence, the AI Regulatory Sandbox strives to support innovative advancements in AI while safeguarding compliance with established laws and frameworks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f8022b105f5e7e2d0ba74bbe75f31f87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-699b82035d71a633a86a67090e5a61e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a46250ea72037444e96653239f2893b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cdf1c7e7ad7fe2c6b1b8f1b0b12db35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe76292b9a553c383dab6b0a4a67cee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-184360d53ae652d7f48a919e168f375a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-475967c83e624bc711a9ff13e8150163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6adb64ff4e7b459fa1df815eac98b096&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94b20fb25052b5f99e867bd24213f8f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43a1516ad8d48077af0d59fc01578f33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0271020749ae70ce56cbd607a6f6662a</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_139.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_57.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_58.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_59.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_138.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_141.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_76.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_140.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657670</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 58">
      <data key="d0">Article 58</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 58 outlines the provisions for AI systems being tested within an AI regulatory sandbox, detailing the surveillance and compliance requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-43a1516ad8d48077af0d59fc01578f33</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_76.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 61">
      <data key="d0">Article 61</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 61 addresses additional compliance requirements related to AI systems, which market surveillance authorities must verify.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 61 establishes the requirements for informed consent from subjects being tested with AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6f6e14583352886a741ac1d51eada03a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43a1516ad8d48077af0d59fc01578f33</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_76.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_60.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657568</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Prospective Provider">
      <data key="d0">Prospective Provider</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Prospective Providers are individuals or entities interested in testing AI systems and must adhere to regulatory requirements during their testing process.&lt;SEP&gt;The prospective provider is an entity that manages the sandbox and conducts operations related to personal data processing within it.&lt;SEP&gt;The Prospective Provider refers to individuals or entities interested in accessing or contributing information to the EU Database.&lt;SEP&gt;The Prospective Provider refers to an entity that may be involved in deploying AI systems and participates in the planning and execution of testing in real-world conditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-18e4ea35b819263359794e3a968f44ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43a1516ad8d48077af0d59fc01578f33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f6e14583352886a741ac1d51eada03a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-800752b66b6fe0cd70bb0290efc2fbbe</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_76.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_60.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_59.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_71.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657577</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Serious Incident">
      <data key="d0">Serious Incident</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A Serious Incident refers to significant occurrences that may compromise the testing of AI systems, prompting intervention from market surveillance authorities.&lt;SEP&gt;A serious incident refers to a significant occurrence that must be reported by providers or deployers of AI systems when they become aware of it.&lt;SEP&gt;A serious incident refers to any event related to high-risk AI systems that requires reporting to the market surveillance authorities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0dc307b8b7cb1f0e39aa9b4b1839c408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b0c31436f0e7ce27ce5952aa2bf9ae5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43a1516ad8d48077af0d59fc01578f33</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_76.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_73.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747464360</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Decision">
      <data key="d0">Decision</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A Decision made by market surveillance authorities can lead to actions affecting the testing of AI systems, including suspensions or modifications.&lt;SEP&gt;The Decision refers to the formal ruling made by the Market Surveillance Authority regarding a provider or prospective provider's compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-43a1516ad8d48077af0d59fc01578f33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb3519876fdebea487c9995e6d3ae4fd</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_76.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 60(4)">
      <data key="d0">Article 60(4)</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 60(4) outlines provisions regarding decisions or objections related to market surveillance in AI systems, specifically on the process of communicating grounds.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cb3519876fdebea487c9995e6d3ae4fd</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_76.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Objection">
      <data key="d0">Objection</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Objection pertains to a formal challenge against the Decision made by the Market Surveillance Authority, including specific grounds for challenge.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cb3519876fdebea487c9995e6d3ae4fd</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_76.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Testing Plan">
      <data key="d0">Testing Plan</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Testing Plan outlines the procedures and requirements for evaluating AI systems by relevant authorities, including the Market Surveillance Authority.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cb3519876fdebea487c9995e6d3ae4fd</data>
