      <data key="d5">1747464741</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Vulnerable Groups">
      <data key="d0">Vulnerable Groups</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Vulnerable Groups refer to specific populations that may be disproportionately affected by the deployment and operation of artificial intelligence (AI) systems. These groups are characterized by a higher risk of experiencing adverse impacts due to socio-economic factors, necessitating special consideration and protection under regulations. Vulnerable Groups include segments of the population such as minors, the elderly, and individuals with disabilities, all of whom may face greater threats from AI systems. Additionally, these groups may require additional safeguards in light of their susceptibility to risk, particularly during the testing of AI systems. Overall, Vulnerable Groups encompass those who might be affected differently by the advancements and implications of AI technology.&lt;SEP&gt;Vulnerable groups are individuals who may face higher risks and ethical considerations during testing due to their circumstances or status.&lt;SEP&gt;Vulnerable groups include individuals who require special consideration during testing due to their age or disability, ensuring their rights and protections.&lt;SEP&gt;Vulnerable groups include populations that face systemic discrimination and bias, often including racial or ethnic minorities that may be adversely affected by AI decision-making.&lt;SEP&gt;Vulnerable groups refer to populations that may be at risk of discrimination or negative impacts from AI systems, including racial or ethnic minorities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-de3f18a6d766d2baa57ae891b9da7741&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8022b105f5e7e2d0ba74bbe75f31f87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-675b49fdde07175ec9a1afb693d1d877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7eb8204c84c6a7310e75effed716fcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cb2802f1b508b813d06e58ae27a1f77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50beca99a2207706ee9f0ad17a4205ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35a30c75209c0fbb0ca1bb4afe44c77d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa9e2916955e882c73231ed69851f6ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-445327adc051facf545b6358f6f01466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb43ec5a01dc502046ab6ffbe3a25504</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_132.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_60.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_9.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_141.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_93.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_67.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_7.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_79.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657792</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Risk Management Procedures">
      <data key="d0">Risk Management Procedures</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Risk Management Procedures are systematic methods established to evaluate and mitigate risks associated with high-risk AI systems during their development and deployment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-35a30c75209c0fbb0ca1bb4afe44c77d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_9.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Intended Purpose">
      <data key="d0">Intended Purpose</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Intended Purpose describes the specific use or objective that high-risk AI systems are designed to achieve, which significantly influences the risk assessment process.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-35a30c75209c0fbb0ca1bb4afe44c77d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_9.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Compliance Requirements">
      <data key="d0">Compliance Requirements</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Compliance Requirements are regulatory standards that high-risk AI systems must meet to ensure safety and efficacy in medical applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Compliance Requirements are the legal and regulatory standards that high-risk AI systems must meet to ensure they are safe for market placement and use.&lt;SEP&gt;Compliance requirements outline the necessary standards and practices that AI systems must adhere to throughout their development and operational lifecycle.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-35a30c75209c0fbb0ca1bb4afe44c77d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc1203d6797827fbb6dbb7dc7c8d7d26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b754e2170dea6f93253ec4fd1fa88d5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_84.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_9.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_71.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657064</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Providers of High-Risk AI Systems">
      <data key="d0">Providers of High-Risk AI Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Providers are organizations that place high-risk AI systems on the market or put them into service and are responsible for ensuring compliance with regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Providers of High-Risk AI Systems are entities or organizations that develop and deploy AI technologies categorized as high risk, responsible for ensuring compliance with regulatory standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Providers of high-risk AI systems are responsible for maintaining safety protocols and systems for improving AI as per market requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Providers of high-risk AI systems are entities that develop, supply, or integrate advanced artificial intelligence systems that pose significant risks to users or society.&lt;SEP&gt;Providers of high-risk AI systems are organizations responsible for ensuring compliance with regulatory standards for AI technology.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8143bb5053cad47b9eaf4c05c9556429&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35a30c75209c0fbb0ca1bb4afe44c77d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68d6983d829937a84d37118dacc3e39c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54948128ea5a4b84a219d7dbaa346a50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e978e96ac6d99cf448b53260c07dded</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_9.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_155.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_16.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_90.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_20.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747658129</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Adverse Impact">
      <data key="d0">Adverse Impact</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Adverse Impact refers to negative consequences that may arise from the use of AI systems, potentially affecting health, safety, or rights of individuals.&lt;SEP&gt;Adverse Impact refers to the potential negative effects that high-risk AI systems may have on individuals, especially among vulnerable populations such as minors.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-50beca99a2207706ee9f0ad17a4205ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35a30c75209c0fbb0ca1bb4afe44c77d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_9.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_7.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Trade Restrictions">
      <data key="d0">Trade Restrictions</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Trade restrictions are policies that limit or control the exchange of goods and services, applied here in the context of AI system regulations to protect health, safety, and rights.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9685a1f72e235a3f5b9ee69878eedb21</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_66.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Risk Management Requirements">
      <data key="d0">Risk Management Requirements</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Risk management requirements are necessary guidelines for high-risk AI systems to ensure safety and compliance with health and fundamental rights standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9685a1f72e235a3f5b9ee69878eedb21</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_66.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Quality and Relevance of Data Sets">
      <data key="d0">Quality and Relevance of Data Sets</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The quality and relevance of data sets used in AI systems are crucial for minimizing risks and ensuring accurate outputs from these technologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9685a1f72e235a3f5b9ee69878eedb21</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_66.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Record-Keeping">
      <data key="d0">Record-Keeping</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Record-keeping is a practice that involves maintaining accurate logs and documentation to ensure compliance and oversight in AI system management.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9685a1f72e235a3f5b9ee69878eedb21</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_66.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Transparency">
      <data key="d0">Transparency</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Transparency in AI involves providing clear information to deployers and users regarding how AI systems operate and their associated risks.&lt;SEP&gt;Transparency in AI signifies the need for traceability and explainability in AI interactions, ensuring users are aware when they are interacting with AI.&lt;SEP&gt;Transparency is an ethical principle that necessitates clarity and traceability in AI systems' operations and implications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9685a1f72e235a3f5b9ee69878eedb21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-256a6003a5841f2764536c55f7086431&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-849f8f0403e6b12fa8a9c24b84c094c7</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_27.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_66.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Human Oversight">
      <data key="d0">Human Oversight</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Human Oversight involves assigning qualified individuals to monitor and guide the operations of high-risk AI systems to ensure safe and compliant usage.&lt;SEP&gt;Human oversight refers to the requirement for human involvement in monitoring high-risk AI systems to prevent misuse or harm.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e8c5a915dca180e1c423cefa27ea6cd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9685a1f72e235a3f5b9ee69878eedb21</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_66.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657948</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Robustness">
      <data key="d0">Robustness</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Robustness refers to the requirement that AI systems can perform accurately and consistently under various conditions without failure.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9685a1f72e235a3f5b9ee69878eedb21</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_66.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Accuracy">
      <data key="d0">Accuracy</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Accuracy in AI systems pertains to the fidelity of the outputs provided relative to the actual real-world conditions they are designed to model.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9685a1f72e235a3f5b9ee69878eedb21</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_66.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Cybersecurity">
      <data key="d0">Cybersecurity</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Cybersecurity encompasses practices intended to safeguard computer systems and networks, which national competent authorities are mandated to oversee.&lt;SEP&gt;Cybersecurity measures are necessary to protect high-risk AI systems from malicious attacks and to safeguard the integrity of data used.&lt;SEP&gt;Cybersecurity refers to the protection of internet-connected systems from cyber threats, which is essential for ensuring the safety of AI models.&lt;SEP&gt;Cybersecurity refers to the practices and technologies designed to protect computers, networks, and data from unauthorized access, attack, or damage.&lt;SEP&gt;Cybersecurity refers to the practice of protecting systems, networks, and programs from digital attacks, particularly focusing on AI systems in this context.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9685a1f72e235a3f5b9ee69878eedb21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bee8a141261944c2193bcb00b304b768&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5765a06abb615496a937c9303e1583cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22275ba6343521309923fef233affa2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d7d6f2dd7e28584da10fdb340b37fd0</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_66.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_54.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_114.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_76.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_70.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657369</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Penalties">
      <data key="d0">Penalties</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Penalties are financial or administrative punishments imposed for violations of the Regulation, aimed at ensuring compliance from Member States and their providers.&lt;SEP&gt;Penalties include various forms of punishment, such as fines, that may be enforced for failure to comply with the Regulation's obligations.&lt;SEP&gt;Penalties refer to the consequences or fines that result from non-compliance with the provisions of the Regulation and will come into effect on 2 August 2025.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1b43f399350f0fc36795c0ce358459d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ad9752391e53e840a2d8ac0861f8948&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae3ab8a3b5c5d0c61e8b99fa718913b0</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_169.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_179.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_168.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747464818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Administrative Fines">
      <data key="d0">Administrative Fines</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Administrative fines are financial penalties imposed for violations of regulations, specifically within the realm of AI practices and data protection. These fines serve as effective and dissuasive measures, and they are typically set by National Competent Authorities or the European Data Protection Supervisor, depending on the regulatory context. The amounts of these fines vary based on the severity of the infringement, with specific amounts designated for different types of violations. While administrative fines are generally applied in response to non-compliance with laws and regulations, they may be waived under certain conditions. Overall, administrative fines are a critical tool for enforcing compliance and ensuring adherence to established legal frameworks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1b43f399350f0fc36795c0ce358459d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c31e49eb2274702ec6ced9550f1ca86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e7b8a0eb1cb8c27dfd822da15429870&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-111c71f234a0f2d1b26490907acae6eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85bb41c1db2d2e1883172e505d5f7b71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-828a2d9070cae319b764e3b609bc9b81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5da2f6b1c2fa5619efa26719534e9c35</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_100.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_57.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_168.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657782</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Infringements">
      <data key="d0">Infringements</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Infringements are violations of the provisions outlined in the Regulation that can lead to the imposition of penalties or fines.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1b43f399350f0fc36795c0ce358459d9</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_168.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SME">
      <data key="d0">SME</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">SME refers to Small and Medium-sized Enterprises, which are considered when assessing penalties for infringements of the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1b43f399350f0fc36795c0ce358459d9</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_168.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Start-Up">
      <data key="d0">Start-Up</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Start-Up refers to newly established enterprises that are taken into consideration regarding penalties and compliance under the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1b43f399350f0fc36795c0ce358459d9</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_168.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="National Competent Authorities">
      <data key="d0">National Competent Authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">National Competent Authorities (NCAs) are designated government bodies within European Union (EU) member states, entrusted with the critical role of enforcing regulations and ensuring compliance with legal standards, particularly in relation to artificial intelligence (AI) systems. Their responsibilities are multifaceted, encompassing the oversight of the implementation of laws and policies related to AI and data protection, thereby ensuring that technological advancements align with established legal frameworks.

NCAs primarily conduct conformity assessments, manage compliance, and uphold safety standards, particularly for high-risk AI systems. They are responsible for addressing any reported infringements of regulations, notifying the European Commission of significant findings, and tackling violations. Additionally, NCAs play a pivotal role in the establishment and supervision of AI regulatory sandboxes—controlled environments designed to foster innovation while ensuring adherence to relevant legal requirements.

In summary, National Competent Authorities are essential players in the EU's regulatory landscape. They safeguard public interests and promote responsible technological progress in the field of AI, maintaining regulatory integrity and overseeing the safe development and testing of AI systems within their jurisdictions. Through their initiatives, NCAs ensure compliance with EU regulations, documentation, and safety standards, effectively coordinating activities related to regulatory compliance for AI technologies and protecting public safety.&lt;SEP&gt;National Competent Authorities are regulatory bodies in EU member states responsible for overseeing compliance with EU legislation regarding high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f13d730755b7535c59eb130d6f7ac62e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72cfde8a7c3c94fdf1dc93c4253bec9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7859a0c655f74761757b416c3b50bf36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dbe8a4749b15b91fcb1062fee4fa778&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b0c31436f0e7ce27ce5952aa2bf9ae5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22275ba6343521309923fef233affa2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0271020749ae70ce56cbd607a6f6662a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe05ef9eea0acc63f05d5b9d6a147298&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0779dfb4a5c0f82f05a67985fe0224a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cdf1c7e7ad7fe2c6b1b8f1b0b12db35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-184360d53ae652d7f48a919e168f375a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98532c431ec75ae38c76dc0730337a16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-595952fa3e7e47cb312adaaad303b73c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34333cde7ca701413cb4d0a0ef1129e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6adb64ff4e7b459fa1df815eac98b096&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85bb41c1db2d2e1883172e505d5f7b71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c31e49eb2274702ec6ced9550f1ca86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d42aaf56c15be020feabced14d2409d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-599d61ad7be34e2603c3fef13f2ff8dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11bdaa862215570a86eed137e3092ea6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac68c725e087cb7c659f2dd75f0a6e34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-447d51c65bac6d28fd62c36c3e70e08b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc97d8ad7f3aa0522d885f92ee323822&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50beca99a2207706ee9f0ad17a4205ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aca56f82b70892874784bcec5c2bb2c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46418d497e0c090818a97380d173293d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-475967c83e624bc711a9ff13e8150163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95424b9dff57302628c496570b4baff4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97ee5867d3c03f24001b650ad752686d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e7b8a0eb1cb8c27dfd822da15429870&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4672fd3df7077626af67d20e46d3fcb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c32bc5fa5cdfa35a393a42535dc4fdfb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77093970e26d1be04734ed16ea88f777</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_36.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_139.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_115.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_17.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_47.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_57.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_154.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_126.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_138.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_73.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_101.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_58.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_18.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_7.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_153.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_53.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_66.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_70.json</data>
