    <node id="Regulation (EU) 2016/679">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) 2016/679</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) 2016/679 is a comprehensive regulation in EU law on data protection and privacy in the European Union and the European Economic Area.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2016/679 is a key piece of data protection legislation in the EU, commonly known as the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), which sets guidelines for the collection and processing of personal data.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2016/679, commonly known as the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), is a comprehensive legislative framework established by the European Parliament and the Council aimed at governing the protection of personal data and privacy across the European Union (EU). This regulation is crucial in safeguarding the rights of individuals concerning the processing of their personal data, ensuring data privacy and security, and facilitating the free movement of personal data within the EU.

The GDPR delineates specific rights for individuals regarding data protection and privacy, particularly focusing on the handling and processing of personal data, including sensitive categories such as biometric information. It plays a vital role in the governance of data processing, especially in relation to high-risk artificial intelligence (AI) systems, to uphold individuals' privacy and data rights across various sectors within the EU.

In addition to enhancing the protection of personal data, the GDPR provides a legal framework that sets guidelines for the collection and processing of personal information. It also addresses the implications of data protection in sensitive areas such as law enforcement, thereby solidifying its significance in today’s digital landscape, ensuring that the personal data of individuals throughout the European Union is adequately protected.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2016/679 pertains to the protection of personal data and privacy in the European Union and the European Economic Area.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2016/679, also known as the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), is a comprehensive data protection legislation in the EU.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fe76292b9a553c383dab6b0a4a67cee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0073df6368131f4f385a66430ef1c4f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0efde0679d72a2d51e7acdaf09979bfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ac98f64f8751ad51246ca16d843f030&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc038db2f25d511bf84cccc9550e10c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8833999c9ef9aa31a007f2e77ffea02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3105f8ed20ed5608a4571fe7b1d8f942&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78dcdae0f5d22df28405d8ae03e038d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bece07e296fce9647a40a0dde904fe4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-602b68fe088482c0037845fc0b520c30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-445327adc051facf545b6358f6f01466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de40ca48bf7dafc1db86f4d8a18d2bba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77a0a99b47c288a96d7474c796efb766&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85605aee8aaac2bf4ad29d80d902148f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15eee417af0ebe299ed66be76a0b845a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a46250ea72037444e96653239f2893b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4882abf1dd869d3dff00b8d88ee946a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4672fd3df7077626af67d20e46d3fcb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-498834b2d84eaf9afe4e5fb0df15933c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77093970e26d1be04734ed16ea88f777</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_2.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_27.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_10.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_53.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_14.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_5.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_67.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_70.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_39.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_140.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_95.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657955</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EU Database">
      <data key="d0">EU Database</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The EU Database is a proposed, secure, non-public repository managed by the European Commission, designed to oversee and manage information concerning high-risk AI systems. This initiative is rooted in the need for enhanced transparency and traceability regarding the registration of AI systems, particularly those related to specific regulations, such as biometric identification systems. By mandating the registration of high-risk AI systems, the EU Database aims to facilitate comprehensive monitoring and compliance with regulatory standards within the European Union.

The repository will contain sensitive information relevant to EU regulations and directives, restricting access to specific authorities to ensure data security. It is tailored to support the monitoring and reporting of AI compliance and incident statistics throughout the Union. Moreover, the EU Database is structured to house information related not only to high-risk AI systems but also to non-high-risk systems, thereby encompassing a broader scope of AI technology under the scrutiny of EU regulations.

Overall, the EU Database represents a strategic effort by the European Commission to bolster oversight and accountability in the deployment of advanced AI technologies, while providing a framework for effective market surveillance and regulatory compliance in the EU.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-18e4ea35b819263359794e3a968f44ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-675b49fdde07175ec9a1afb693d1d877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffc59c087d680631c2a594779449f195&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72498ec90c19419f10373dde7e7b51b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7f74259ac0ec20e9f3989df868f56b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98532c431ec75ae38c76dc0730337a16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-166a35f517674f4ceba2754c65f88c5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4672fd3df7077626af67d20e46d3fcb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77093970e26d1be04734ed16ea88f777&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8022b105f5e7e2d0ba74bbe75f31f87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2806e288e0b71013209c4ad85ecaa38b</data>
