    <node id="Article 49">
      <data key="d0">Article 49</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 49 describes the registration process for systems utilized in law enforcement, allowing for monitoring and accountability.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 49 outlines specific obligations and procedures related to the registration of AI systems deemed not high-risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 49 outlines specific legal provisions for the registration and testing of high-risk AI systems within the EU.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 49 pertains to the registration obligations for deployers of high-risk AI systems as mandated by EU regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 49 refers to specific obligations related to the registration of high-risk AI systems as defined in Union regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-675b49fdde07175ec9a1afb693d1d877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffc59c087d680631c2a594779449f195&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78dcdae0f5d22df28405d8ae03e038d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bece07e296fce9647a40a0dde904fe4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d64a2a65aec35f8304efaaee30e0034d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_5.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_60.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_6.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657948</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 96">
      <data key="d0">Article 96</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 96 involves guidelines related to determining the practical implementation of regulations concerning AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 96 refers to the specific provision within the Regulation that mandates the issuance of guidelines by the Commission regarding penalties.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d64a2a65aec35f8304efaaee30e0034d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7365f713d09e74d49090cb78cb3e19b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_6.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 97">
      <data key="d0">Article 97</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 97 empowers the Commission to adopt delegated acts that may amend existing regulatory documents concerning high-risk AI compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 97 is a crucial provision within the European Union regulatory framework that grants the Commission the authority to adopt delegated acts pertaining to artificial intelligence (AI) regulations. This article enables the Commission to amend conditions related to compliance and safety considerations based on evidence. Specifically, Article 97 outlines the procedural guidelines for modifying thresholds and supplementary benchmarks in AI regulation. Additionally, it plays a significant role in the amendment of technical documentation associated with compliance assessment and allows changes to the Annexes linked to compliance. Furthermore, Article 97 empowers the Commission to amend existing laws regarding the EU Declaration of Conformity, ensuring a robust legal framework for adapting to evolving standards in AI regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f13d730755b7535c59eb130d6f7ac62e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5abff9e94aff7675c473268fd21bf551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41e5d20a8e9427a4698b84f758676994&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55bfb9287798720e37fcd8bae961e88b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d64a2a65aec35f8304efaaee30e0034d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e519b84a1d0987cd3b0aab32a476aa33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdd0ab3aadbdd5226fa3661ea9057181</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_47.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_6.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_53.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_43.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_51.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_11.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657909</data>
    </node>
    <node id="February 2, 2026">
      <data key="d0">February 2, 2026</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">February 2, 2026, is the deadline set for the Commission to provide guidelines on the implementation of AI-related regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8cb1edc11e8b8d0e952b15617a80f379</data>
