      <data key="d5">1747464838</data>
    </node>
    <node id="2 August 2027">
      <data key="d0">2 August 2027</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">2 August 2027 is the deadline for compliance with the regulation for providers of general-purpose AI models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-47ce3f90343791af10ffae2a7848f26e</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_111.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="2 August 2030">
      <data key="d0">2 August 2030</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">2 August 2030 represents the date mentioned in the regulation, outlining the compliance timeline for AI model providers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-47ce3f90343791af10ffae2a7848f26e</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_111.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation on General-Purpose AI Models">
      <data key="d0">Regulation on General-Purpose AI Models</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The Regulation on General-Purpose AI Models sets forth rules and deadlines for compliance and market entry for AI providers.&lt;SEP&gt;This Regulation outlines the rules and standards governing the development and implementation of general-purpose AI models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-47ce3f90343791af10ffae2a7848f26e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af991f85166d6ddfbbf84e4a73207d3d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_111.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_162.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657343</data>
    </node>
    <node id="scientific panel">
      <data key="d0">scientific panel</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The scientific panel is a specialized group composed of independent experts selected by the Commission for their expertise in artificial intelligence (AI). This panel plays a crucial role in offering advice and support to Member States concerning the enforcement of AI regulations. Its responsibilities include evaluating general-purpose AI models and identifying potential systemic risks associated with these technologies at the Union level. In addition, the scientific panel is tasked with overseeing governance systems pertinent to AI and providing alerts about any identified risks that may arise from the use of AI models. Through its evaluations and alerts, the panel aims to ensure the safety and effectiveness of AI technologies while aiding in regulatory tasks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1c408a5b914a49af8b42e7e84ad02be6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ea6a588c10ad2fe493ec8cc1913f72d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-140dff8b8263721e25ea86a4104c273d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f3c3fe390cb5d40b199e1bcc024928f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a0c1908573a7d6a832a6b35befbd7ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec7c9ce58b650afe456517c2483e56c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_163.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_113.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_69.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_68.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_90.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747464141</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union AI testing support">
      <data key="d0">Union AI testing support</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Union AI testing support is a framework that aids Member States in accessing expert advice and support for AI testing activities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5ea6a588c10ad2fe493ec8cc1913f72d</data>
