    <node id="Third-Party Conformity Assessments">
      <data key="d0">Third-Party Conformity Assessments</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Third-party conformity assessments are evaluations performed by independent bodies to ensure compliance with established standards and regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-97ee5867d3c03f24001b650ad752686d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_126.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Requirements">
      <data key="d0">Requirements</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Requirements encompass the set of conditions that notified bodies must fulfill to operate effectively and compliantly.&lt;SEP&gt;Requirements refer to the obligations and standards that entities must meet when integrating or utilizing AI components, especially related to the responsibilities along the AI value chain.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-97ee5867d3c03f24001b650ad752686d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-778cb9e68fcb25e3f810e3cea927f7b2</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_89.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_126.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Providers of high-risk AI systems">
      <data key="d0">Providers of high-risk AI systems</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Providers of high-risk AI systems are entities responsible for maintaining logs generated by their AI systems, ensuring compliance with Union and national laws.&lt;SEP&gt;Providers of high-risk AI systems refers to companies or entities developing artificial intelligence technologies that have significant societal risks and obligations under the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c852bda35515c8d5385ef007c8140254&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70337c5367702b9a8ef4dd8a241aa46d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_19.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_178.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EU Union Law">
      <data key="d0">EU Union Law</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">EU Union Law encompasses regulations and directives governing the operation of high-risk AI systems, especially concerning data protection and log maintenance.&lt;SEP&gt;EU Union Law encompasses regulations governing the deployment of AI systems, ensuring they adhere to prescribed standards and obligations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e8c5a915dca180e1c423cefa27ea6cd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c852bda35515c8d5385ef007c8140254</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_19.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_26.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657948</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 12(1)">
      <data key="d0">Article 12(1)</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 12(1) refers to specific provisions regarding logging requirements for high-risk AI systems within legal frameworks, likely within EU regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c852bda35515c8d5385ef007c8140254</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_19.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="High-risk AI Systems">
      <data key="d0">High-risk AI Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">High-risk AI Systems refer to AI applications that present significant risks, particularly in areas like law enforcement, migration, asylum, and critical infrastructure.&lt;SEP&gt;High-risk AI systems are advanced artificial intelligence systems considered to pose potential risks to safety or rights, necessitating strict regulatory oversight.&lt;SEP&gt;High-risk AI systems are defined categories of artificial intelligence that require registration and specific regulatory oversight due to their potential impact.&lt;SEP&gt;High-risk AI systems are artificial intelligence applications deemed to pose significant risks to safety or fundamental rights.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4f41337092de45470ab838aff17309ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c852bda35515c8d5385ef007c8140254&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-166a35f517674f4ceba2754c65f88c5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7f74259ac0ec20e9f3989df868f56b4</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_19.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_49.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_41.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_131.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747658160</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI-enabled Manipulative Techniques">
      <data key="d0">AI-enabled Manipulative Techniques</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">AI-enabled manipulative techniques refer to methods that use artificial intelligence to influence individuals' decisions and behaviors in ways that impair their autonomy and decision-making.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7a0ae2ebdd7c0c6e56069b878ca85c78</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_29.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive (EU) 2019/882">
      <data key="d0">Directive (EU) 2019/882</data>
      <data key="d1">legislation</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive (EU) 2019/882 is a European Parliament regulation that focuses on establishing accessibility requirements for products and services within the EU market. It is designed to ensure that all individuals, including those with disabilities, can access and use these products and services without encountering barriers. The directive also addresses the standards for accessibility of technology, aiming to protect individuals from manipulative and deceptive practices related to AI systems. Furthermore, Directive (EU) 2019/882 outlines specific requirements regarding the availability and use of public databases, particularly concerning high-risk AI systems, which must comply with the established accessibility standards. Overall, this legislation reflects the EU's commitment to fostering an inclusive environment by ensuring accessibility across various domains.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-41b3ba2302e956849a6be7455071577d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33366c5df404f37775ccbf3ec455b578&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a0ae2ebdd7c0c6e56069b878ca85c78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2806e288e0b71013209c4ad85ecaa38b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-166a35f517674f4ceba2754c65f88c5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17045c951f494f621b2305960aade53f</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_29.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_131.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_80.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747464631</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Machine-Brain Interfaces">
      <data key="d0">Machine-Brain Interfaces</data>
      <data key="d1">technology</data>
      <data key="d2">Machine-brain interfaces allow for direct communication between a brain and an external device, potentially manipulating user behavior through stimuli that users may not consciously perceive.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7a0ae2ebdd7c0c6e56069b878ca85c78</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_29.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Virtual Reality">
      <data key="d0">Virtual Reality</data>
      <data key="d1">technology</data>
      <data key="d2">Virtual reality creates simulated environments that can alter users' perceptions and experiences, potentially impacting their decision-making and behaviors without their awareness.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7a0ae2ebdd7c0c6e56069b878ca85c78</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_29.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Extreme Poverty">
      <data key="d0">Extreme Poverty</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">Extreme poverty describes a socioeconomic condition that increases individuals' vulnerability to exploitation by manipulative AI practices.&lt;SEP&gt;Extreme poverty refers to a condition where individuals lack sufficient resources to meet basic living standards and are vulnerable to exploitation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7a0ae2ebdd7c0c6e56069b878ca85c78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41b3ba2302e956849a6be7455071577d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_29.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Ethnic or Religious Minorities">
      <data key="d0">Ethnic or Religious Minorities</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">Ethnic or religious minorities are groups of people who are distinct from the majority population in terms of ethnicity or religion and may face vulnerability and discrimination.&lt;SEP&gt;Ethnic or religious minorities may face heightened risks of exploitation through manipulative AI systems due to their marginalized social status.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7a0ae2ebdd7c0c6e56069b878ca85c78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41b3ba2302e956849a6be7455071577d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_29.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Manipulation Techniques">
      <data key="d0">Manipulation Techniques</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Manipulation techniques utilize psychological and technological methods to influence individuals' choices and behaviors without their conscious awareness.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7a0ae2ebdd7c0c6e56069b878ca85c78</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_29.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Subliminal Components">
      <data key="d0">Subliminal Components</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Subliminal components are stimuli that are presented below the threshold of conscious perception, potentially affecting decision-making and behavior without individuals being aware.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7a0ae2ebdd7c0c6e56069b878ca85c78</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_29.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="User Autonomy">
      <data key="d0">User Autonomy</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">User autonomy is the capacity of individuals to make their own choices and exercise control over their actions, which can be compromised by manipulative technologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7a0ae2ebdd7c0c6e56069b878ca85c78</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_29.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Psychological Health">
      <data key="d0">Psychological Health</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Psychological health encompasses the emotional and mental well-being of individuals, which can be adversely affected by manipulative AI practices.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7a0ae2ebdd7c0c6e56069b878ca85c78</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_29.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Financial Interests">
      <data key="d0">Financial Interests</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Financial interests relate to a person's monetary benefits or losses, which may be manipulated by AI systems to influence their decision-making.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7a0ae2ebdd7c0c6e56069b878ca85c78</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_29.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Exploitation of Vulnerabilities">
      <data key="d0">Exploitation of Vulnerabilities</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Exploitation of vulnerabilities refers to the manipulation of individuals' weaknesses, such as age, disability, or socioeconomic status, through deceptive practices.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7a0ae2ebdd7c0c6e56069b878ca85c78</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_29.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive 2005/29/EC">
      <data key="d0">Directive 2005/29/EC</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive 2005/29/EC addresses unfair business-to-consumer commercial practices in the internal market.&lt;SEP&gt;Directive 2005/29/EC addresses unfair commercial practices that harm consumers, setting regulations applicable to all member states.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-17045c951f494f621b2305960aade53f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41b3ba2302e956849a6be7455071577d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_29.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Manipulative AI Practices">
      <data key="d0">Manipulative AI Practices</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Manipulative AI practices involve techniques used by AI systems that distort or exploit user behavior, potentially leading to significant harm to individuals or groups.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-41b3ba2302e956849a6be7455071577d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_29.json</data>
    </node>
