    <node id="Unfair Commercial Practices Directive">
      <data key="d0">Unfair Commercial Practices Directive</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The Unfair Commercial Practices Directive addresses consumer protection and aims to prevent misleading advertising and aggressive marketing practices.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-41d5cbcbecdcfde489e01bbfe08dc447</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_29.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directives 97/7/EC">
      <data key="d0">Directives 97/7/EC</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive 97/7/EC relates to the protection of consumers in distance contracts, providing regulations on e-commerce transactions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-41d5cbcbecdcfde489e01bbfe08dc447</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_29.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Information Ecosystem">
      <data key="d0">Information Ecosystem</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The information ecosystem encompasses the dynamics of information creation, distribution, and trust, affected by advancements in AI and synthetic content generation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3bb5eb0651d16c25633339b4b2cb2e46</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_133.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Forgery Techniques">
      <data key="d0">Forgery Techniques</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Forgery techniques include methods of creating misleading or fraudulent content that can be hard to distinguish from genuine content, especially when generated by AI.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3bb5eb0651d16c25633339b4b2cb2e46</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_133.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Watermarks">
      <data key="d0">Watermarks</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Watermarks are technical solutions used to mark content in a machine-readable format to indicate its origin, particularly useful in tracing AI-generated material.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3bb5eb0651d16c25633339b4b2cb2e46</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_133.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Metadata Identifications">
      <data key="d0">Metadata Identifications</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Metadata identifications provide additional data about content that can aid in establishing its authenticity and origin, especially in the context of AI-generated content.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3bb5eb0651d16c25633339b4b2cb2e46</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_133.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Cryptographic Methods">
      <data key="d0">Cryptographic Methods</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Cryptographic methods are advanced techniques used to secure data, ensuring the authenticity and provenance of content, especially in digital formats.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3bb5eb0651d16c25633339b4b2cb2e46</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_133.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Technical Solutions">
      <data key="d0">Technical Solutions</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Technical Solutions are strategies or approaches designed to enhance the safety and reliability of AI systems, aiming to prevent negative outcomes.&lt;SEP&gt;Technical solutions refer to various implemented methods aimed at enhancing the reliability and traceability of generated content, particularly against misinformation.&lt;SEP&gt;Technical Solutions involve methods and strategies designed to correct or reverse adverse outcomes produced by AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Technical solutions refer to methods and technologies developed to meet compliance and operational efficiency in line with regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3bb5eb0651d16c25633339b4b2cb2e46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50beca99a2207706ee9f0ad17a4205ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e24261c10195e33e965bd7e966c33337&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f15de033aa4361b6dbf4b5d72ede05a5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_75.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_133.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_121.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_7.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Content Generation">
      <data key="d0">Content Generation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Content generation refers to the process of creating media and information, which can be done through human effort or by automated systems such as AI.&lt;SEP&gt;Content generation refers to the process where various forms of media, including text, audio, images, and video, are created using generative AI technology.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3bb5eb0651d16c25633339b4b2cb2e46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8033b978339bfb2f89fde823ffa3f524</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_133.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Synthetic Content">
      <data key="d0">Synthetic Content</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Synthetic content encompasses material generated by AI systems that mimics human-created content, often raising concerns over authenticity and trust.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3bb5eb0651d16c25633339b4b2cb2e46</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_133.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Misinformation">
      <data key="d0">Misinformation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Misinformation involves the distribution of false or misleading information, which can be exacerbated by the capabilities of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3bb5eb0651d16c25633339b4b2cb2e46</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_133.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Consumer Deception">
      <data key="d0">Consumer Deception</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Consumer deception refers to practices that mislead consumers, often facilitated by misleading synthetic content produced by AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3bb5eb0651d16c25633339b4b2cb2e46</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_133.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Manipulation at Scale">
      <data key="d0">Manipulation at Scale</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Manipulation at scale refers to a significant level of influence or alteration of information that can affect large audiences using AI technologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3bb5eb0651d16c25633339b4b2cb2e46</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_133.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Providers">
      <data key="d0">AI Providers</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">AI Providers are companies or entities that develop and offer AI models, including those that fall under general-purpose categories.&lt;SEP&gt;AI providers are organizations or individuals responsible for creating and supplying AI systems capable of generating synthetic content.&lt;SEP&gt;AI Providers are organizations that develop and manage high-risk AI systems subject to stringent regulations for compliance and quality management.&lt;SEP&gt;AI providers are organizations or individuals that develop and offer AI models, responsible for ensuring compliance with regulatory standards.&lt;SEP&gt;AI Providers are entities responsible for creating and implementing AI systems, especially those that are categorized as high-risk or non-high-risk.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1fb0ee5d200ca5b71eb6d9f53ad070ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c49e78c25e30ed3a2557915010f14f3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bb5eb0651d16c25633339b4b2cb2e46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c32bc5fa5cdfa35a393a42535dc4fdfb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c14e1756e1d8d71ac3ba07125f122da</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_17.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_133.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_112.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_165.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_53.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657067</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Provenance">
      <data key="d0">Provenance</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Provenance refers to the origin or source of information, which is crucial for verifying authenticity, particularly in AI-generated content.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3bb5eb0651d16c25633339b4b2cb2e46</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_133.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Downstream Provider">
      <data key="d0">Downstream Provider</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A downstream provider is an entity that utilizes an AI system to integrate models into applications or services, regardless of the source of the AI model.&lt;SEP&gt;The downstream provider is the entity deploying AI systems and is responsible for complying with regulatory obligations regarding AI content handling.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6570d0db42cf764ebb073d69da0137e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-decd01dd1bf25270eddf9979fe28678a</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_133.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657226</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Model">
      <data key="d0">AI Model</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">AI Model refers to a computational system designed to perform tasks that typically require human intelligence, enabling content generation and data processing.&lt;SEP&gt;An AI model is a mathematical construct that uses algorithms and data to perform tasks such as generating content, making predictions, or identifying patterns.&lt;SEP&gt;An AI model refers to a computational framework that is capable of performing various tasks and can be integrated into different AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6570d0db42cf764ebb073d69da0137e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8033b978339bfb2f89fde823ffa3f524&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-decd01dd1bf25270eddf9979fe28678a</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_133.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_99.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657226</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Assistive Function AI Systems">
      <data key="d0">Assistive Function AI Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Assistive Function AI Systems are AI models that primarily aid in tasks like standard editing without substantially altering the input data or semantics.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6570d0db42cf764ebb073d69da0137e3</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_133.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI-Generated Content">
      <data key="d0">AI-Generated Content</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">AI-Generated Content includes any content that is artificially created or manipulated, requiring detection and labeling to ensure authenticity and help the public distinguish it from human-created content.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-51cb0d95dff3b7f033b351a9352b26a0</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_135.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Codes of Practice">
      <data key="d0">Codes of Practice</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Codes of Practice are guidelines developed to ensure compliance with transparency obligations related to AI-generated content detection and labeling.&lt;SEP&gt;Codes of practice are guidelines established for providers of general-purpose AI models to ensure compliance and safety standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Codes of practice are guidelines that aim to ensure compliance with AI regulations and proper application of obligations outlined in the relevant articles.&lt;SEP&gt;Codes of practice are guidelines developed by the AI Office to oversee the obligations and practices of providers of general-purpose AI models, with a focus on safety and diversity.&lt;SEP&gt;Codes of Practice are guidelines that may be adopted by the Commission to govern the standards for detecting and labelling manipulated content.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c4dc0271c68856282748506ff58069b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-daa2a9a43bd7a2482ad876b406b9e9c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3034aa8ff1b6d41ac6e0b8ff655b76ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69b5f24963810305f2a7846d54923bf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51cb0d95dff3b7f033b351a9352b26a0</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_135.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_56.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_116.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_50.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747464578</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union Level">
      <data key="d0">Union Level</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">Union Level refers to a regulatory framework or collective governance structure involved in managing transparency obligations across member states.&lt;SEP&gt;Union level refers to the collective level of governance or regulatory framework within the Union, impacting AI practices and regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Union Level refers to the European Union's hierarchical governance structure, which aims to coordinate AI regulation across Member States.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-51cb0d95dff3b7f033b351a9352b26a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4dc0271c68856282748506ff58069b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e6a5cc59273abbe42c743808026477c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_56.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_148.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_135.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657832</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Detection Mechanisms">
      <data key="d0">Detection Mechanisms</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Detection Mechanisms are tools and processes aimed at identifying and verifying the authenticity of AI-generated content.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-51cb0d95dff3b7f033b351a9352b26a0</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_135.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Value Chain">
      <data key="d0">Value Chain</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Value Chain refers to the series of processes and activities involved in the development and distribution of AI systems, highlighting the roles of different operators.&lt;SEP&gt;Value Chain refers to the series of processes through which AI-generated content is disseminated and checked for authenticity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-51cb0d95dff3b7f033b351a9352b26a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-197c7357cf5fefe6ca4e08f847ff6a75</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_83.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_135.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657846</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Cooperation with Other Actors">
      <data key="d0">Cooperation with Other Actors</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Cooperation with Other Actors involves collaboration between different stakeholders to enhance content detection and verification processes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-51cb0d95dff3b7f033b351a9352b26a0</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_135.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 91">
      <data key="d0">Article 91</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 91 outlines the obligations of providers of general-purpose AI models under the specified regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 91 outlines the requirements for providers of general-purpose AI models regarding documentation and information requests from the Commission.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-23ab4f338bfa06297d4c996d7d54dc70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b16c22014fb75795531a9a187b8fc81</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_92.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_101.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 93">
      <data key="d0">Article 93</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 93 pertains to actions the Commission can take regarding compliance measures and the evaluation of AI models with systemic risk.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0b16c22014fb75795531a9a187b8fc81</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_101.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 92">
      <data key="d0">Article 92</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 92 involves evaluations that can lead to actions concerning systemic risks posed by AI models.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 92 refers to the evaluation process the Commission must conduct on general-purpose AI models that present systemic risks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1a0bef2c1dcc3d7b428c7611732f7ffc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b16c22014fb75795531a9a187b8fc81</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_93.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_101.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747464244</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 98">
      <data key="d0">Article 98</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 98 describes the procedural framework for adopting implementing acts related to the enforcement of the regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 98 refers to a specific article within a legal or regulatory framework that outlines certain implementing acts and examination procedures.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 98 outlines the examination procedure to be followed when the Commission adopts implementing acts regarding standardization.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4f41337092de45470ab838aff17309ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b16c22014fb75795531a9a187b8fc81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bec338e77f01240f23cac5480d2c8ae4</data>
