      <data key="d5">1747658160</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EUR 15 000 000">
      <data key="d0">EUR 15 000 000</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">EUR 15 000 000 is the specified amount that can be imposed as a fine on providers of general-purpose AI models for violations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0b16c22014fb75795531a9a187b8fc81</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_101.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Fines">
      <data key="d0">Fines</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Fines are financial penalties imposed for non-compliance with regulatory obligations, particularly regarding Artificial Intelligence models in this context.&lt;SEP&gt;Fines are financial penalties imposed to deter illegal or undesirable behavior, required to be effective, proportionate, and dissuasive according to legal standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Fines refer to penalties imposed on organizations or individuals for violating data protection regulations, contributing to the Union's budget.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-de6a0d59bb86cca6093fbb52cf156b4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae3ab8a3b5c5d0c61e8b99fa718913b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-828a2d9070cae319b764e3b609bc9b81</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_101.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_100.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_169.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657789</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 98(2)">
      <data key="d0">Article 98(2)</data>
      <data key="d1">legal_article</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 98(2) refers to a specific legal provision within European Union law that governs the examination procedure for various implementing acts. This article outlines the necessary procedures that the Commission must follow for a range of regulatory matters, including the compliance of notified bodies and the approval of codes of practice within the Union. Additionally, Article 98(2) emphasizes the examination processes relative to the regulations surrounding artificial intelligence, particularly concerning high-risk AI systems and obligations related to content regulation. Furthermore, it details the examination procedure for the adoption of decisions associated with fines, ensuring a comprehensive regulatory framework. Overall, Article 98(2) serves as a crucial component in the regulatory landscape of the European Union, establishing clear protocols for implementing acts across multiple domains.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-de6a0d59bb86cca6093fbb52cf156b4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff61ec794793cf787d4a0473487a06f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3034aa8ff1b6d41ac6e0b8ff655b76ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6de18717bcb0167956be85a15dd210f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-daa2a9a43bd7a2482ad876b406b9e9c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97182f6b8815d40f51faf3e8eaeb7c7d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_60.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_37.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_101.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_50.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_56.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657540</data>
    </node>
    <node id="post-remote biometric identification systems">
      <data key="d0">post-remote biometric identification systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Post-remote biometric identification systems are high-risk AI systems that are used to identify or track individuals, particularly in law enforcement and security contexts.&lt;SEP&gt;Post-remote biometric identification systems are technologies that analyze and recognize individual characteristics from recorded video footage, raising privacy and ethical concerns.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-de40ca48bf7dafc1db86f4d8a18d2bba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4882abf1dd869d3dff00b8d88ee946a8</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_95.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657974</data>
    </node>
    <node id="safeguards">
      <data key="d0">safeguards</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Safeguards refer to protective measures established within legal frameworks to mitigate the risks associated with the use of sensitive technologies like biometric identification systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-de40ca48bf7dafc1db86f4d8a18d2bba</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_95.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="surveillance">
      <data key="d0">surveillance</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Surveillance refers to close observation, especially of a suspected individual or group, which can raise concerns about privacy and civil liberties when applied indiscriminately.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-de40ca48bf7dafc1db86f4d8a18d2bba</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_95.json</data>
    </node>
