      <data key="d0">Denmark</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">Denmark is a country in Northern Europe that operates under specific legal protocols regarding police and judicial cooperation with the EU.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-500c97cae442a182ecf77fd6f39000b4</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_41.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Protocol No 22">
      <data key="d0">Protocol No 22</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Protocol No 22 is a legal framework that outlines specific conditions applicable to Denmark within the EU treaties, particularly regarding biometric and AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-500c97cae442a182ecf77fd6f39000b4</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_41.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TEU">
      <data key="d0">TEU</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Treaty on European Union (TEU) defines the foundational principles of the European Union, including governance related to criminal justice and police cooperation.&lt;SEP&gt;The Treaty on European Union (TEU) establishes the foundational legal framework for the European Union.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-76a2f07f347fedfe788b6636feb212d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-500c97cae442a182ecf77fd6f39000b4</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_41.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_40.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747464907</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TFEU">
      <data key="d0">TFEU</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The TFEU refers to the Treaty on the Functioning of the European Union, which governs the legal framework and regulations within the EU.&lt;SEP&gt;The Treaty on the Functioning of the European Union (TFEU) governs the functioning of the EU, providing legal bases for various cooperative measures among member states.&lt;SEP&gt;The Treaty on the Functioning of the European Union (TFEU) provides detailed governance and operational structures for the EU.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-76a2f07f347fedfe788b6636feb212d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-500c97cae442a182ecf77fd6f39000b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae3ab8a3b5c5d0c61e8b99fa718913b0</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_41.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_40.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_169.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747464907</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 5(1)">
      <data key="d0">Article 5(1)</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 5(1) is a provision that discusses the application of biometric categorization systems in law enforcement and judicial activities.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 5(1) is a provision within the TEU and TFEU that outlines specific rules regarding the processing of personal data and the use of biometric systems by Member States in judicial and police cooperation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-76a2f07f347fedfe788b6636feb212d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-500c97cae442a182ecf77fd6f39000b4</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_41.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_40.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747464907</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Chapter 4">
      <data key="d0">Chapter 4</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Chapter 4 of Title V of Part Three of the TFEU addresses specific legal frameworks regarding police cooperation among EU Member States.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-500c97cae442a182ecf77fd6f39000b4</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_41.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Chapter 5">
      <data key="d0">Chapter 5</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Chapter 5 of Title V of Part Three of the TFEU deals with judicial cooperation in criminal matters among Member States of the EU.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-500c97cae442a182ecf77fd6f39000b4</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_41.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Post Market Monitoring">
      <data key="d0">Post Market Monitoring</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Post market monitoring involves ongoing oversight of AI systems after their deployment to ensure that they operate within the regulatory framework and comply with safety practices.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6b754e2170dea6f93253ec4fd1fa88d5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_71.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Records">
      <data key="d0">Records</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Records are detailed accounts of the characteristics, capabilities, and performance of high-risk AI systems that support compliance and monitoring.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6b754e2170dea6f93253ec4fd1fa88d5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_71.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Performance Evaluation">
      <data key="d0">Performance Evaluation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Performance evaluation involves assessing the effectiveness and compliance of AI systems against established standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6b754e2170dea6f93253ec4fd1fa88d5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_71.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Risk-Management System">
      <data key="d0">Risk-Management System</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A structured process aimed at identifying and mitigating risks associated with high-risk AI systems, covering health, safety, and fundamental rights throughout their lifecycle.&lt;SEP&gt;Risk-management systems are protocols designed to identify, assess, and mitigate risks associated with high-risk AI systems throughout their lifecycle.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7b5e606b14946a1b388f008868e8e155&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b754e2170dea6f93253ec4fd1fa88d5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_65.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_71.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747464790</data>
    </node>
    <node id="providers of the general-purpose AI model">
      <data key="d0">providers of the general-purpose AI model</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Providers of general-purpose AI models are entities that develop, manage, or supply AI systems designed for a wide range of applications and must comply with the Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 to ensure their models meet established safety and performance criteria.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8affbc363cca00e716c4494cb81a558a</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_94.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 16">
      <data key="d0">Article 16</data>
      <data key="d1">document</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 16 outlines distributor obligations concerning the verification and compliance of high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 16 outlines obligations for providers which are relevant for compliance under the Regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 16 specifies obligations of providers in relation to the regulation's enforcement and compliance requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 16 outlines the specific obligations that high-risk AI system providers must fulfill under this Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e7365f713d09e74d49090cb78cb3e19b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e7b8a0eb1cb8c27dfd822da15429870&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4329be6d4972c392a3a71593d402998&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73fd7e801c2d8d41361f6b16b45c6ed0</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_24.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_25.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657382</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 22">
      <data key="d0">Article 22</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 22 details the obligations of authorized representatives within the context of the regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 22 refers to obligations of authorized representatives that need to be adhered to by undertakings.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 22 refers to a provision of Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012, detailing the committee's responsibilities when drafting implementing acts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4f41337092de45470ab838aff17309ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7365f713d09e74d49090cb78cb3e19b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e7b8a0eb1cb8c27dfd822da15429870</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_41.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747658160</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 23">
      <data key="d0">Article 23</data>
      <data key="d1">document</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 23 outlines the obligations of importers regarding compliance with specific regulatory standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 23 specifies obligations of importers that are of regulatory importance.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 23 sets additional obligations for distributors regarding high-risk AI systems, particularly in documenting and reporting compliance status.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e7365f713d09e74d49090cb78cb3e19b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e7b8a0eb1cb8c27dfd822da15429870&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73fd7e801c2d8d41361f6b16b45c6ed0</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_24.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657382</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 24">
      <data key="d0">Article 24</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 24 delineates obligations of distributors within the regulatory framework.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 24 describes the obligations imposed on distributors under the regulation's framework.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e7b8a0eb1cb8c27dfd822da15429870&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7365f713d09e74d49090cb78cb3e19b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 26">
      <data key="d0">Article 26</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 26 addresses obligations of deployers related to the use of AI technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 26 sets out obligations for deployers in relation to regulatory compliance and enforcement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e7b8a0eb1cb8c27dfd822da15429870&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7365f713d09e74d49090cb78cb3e19b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 33">
      <data key="d0">Article 33</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 33 comprises further details regarding obligations tied to notified bodies as well.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 33 consists of provisions that outline additional obligations for notified bodies under the regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e7b8a0eb1cb8c27dfd822da15429870&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7365f713d09e74d49090cb78cb3e19b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 34">
      <data key="d0">Article 34</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 34 continues the stipulations related to the roles of notified bodies in regulatory compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 34 specifies further obligations concerning notified bodies in regulatory compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e7b8a0eb1cb8c27dfd822da15429870&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7365f713d09e74d49090cb78cb3e19b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="penalties">
      <data key="d0">penalties</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Penalties refer to the sanctions imposed for non-compliance with the Regulation, including administrative fines and other measures.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e7365f713d09e74d49090cb78cb3e19b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="operators">
      <data key="d0">operators</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Operators are entities that are subject to the enforcement measures and penalties specified in the Regulation for non-compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;Operators are individuals or organizations that manage or run AI systems and are responsible for compliance with regulations and obligations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e7365f713d09e74d49090cb78cb3e19b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0bd7056742f766183c11176d91fb1e8</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_26.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657306</data>
    </node>
    <node id="enforcement measures">
      <data key="d0">enforcement measures</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Enforcement measures are the actions taken to ensure compliance with the Regulation, including warnings and fines.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e7365f713d09e74d49090cb78cb3e19b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="administrative fines">
      <data key="d0">administrative fines</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Administrative fines are monetary penalties imposed for various levels of non-compliance with the Regulation, with specific amounts outlined.&lt;SEP&gt;Administrative fines are penalties imposed for violations of regulations or laws, particularly concerning public authorities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8c31e49eb2274702ec6ced9550f1ca86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7365f713d09e74d49090cb78cb3e19b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="total worldwide annual turnover">
      <data key="d0">total worldwide annual turnover</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Total worldwide annual turnover refers to the overall revenue generated by an undertaking, which is considered when calculating penalties.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e7365f713d09e74d49090cb78cb3e19b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="non-monetary measures">
      <data key="d0">non-monetary measures</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Non-monetary measures refer to penalties that do not involve monetary fines, such as warnings or other corrective actions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e7365f713d09e74d49090cb78cb3e19b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Articles 5">
      <data key="d0">Articles 5</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Articles 5 refer to specific regulatory provisions that outline obligations and consequences for various operators under the regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e7b8a0eb1cb8c27dfd822da15429870</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Financial Year">
      <data key="d0">Financial Year</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Financial Year refers to the annual accounting period used to assess the total worldwide annual turnover of organizations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e7b8a0eb1cb8c27dfd822da15429870</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Administrative Fine">
      <data key="d0">Administrative Fine</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Administrative fines are penalties imposed for infractions, considering various aspects such as the nature and gravity of the infringement, and the impact on affected persons.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-599d61ad7be34e2603c3fef13f2ff8dd</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Infringement">
      <data key="d0">Infringement</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An infringement refers to a violation of laws or regulations that the operator needs to address.&lt;SEP&gt;Infringements refer to violations of regulations or laws that can lead to penalties such as administrative fines, often determined by relevant authorities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8c31e49eb2274702ec6ced9550f1ca86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-599d61ad7be34e2603c3fef13f2ff8dd</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Operator">
      <data key="d0">Operator</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">An operator encompasses various roles including provider, importer, and distributor, responsible for ensuring the proper use and deployment of AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;An operator encompasses various roles including providers, manufacturers, deployers, representatives, importers, or distributors involved with AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;An operator refers to any individual or entity that manages or runs an AI system within a given legal framework, especially within the Union or third countries.&lt;SEP&gt;Operator refers to any organization or entity that may commit infringements leading to the imposition of administrative fines.&lt;SEP&gt;The Operator is responsible for ensuring compliance with regulations and mitigating the effects of any legal infringements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-599d61ad7be34e2603c3fef13f2ff8dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e78bce1eaa5df9c186492b5e1482218&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dbd41da6ea2a77fff5beb18c8e7c896&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7d62750f1113d24ac155fcd2b2ef02c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c31e49eb2274702ec6ced9550f1ca86</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_22.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657159</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Affected Persons">
      <data key="d0">Affected Persons</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Affected Persons are individuals who are located in the Union and may be impacted by AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Affected persons are individuals or groups that experience negative consequences as a result of infringements committed by operators.&lt;SEP&gt;Affected persons are individuals whose rights and interests may be adversely affected by decisions made based on high-risk AI systems and should have the right to obtain explanations regarding such decisions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-727225adfedcad573a12c2ed92e8ee1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13991bdab077b3114e8913f89a1371e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-599d61ad7be34e2603c3fef13f2ff8dd</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_2.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_171.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747464649</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Competent National Courts">
      <data key="d0">Competent National Courts</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Competent national courts are judicial bodies in Member States responsible for adjudicating disputes related to the imposition of administrative fines.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-599d61ad7be34e2603c3fef13f2ff8dd</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Procedural Safeguards">
      <data key="d0">Procedural Safeguards</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Procedural safeguards refer to the legal protections and due process required during the imposition of administrative fines to ensure fair treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-599d61ad7be34e2603c3fef13f2ff8dd</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Annual Reports">
      <data key="d0">Annual Reports</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Annual Reports are comprehensive documents produced by the National Competent Authorities, detailing various initiatives and regulatory frameworks related to artificial intelligence and biometric identification systems. They encompass insights and outcomes from AI regulatory sandbox initiatives, which are experimental environments for testing AI technologies under regulatory oversight. These reports are intended for public availability, ensuring transparency about the operations and results of AI regulatory sandboxes.

Furthermore, Annual Reports also cover the use of biometric identification systems in public spaces, particularly for law enforcement purposes. They include documentation submitted by Member States to The Commission that outlines the administrative fines issued and associated litigation throughout the year.

Additionally, Annual Reports require deployers of high-risk AI systems to submit detailed accounts of their systems' usage, compliance with regulations, and the impact of these technologies while ensuring adherence to data protection laws. This multifaceted approach ensures that both AI technologies and biometric identification systems are scrutinized and regulated adequately, promoting accountability and safety in their deployment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-599d61ad7be34e2603c3fef13f2ff8dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-911571ee28a1070a8fcc503dd5d91e14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4882abf1dd869d3dff00b8d88ee946a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6adb64ff4e7b459fa1df815eac98b096&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85bb41c1db2d2e1883172e505d5f7b71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4988a00689afb1245e0f0ce4ceef5921&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50be48c46c67191e901c756873069fcb</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_5.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_57.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657974</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Judicial Remedies">
      <data key="d0">Judicial Remedies</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Judicial remedies are legal solutions available to individuals or entities seeking redress after the imposition of administrative fines.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-599d61ad7be34e2603c3fef13f2ff8dd</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="national competent authorities">
      <data key="d0">national competent authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">National competent authorities are agencies or organizations responsible for enforcing laws and regulations in their respective Member States.&lt;SEP&gt;National competent authorities are regulatory bodies responsible for ensuring that high-risk AI systems comply with established standards and requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;National competent authorities are designated bodies within member states responsible for enforcing compliance with EU regulations and legislation.&lt;SEP&gt;National competent authorities are organizations within member states responsible for enforcing laws and regulations, especially in the context of AI systems and public security.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fdf8a675497acfbeb420b95621b7cb31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75ec68339f2da8ef06976767a0d5b494&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c31e49eb2274702ec6ced9550f1ca86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36cb0fd5abf1b169a8aa13021f58c7b2</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_11.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_78.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747464109</data>
    </node>
    <node id="judicial remedies">
      <data key="d0">judicial remedies</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Judicial remedies refer to legal means by which a court can enforce a right, impose penalties, or provide relief for violations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8c31e49eb2274702ec6ced9550f1ca86</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Judicial Proceedings">
      <data key="d0">Judicial Proceedings</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Judicial proceedings refer to the legal processes that result from administrative fines or infringements reported by Member States to the Commission.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8c31e49eb2274702ec6ced9550f1ca86</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Operational">
      <data key="d0">Operational</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-599d61ad7be34e2603c3fef13f2ff8dd</data>
      <data key="d2">Competent national courts adjudicate disputes arising from the imposition of administrative fines by market surveillance authorities.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive (EU) 2019/790">
      <data key="d0">Directive (EU) 2019/790</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive (EU) 2019/790 is a European Union legal framework regarding copyright and related rights that impacts the obligations of AI model providers.&lt;SEP&gt;Directive (EU) 2019/790 is a legal framework established by the European Union concerning copyright and related rights, particularly as they pertain to digital content.&lt;SEP&gt;Directive (EU) 2019/790 is a regulation that introduces exceptions and limitations for text and data mining, impacting copyright protected content.&lt;SEP&gt;Directive (EU) 2019/790 is a legislative document that addresses copyright and related rights in the Digital Single Market, influencing regulations regarding AI model transparency and usage.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5429fed5961ecea1e5eed049e922476f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-212b902a4529db42951674775ac3ec73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1ae06c8c76fc5976313d75e4ffabdfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4dc89de2edca5d2bfe0d5e9e7c99665b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_53.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_105.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_106.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_104.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747464756</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European harmonised standards">
      <data key="d0">European harmonised standards</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">European harmonised standards refer to established regulations providing guidelines for compliance, particularly in technology fields.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4dc89de2edca5d2bfe0d5e9e7c99665b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_53.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Providers of general-purpose AI models">
      <data key="d0">Providers of general-purpose AI models</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Providers of general-purpose AI models are entities that develop and maintain AI technologies, required to comply with specific regulations regarding documentation and transparency.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4dc89de2edca5d2bfe0d5e9e7c99665b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_53.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Annex XI">
      <data key="d0">Annex XI</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Annex XI contains specific points necessary for compliance assessment, particularly regarding measurement and calculation methodologies.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex XI is a regulatory appendix that outlines specific obligations related to the compliance of AI providers and their models.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex XI outlines the minimum information that must be included in the technical documentation of general-purpose AI models, as specified in the regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex XI contains specific technical requirements and documentation standards that AI model providers must meet for compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c49e78c25e30ed3a2557915010f14f3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5abff9e94aff7675c473268fd21bf551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4dc89de2edca5d2bfe0d5e9e7c99665b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-873c3732f26f3ace86c77cfec67991ee</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_53.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_54.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Annex XII">
      <data key="d0">Annex XII</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Annex XII is a regulatory appendix that outlines additional standards and obligations that AI providers must adhere to.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex XII likely contains additional requirements or amendments related to compliance and assessment processes that can evolve with technology.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex XII lists the essential elements that need to be disclosed by AI model providers for compliance and understanding of the model's capabilities and limitations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c49e78c25e30ed3a2557915010f14f3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5abff9e94aff7675c473268fd21bf551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4dc89de2edca5d2bfe0d5e9e7c99665b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_53.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union and national law">
      <data key="d0">Union and national law</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Union and national law refers to legal frameworks governing the activities of AI providers, especially in terms of intellectual property and confidential information.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4dc89de2edca5d2bfe0d5e9e7c99665b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_53.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="state-of-the-art technologies">
      <data key="d0">state-of-the-art technologies</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">State-of-the-art technologies are advanced methods or tools that providers must use to ensure compliance with copyright and intellectual property regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4dc89de2edca5d2bfe0d5e9e7c99665b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_53.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Downstream Providers">
      <data key="d0">Downstream Providers</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Downstream Providers are individuals or organizations that utilize or implement general-purpose AI models and have rights to complain about potential infringements of regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Downstream providers utilize general-purpose AI models to create products and systems that require a deep understanding of these models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-11bdaa862215570a86eed137e3092ea6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18d33fd192f06f727ac6bb21becbaa57</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_89.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_101.json</data>
