    </node>
    <node id="This Regulation">
      <data key="d0">This Regulation</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">This Regulation refers to the set of rules governing the use, integration, and documentation of general-purpose AI models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-11bdaa862215570a86eed137e3092ea6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_101.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Transparency Measures">
      <data key="d0">Transparency Measures</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Transparency measures are protocols and practices aimed at ensuring that information regarding AI models and their functionality is accessible and clear to all stakeholders involved.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-11bdaa862215570a86eed137e3092ea6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_101.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulations">
      <data key="d0">Regulations</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulations encompass the legal frameworks and guidelines that govern the development and use of AI technologies, ensuring ethical and responsible practices.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-11bdaa862215570a86eed137e3092ea6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_101.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Third Parties">
      <data key="d0">Third Parties</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Third parties refer to entities that provide tools, services, processes, or AI components to the public, particularly focusing on free and open-source resources.&lt;SEP&gt;Third parties refer to entities that supply tools, services, components, or processes used in conjunction with high-risk AI systems to enhance functionality or compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8143bb5053cad47b9eaf4c05c9556429&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-778cb9e68fcb25e3f810e3cea927f7b2</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_90.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_89.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657588</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Free and Open-Source Licence">
      <data key="d0">Free and Open-Source Licence</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A free and open-source licence allows users to freely access, use, modify, and redistribute software and data, provided that original creators are credited.&lt;SEP&gt;The free and open-source license allows third parties to make their tools and services available without imposing certain compliance requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-769497b509433ed0e4746ff50bbdec69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-778cb9e68fcb25e3f810e3cea927f7b2</data>
