      <data key="d0">Model Cards</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Model cards are documentation practices recommended for AI technologies to promote transparency and information sharing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-778cb9e68fcb25e3f810e3cea927f7b2</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_89.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Sheets">
      <data key="d0">Data Sheets</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Data sheets are documents that provide essential information about data used in AI systems, promoting better understanding and trust.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-778cb9e68fcb25e3f810e3cea927f7b2</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_89.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Documentation Practices">
      <data key="d0">Documentation Practices</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Documentation practices include methodologies like model cards and data sheets that developers should adopt to enhance transparency and information sharing in AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-778cb9e68fcb25e3f810e3cea927f7b2</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_89.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Trustworthy AI Systems">
      <data key="d0">Trustworthy AI Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Trustworthy AI systems are those designed with ethical guidelines and practices, ensuring accountability, transparency, and reliability in their applications in society.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-778cb9e68fcb25e3f810e3cea927f7b2</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_89.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Providers of AI Systems">
      <data key="d0">Providers of AI Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Providers of AI Systems are entities or individuals responsible for developing and offering AI solutions, which require adherence to regulatory standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Providers of AI Systems refer to organizations or individuals that create, implement, or manage artificial intelligence technologies and systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Providers of AI systems are entities or companies that develop and distribute AI technologies, needing to ensure compliance with regulations regarding safety and risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Providers of AI systems are organizations or entities responsible for creating and deploying artificial intelligence technologies, subject to specific obligations under the regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Providers of AI systems develop and ensure that these systems comply with legal and ethical standards, particularly in interactions with natural persons.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fa2298fd83910d35175065de74977bd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40f3761e589fb7702938fd4fbbecfdcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7e1bc352c7c8d3a7ba58b9b1a4f9f37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d08b537f9a5bb2b4f4bbdf442ba39bdd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bccefc944ad0794c75bc69b977c88a1</data>
