    </node>
    <node id="notified body">
      <data key="d0">notified body</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A notified body is an authorized organization designated to assess the compliance of products and systems with regulatory standards.&lt;SEP&gt;A notified body refers to an organization designated to assess the compliance of high-risk AI systems and issue certificates.&lt;SEP&gt;The notified body is an entity involved in assessing and ensuring compliance with regulations, especially regarding terminations and mandates.&lt;SEP&gt;Notified bodies are organizations designated to assess and monitor compliance concerning high-risk AI systems and their associated certifications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8af2de29a8b78dd2b512b6eb64d912a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c361162e59f587f531364714bb3e3c4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cdf6e3e080867f88ec52fa9fabbeafd6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b341fa074527a308a2434a3c68244d02</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_36.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_22.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657339</data>
    </node>
    <node id="competent authority">
      <data key="d0">competent authority</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Competent authorities are regulatory agencies tasked with overseeing the implementation of regulations surrounding high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8af2de29a8b78dd2b512b6eb64d912a6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_22.json</data>
    </node>
