      <data key="d0">Regulation Section 2</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation Section 2 outlines the specific requirements that high-risk AI systems must adhere to for compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8af2de29a8b78dd2b512b6eb64d912a6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_22.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="registration obligations">
      <data key="d0">registration obligations</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Registration obligations refer to the requirements set forth in the Regulation regarding the documentation and verification of high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8af2de29a8b78dd2b512b6eb64d912a6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_22.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="market surveillance authority">
      <data key="d0">market surveillance authority</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Market surveillance authorities are entities responsible for monitoring compliance with laws and regulations concerning products and services in the market.&lt;SEP&gt;Market surveillance authorities are organizations responsible for overseeing compliance with market regulations and handling complaints.&lt;SEP&gt;The market surveillance authority is a national regulatory body tasked with overseeing compliance with market regulations, particularly in accordance with Regulation (EU) 2019/1020. Its primary responsibilities include ensuring that entities, such as providers, adhere to legal obligations and protecting consumer rights. Additionally, the authority is specifically charged with monitoring compliance related to the use of various technologies, including biometric identification systems, in public spaces. Furthermore, it plays a key role in overseeing the compliance of high-risk AI systems with applicable legal requirements. The market surveillance authority also monitors regulations concerning AI systems and is responsible for receiving notifications of assessments from their deployers, ensuring that all market actors conform to established standards and regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Market surveillance authorities are regulatory bodies responsible for monitoring products in the market to ensure compliance with safety and other regulatory standards.&lt;SEP&gt;The market surveillance authority is responsible for ensuring that products and services comply with regulations and standards to protect citizens.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9c27775e23d04f7dd6b8ec477a62efd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27c28ab4482e4bec149657c656192c46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4c7e75432b8ffa8e0b96687dc4dd380&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77a0a99b47c288a96d7474c796efb766&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-610573a7c194ad780ed97782200a740c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78dcdae0f5d22df28405d8ae03e038d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb040a8b4e6e3fa6f26776f560b6591c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4882abf1dd869d3dff00b8d88ee946a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43e82a7af456b2ae813a7217f92c2008&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c361162e59f587f531364714bb3e3c4c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_22.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_170.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_27.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_46.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_5.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_85.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_80.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747658093</data>
    </node>
    <node id="mandate">
      <data key="d0">mandate</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A mandate refers to the authorization or directive given to a provider, which outlines their responsibilities and obligations under the regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c361162e59f587f531364714bb3e3c4c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_22.json</data>
    </node>
