    <node id="Union harmonisation legislation">
      <data key="d0">Union harmonisation legislation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Union harmonisation legislation encompasses laws that ensure products meet consistent standards across Member States.&lt;SEP&gt;Union harmonisation legislation refers to a set of regulatory requirements designed to ensure products meet safety and performance standards across member states.&lt;SEP&gt;Union harmonisation legislation refers to a set of legal standards within the European Union that ensure the uniformity of technical regulations for products, including high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Union harmonisation legislation sets the regulatory framework within which high-risk AI systems must comply, particularly when related to product safety.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1952e0d35566561db978f8ee1ebdbd3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c9021d6cb53dceeddd1e648d3e37fbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36cb0fd5abf1b169a8aa13021f58c7b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4c7e75432b8ffa8e0b96687dc4dd380</data>
