    </node>
    <node id="implementing acts">
      <data key="d0">implementing acts</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Implementing acts are legal provisions established by the Commission that outline the procedures and criteria for evaluating general-purpose AI models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-075ecb5835777e6044264a23ca0cb20a</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_92.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="law">
      <data key="d0">law</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Law refers to the system of rules which a particular country or community recognizes as regulating the actions of its members.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-075ecb5835777e6044264a23ca0cb20a</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_92.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="internal testing">
      <data key="d0">internal testing</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Internal testing refers to the examination processes and evaluations conducted by providers on their AI models to ensure safety and effectiveness before public access.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-075ecb5835777e6044264a23ca0cb20a</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_92.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="General-Purpose AI Systems">
      <data key="d0">General-Purpose AI Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">General-purpose AI systems are versatile AI technologies that can operate independently or as parts of more complex, high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a67563c32c3414ab14ce22666bed23dc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_85.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="national public authorities">
      <data key="d0">national public authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">National public authorities are governmental bodies responsible for maintaining public order and safety, ensuring laws and regulations are followed.&lt;SEP&gt;National public authorities are governmental bodies responsible for supervising the application of Union law and protecting fundamental rights within their respective countries.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2315cd7abb88dee440f081de5430a32f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8512760339eb776d946a91a28089b34</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_77.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_157.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747464338</data>
    </node>
    <node id="fundamental rights">
      <data key="d0">fundamental rights</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Fundamental rights are basic human rights and freedoms that are intended to be protected by law, including equality and data protection.&lt;SEP&gt;Fundamental rights are basic human rights that should be protected during processes such as development, testing, and experimentation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2315cd7abb88dee440f081de5430a32f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62e8b28075fdfa33850ed4b5a4d9a52f</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_157.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_140.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="National Public Authorities">
      <data key="d0">National Public Authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">National Public Authorities are bodies that receive notifications of serious incidents from market surveillance authorities and play a role in the regulatory framework.&lt;SEP&gt;National Public Authorities are government bodies that supervise and enforce compliance with Union laws pertaining to fundamental rights and high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;National Public Authorities are government entities responsible for enforcing and supervising the application of regulations, including those relating to AI and fundamental rights.&lt;SEP&gt;National Public Authorities are governmental bodies within Member States responsible for enforcing regulations and cooperating with market surveillance authorities on public safety matters.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0dc307b8b7cb1f0e39aa9b4b1839c408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2315cd7abb88dee440f081de5430a32f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cb2802f1b508b813d06e58ae27a1f77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e853663a3f2d06a9cfea8582e10f089</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_77.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_73.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_79.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_157.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747464360</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Quality Management System Documentation">
      <data key="d0">Quality Management System Documentation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Quality Management System Documentation refers to the records and procedures that organizations must maintain to ensure quality control and compliance with regulations regarding AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-46418d497e0c090818a97380d173293d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_18.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Europol">
      <data key="d0">Europol</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Europol is a European Union agency for law enforcement cooperation, facilitating collaboration among EU member states' law enforcement agencies.&lt;SEP&gt;Europol is the European Union's law enforcement agency that assists member states in combating serious international crime and terrorism.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3e78bce1eaa5df9c186492b5e1482218&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a90a47461f525bba18d74c42ea04f88</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_22.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="International Organizations">
      <data key="d0">International Organizations</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">International Organizations are entities that operate across borders, often involved in cooperation with Union Member States concerning AI regulations and law enforcement.&lt;SEP&gt;International organizations are entities established by treaties between countries, which may engage with the Union under cooperation agreements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3e78bce1eaa5df9c186492b5e1482218&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3105f8ed20ed5608a4571fe7b1d8f942</data>
