    </node>
    <node id="Council Framework Decision 2002/584/JHA">
      <data key="d0">Council Framework Decision 2002/584/JHA</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The Council Framework Decision 2002/584/JHA establishes procedures for the European arrest warrant and cooperation between Member States regarding the surrender of suspects.&lt;SEP&gt;The Council Framework Decision 2002/584/JHA pertains to the European arrest warrant and surrender procedures between Member States.&lt;SEP&gt;The Council Framework Decision 2002/584/JHA refers to a specific legal framework in the EU regarding criminal offenses and their coordination among member states.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a23e03a78af2035b69e69bd4fc65a435&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d91755cda6acde2b40257e6d4cef1695&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6badc71855b10bbd17a31c7dfef0c442</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_33.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Missing Persons">
      <data key="d0">Missing Persons</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Missing Persons refers to individuals whose whereabouts are unknown, and search efforts may involve law enforcement using advanced identification systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d91755cda6acde2b40257e6d4cef1695</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_33.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Terrorist Attack Threats">
      <data key="d0">Terrorist Attack Threats</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Terrorist Attack Threats refer to imminent dangers posed by extremist activities that significantly endanger public safety and may require immediate law enforcement response.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d91755cda6acde2b40257e6d4cef1695</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_33.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Custodial Sentence">
      <data key="d0">Custodial Sentence</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Custodial Sentence is a legal punishment involving detention or imprisonment of an individual for a duration determined by law, as mentioned in the context of criminal offenses.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d91755cda6acde2b40257e6d4cef1695</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_33.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="biometric identification">
      <data key="d0">biometric identification</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Biometric identification involves technologies and methods used to recognize individuals based on their physiological characteristics, such as fingerprints and facial recognition.&lt;SEP&gt;Biometric identification is the automated recognition of human features to establish identity by comparing individual biometric data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a23e03a78af2035b69e69bd4fc65a435&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43e82a7af456b2ae813a7217f92c2008</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_33.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657184</data>
    </node>
    <node id="criminal offences">
      <data key="d0">criminal offences</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Criminal offences are violations of law that can lead to legal prosecution and penalties, impacting societal order and security.&lt;SEP&gt;Criminal offences refer to actions that are punishable by law, which may require identification of suspects and perpetrators.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a23e03a78af2035b69e69bd4fc65a435&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfc036b3a79fdcd1eb36c0af6aafbb4d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_33.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657205</data>
    </node>
    <node id="critical infrastructure">
      <data key="d0">critical infrastructure</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Critical infrastructure consists of essential services, facilities, and systems that are vital for the security and economy of a state, where disruption may lead to significant harm.&lt;SEP&gt;Critical infrastructure includes essential services, systems, and assets that are fundamental to the functioning of society, as defined in EU regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3266d68b5262e6852cabbe36178dec96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a23e03a78af2035b69e69bd4fc65a435</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_33.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657226</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive 2008/114/EC">
      <data key="d0">Directive 2008/114/EC</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive 2008/114/EC pertains to the identification and designation of European critical infrastructures and the assessment of need for improved protection.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a23e03a78af2035b69e69bd4fc65a435</data>
