    <node id="Real-Time Biometric Identification System">
      <data key="d0">Real-Time Biometric Identification System</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A Real-Time Biometric Identification System refers to technology that identifies individuals using biometric data in real time, often for law enforcement purposes.&lt;SEP&gt;The Real-Time Biometric Identification System refers to technological systems used for identifying individuals based on biometric data in real-time.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2187eb3476528ac7c75b571eb3844f0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc0db03f57b007cfc458657e88e273ae</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_36.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_35.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747464271</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Model">
      <data key="d0">Model</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A model refers to a mathematical representation or simulation designed to predict or analyze behaviors based on input parameters.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e93dbcfb179aa98bf5518ab208d544fc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_98.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Parameters">
      <data key="d0">Parameters</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Parameters are variables or factors that are integral in defining the characteristics and performance of a model.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e93dbcfb179aa98bf5518ab208d544fc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_98.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Self-Supervision">
      <data key="d0">Self-Supervision</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Self-supervision is a training method where a model generates labels from the input data itself, enabling learning without human annotations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e93dbcfb179aa98bf5518ab208d544fc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_98.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data">
      <data key="d0">Data</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Data constitutes the information processed or produced by AI systems, which can include input data, training data, and operational data.&lt;SEP&gt;Data represents the collection of facts, statistics, or information analyzed or processed by the model to achieve significant generality.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7ef570a9dfbda3c55d0d5bcc36fd77c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e93dbcfb179aa98bf5518ab208d544fc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_98.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_103.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657366</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EU Regulation">
      <data key="d0">EU Regulation</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">EU Regulation refers to legislative measures enacted by the European Union, which may include guidelines for various sectors and compliance standards.&lt;SEP&gt;EU Regulation refers to the legislative acts that are binding across all Member States of the European Union and require member compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3fa5fe9ac042448be58de6c82bb33ea4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e4f07f79ad3c90c82b86c0a02d0fae9</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_175.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_63.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI regulatory sandbox">
      <data key="d0">AI regulatory sandbox</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">An AI regulatory sandbox is a controlled framework established to facilitate the testing and validation of AI systems under regulatory supervision.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI regulatory sandbox is a controlled environment allowing for the development, testing, and regulation of AI systems while safeguarding public interest.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cfc036b3a79fdcd1eb36c0af6aafbb4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a46250ea72037444e96653239f2893b2</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_140.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657205</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Significant Risks">
      <data key="d0">Significant Risks</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Significant risks refer to potential threats to safety, health, and fundamental rights that need to be identified and mitigated during the development and testing of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a46250ea72037444e96653239f2893b2</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_140.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="sandbox">
      <data key="d0">sandbox</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A sandbox in this context refers to a controlled environment where development, testing, and experimentation can occur while managing risks to safety, health, and fundamental rights.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-62e8b28075fdfa33850ed4b5a4d9a52f</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_140.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="significant risks">
      <data key="d0">significant risks</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Significant risks refer to potential dangers that may affect safety, health, and fundamental rights during development and testing processes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-62e8b28075fdfa33850ed4b5a4d9a52f</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_140.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="safety">
      <data key="d0">safety</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Safety encompasses the measures and precautions taken to prevent accidents and ensure the well-being of individuals involved in the development and testing phases.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-62e8b28075fdfa33850ed4b5a4d9a52f</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_140.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="health">
      <data key="d0">health</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Health refers to the overall physical and mental well-being of individuals, particularly in the context of activities that could pose risks during development and testing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-62e8b28075fdfa33850ed4b5a4d9a52f</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_140.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Commission Work Programme 2021">
      <data key="d0">Commission Work Programme 2021</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Commission Work Programme 2021 outlines strategic initiatives and priorities related to work-related contractual relationships, including the implications of AI systems on employment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6fa05c618cc92c392c091a0299038b25</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_57.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Women">
      <data key="d0">Women</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Women are identified as one of the groups particularly vulnerable to discrimination during recruitment and evaluation processes affected by AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6fa05c618cc92c392c091a0299038b25</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_57.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Persons with Disabilities">
      <data key="d0">Persons with Disabilities</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Persons with Disabilities are individuals whose access to social and environmental opportunities is enhanced through AI-based solutions.&lt;SEP&gt;Persons with disabilities are highlighted as a group that may face discrimination due to biases in AI systems used for employment.&lt;SEP&gt;Persons with disabilities refer to individuals who have physical, mental, intellectual, or sensory impairments that hinder their full and effective participation in society.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-33366c5df404f37775ccbf3ec455b578&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7912c5a4fb8a11a998bec401999088b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fa05c618cc92c392c091a0299038b25</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_57.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_80.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_142.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657841</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Racial or Ethnic Origins">
      <data key="d0">Racial or Ethnic Origins</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Racial or ethnic origins refer to demographic groups that may experience discrimination as a result of AI systems in workplace decision-making.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6fa05c618cc92c392c091a0299038b25</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_57.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Systems in Employment">
      <data key="d0">AI Systems in Employment</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">AI Systems in Employment refers to the use of artificial intelligence technologies in various HR practices, including recruitment, management, and evaluation of job candidates and employees.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6fa05c618cc92c392c091a0299038b25</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_57.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Workers">
      <data key="d0">Workers</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Workers are individuals who are employed or provide services, often in contexts affected by AI systems in recruitment and management.&lt;SEP&gt;Workers are individuals who are impacted by regulations concerning workplace conditions and their rights regarding the use of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c664ec81872dda212b64d449aa7a2014&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fa05c618cc92c392c091a0299038b25</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_57.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_92.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747464883</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Self-Employment">
      <data key="d0">Self-Employment</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Self-Employment refers to the status of individuals who work for themselves rather than being employed by a company or organization, potentially influenced by AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6fa05c618cc92c392c091a0299038b25</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_57.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Discrimination Against Specific Groups">
      <data key="d0">Discrimination Against Specific Groups</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Discrimination Against Specific Groups refers to unfair treatment experienced by individuals based on characteristics such as gender, age, disability, race, or sexual orientation, particularly in the context of AI-driven systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6fa05c618cc92c392c091a0299038b25</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_57.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Protection">
      <data key="d0">Data Protection</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Data Protection involves safeguarding personal information, which can be compromised by AI systems monitoring workplace behavior.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6fa05c618cc92c392c091a0299038b25</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_57.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Privacy Rights">
      <data key="d0">Privacy Rights</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Privacy Rights refer to the fundamental entitlements pertaining to the protection of personal data and privacy, potentially undermined by workplace AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6fa05c618cc92c392c091a0299038b25</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_57.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation on Artificial Intelligence">
      <data key="d0">Regulation on Artificial Intelligence</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Regulation on Artificial Intelligence aims to provide a uniform legal framework for AI systems in the Union, promoting trustworthy AI while ensuring protection of fundamental rights and health.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6c2f867de2be6cb439557f91700b051c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_1.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Charter of Fundamental Rights of the European Union">
      <data key="d0">Charter of Fundamental Rights of the European Union</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The Charter of Fundamental Rights outlines fundamental rights and freedoms in the EU, relevant to ensuring rights when dealing with AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6c2f867de2be6cb439557f91700b051c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_1.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Artificial Intelligence Systems">
      <data key="d0">Artificial Intelligence Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Artificial Intelligence Systems include various types of AI technologies that can be categorized by their risk level, significantly impacting society and industries.&lt;SEP&gt;Artificial Intelligence Systems refer to technologies or applications that can perform tasks typically requiring human intelligence, which are being regulated under the AI Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6c2f867de2be6cb439557f91700b051c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c14e1756e1d8d71ac3ba07125f122da</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_1.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_165.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657067</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union Values">
      <data key="d0">Union Values</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Union Values encompass principles fundamental to the European Union such as democracy, the rule of law, and respect for human rights, guiding the implementation of AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Union values include respect for human dignity, freedom, equality, democracy, and the rule of law, as outlined in the Charter.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-14f663363e3d8f01aa5c0b361bddc380&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c2f867de2be6cb439557f91700b051c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_28.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_1.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747658099</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Civil Protection Authorities">
      <data key="d0">Civil Protection Authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Civil Protection Authorities are agencies focused on protecting citizens from crises, which can include the use of AI systems without prior authorization during emergencies.&lt;SEP&gt;Civil Protection Authorities are agencies that respond to emergencies and threats to public safety, and may authorize the use of high-risk AI systems in urgent situations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-878d589bc7b69ae2d9c3a44284a1badc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e07ee6b3452d764ccd9733dceadb1ac7</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_46.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_130.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657660</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Public Security">
      <data key="d0">Public Security</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Public Security involves measures and actions taken to ensure the safety and protection of individuals and communities from serious threats and emergencies.&lt;SEP&gt;Public Security is a situation that necessitates the use of AI technologies without prior compliance if life and health are at immediate risk.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-878d589bc7b69ae2d9c3a44284a1badc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e07ee6b3452d764ccd9733dceadb1ac7</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_46.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_130.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657660</data>
    </node>
    <node id="15 calendar days">
      <data key="d0">15 calendar days</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">15 calendar days is the duration within which Member States can raise objections to authorisations issued for high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d4c7e75432b8ffa8e0b96687dc4dd380</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_46.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Authorisation">
      <data key="d0">Authorisation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Authorisation refers to the official permission or approval granted by the Commission regarding the use of AI systems within regulatory frameworks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-13bd6c41d609ae7976a7b3ac4ab8e3fa</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_46.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Governance and Management Practices">
      <data key="d0">Data Governance and Management Practices</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Data governance and management practices are essential procedures for handling training, validation, and testing data sets, focusing on quality, representation, and compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;Data governance and management practices are frameworks and procedures implemented to manage data quality, privacy, and compliance with legal standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2fde742696dfc1372a034cc9cadcb58d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-445327adc051facf545b6358f6f01466</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_67.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_10.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657792</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Testing Data Sets">
      <data key="d0">Testing Data Sets</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Testing data sets are employed to evaluate the final performance of AI models in real-world scenarios, ensuring they are robust and reliable.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2fde742696dfc1372a034cc9cadcb58d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_10.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Quality Criteria">
      <data key="d0">Data Quality Criteria</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Data quality criteria refer to the standards that training, validation, and testing data sets must meet to be deemed suitable for high-risk AI uses.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2fde742696dfc1372a034cc9cadcb58d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_10.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Bias Detection Measures">
      <data key="d0">Bias Detection Measures</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Bias detection measures are procedures to identify and mitigate biases that could adversely affect AI systems, especially in regards to fairness and safety.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2fde742696dfc1372a034cc9cadcb58d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_10.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Geographical Context">
      <data key="d0">Geographical Context</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Geographical context refers to the characteristics of the physical location that may impact the functioning and development of high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2fde742696dfc1372a034cc9cadcb58d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_10.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Special Categories of Personal Data">
      <data key="d0">Special Categories of Personal Data</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Special categories of personal data are sensitive types of personal data requiring enhanced protection measures due to their nature.&lt;SEP&gt;Special categories of personal data include sensitive information that requires additional safeguards during processing in high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Special categories of personal data refer to sensitive information requiring additional protections, such as data on race, health, or sexual orientation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-68df7ac042ba1913236779113868f934&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fde742696dfc1372a034cc9cadcb58d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0639a0bd62e8b0bbe41bc1bee4a3098</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_10.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Sets">
      <data key="d0">Data Sets</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Data sets are collections of data meant for training, validation, and testing high-risk AI systems, aimed at ensuring their effectiveness and accuracy.&lt;SEP&gt;Data sets are collections of data used for training and testing AI systems, crucial for ensuring the effectiveness and fairness of machine learning algorithms.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d7eb8204c84c6a7310e75effed716fcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0639a0bd62e8b0bbe41bc1bee4a3098</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_67.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_10.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657792</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EU Regulations 2016/679 and 2018/1725">
      <data key="d0">EU Regulations 2016/679 and 2018/1725</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">These EU Regulations govern the processing and protection of personal data, ensuring privacy and security in data handling.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a0639a0bd62e8b0bbe41bc1bee4a3098</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_10.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Gaps">
      <data key="d0">Data Gaps</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Data gaps refer to the shortcomings in data collection and management that hinder compliance with relevant regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a0639a0bd62e8b0bbe41bc1bee4a3098</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_10.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Bias Detection and Correction">
      <data key="d0">Bias Detection and Correction</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Bias Detection and Correction refers to the processes and methodologies used to identify and rectify biases in data, particularly in relation to personal data processing.&lt;SEP&gt;Bias detection and correction are processes required to identify and mitigate any biases in AI systems to ensure fairness and accuracy in data processing.&lt;SEP&gt;Bias detection and correction involves identifying and mitigating biases in AI systems to ensure fairness and prevent discrimination.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-602b68fe088482c0037845fc0b520c30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68df7ac042ba1913236779113868f934&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0639a0bd62e8b0bbe41bc1bee4a3098</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_10.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_70.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747464901</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Statistical Properties">
      <data key="d0">Statistical Properties</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Statistical properties are characteristics that data sets must possess to be deemed adequate for the intended purposes of high-risk AI systems, including representation and accuracy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a0639a0bd62e8b0bbe41bc1bee4a3098</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_10.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Individuals and Groups">
      <data key="d0">Individuals and Groups</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Individuals and groups refer to the people whose data may be processed by high-risk AI systems, requiring specific considerations to ensure their rights are protected.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a0639a0bd62e8b0bbe41bc1bee4a3098</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_10.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Pseudonymisation">
      <data key="d0">Pseudonymisation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Pseudonymisation is a data management process that replaces private identifiers with artificial identifiers to protect individuals' identities.&lt;SEP&gt;Pseudonymisation is a data processing technique that replaces private identifiers with artificial identifiers to protect personal data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-68df7ac042ba1913236779113868f934&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0639a0bd62e8b0bbe41bc1bee4a3098</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_10.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Access Control Measures">
      <data key="d0">Access Control Measures</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Access control measures are protocols put in place to restrict access to personal data to authorized individuals only.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a0639a0bd62e8b0bbe41bc1bee4a3098</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_10.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive (EU) 2018/1725">
      <data key="d0">Directive (EU) 2018/1725</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive (EU) 2018/1725 relates to the processing of personal data within the EU institutions and bodies, complementing the GDPR.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-68df7ac042ba1913236779113868f934</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_10.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EU Regulations">
      <data key="d0">EU Regulations</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">EU Regulations refer to the series of legal frameworks established by the European Union to govern data protection, privacy, and other related issues.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-68df7ac042ba1913236779113868f934</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_10.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Security and Privacy-Preserving Measures">
      <data key="d0">Security and Privacy-Preserving Measures</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
