    </node>
    <node id="Biometric Systems">
      <data key="d0">Biometric Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Biometric systems are technologies that use biometric data for tasks such as identification, authentication, and categorization of individuals.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b65e9562dd645622f1390ba1863fee19</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_54.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747464903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Remote Biometric Identification">
      <data key="d0">Remote Biometric Identification</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Remote biometric identification refers to AI systems that identify individuals from a distance using biometric data, which may pose high-risk factors.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b65e9562dd645622f1390ba1863fee19</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_54.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747464903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Discriminatory Effects">
      <data key="d0">Discriminatory Effects</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Discriminatory effects arise when the use of biometric systems leads to biased outcomes based on attributes such as age, ethnicity, or disabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Discriminatory effects refer to potential biases that may arise from AI systems, particularly concerning age, ethnicity, and other attributes of natural persons.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b65e9562dd645622f1390ba1863fee19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab148daacc5693b15ec462635a5502a7</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_32.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_54.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657468</data>
    </node>
    <node id="High-Risk Classification">
      <data key="d0">High-Risk Classification</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">High-risk classification identifies biometric systems that pose significant risks related to bias and discrimination, necessitating stricter regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b65e9562dd645622f1390ba1863fee19</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_54.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747464903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Biometric Verification">
      <data key="d0">Biometric Verification</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Biometric verification is the one-to-one authentication process of confirming a person's identity based on their biometric data.&lt;SEP&gt;Biometric verification is the process by which a biometric system confirms the identity of a person based on their biometric data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b65e9562dd645622f1390ba1863fee19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ac98f64f8751ad51246ca16d843f030</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_54.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657195</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Authentication Systems">
      <data key="d0">Authentication Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Authentication systems use biometric data strictly to verify an individual's identity for access to services or secure areas.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b65e9562dd645622f1390ba1863fee19</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_54.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747464903</data>
    </node>
