    <node id="Legal Authority">
      <data key="d0">Legal Authority</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Legal Authority refers to the individuals who are responsible for registering AI systems and have the legal power to represent either the provider or deployer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-72498ec90c19419f10373dde7e7b51b3</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_71.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747464916</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Migration and Asylum">
      <data key="d0">Migration and Asylum</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Migration and asylum refer to the processes and policies governing the movement of individuals across borders and their legal protections.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f736e1ff707eaba05079b0f194d8a123</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_159.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747464919</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Border Control Management">
      <data key="d0">Border Control Management</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Border control management includes practices and regulations that govern the entry and exit of individuals at national borders.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f736e1ff707eaba05079b0f194d8a123</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_159.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747464919</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Administration of Justice">
      <data key="d0">Administration of Justice</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Administration of justice involves legal processes and frameworks that uphold the rule of law and protect citizens' rights.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f736e1ff707eaba05079b0f194d8a123</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_159.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747464919</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Accessibility Formats">
      <data key="d0">Accessibility Formats</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Accessibility Formats describe the ways information is made available to ensure that people with disabilities can understand notifications related to AI interactions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-eb43ec5a01dc502046ab6ffbe3a25504</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_132.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747464929</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Disabilities">
      <data key="d0">Disabilities</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Disabilities refer to various physical or mental conditions that can hinder individuals' daily activities and participation in society.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-aab48a13d1c4363ad8edd440c125d4a3</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_132.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747464929</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Inclusion">
      <data key="d0">Inclusion</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-aab48a13d1c4363ad8edd440c125d4a3</data>
      <data key="d2">Disabilities are often a focal point for discussions on social inclusion and accessibility for individuals with limitations.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_132.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747464929</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Accessibility">
      <data key="d0">Accessibility</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c7912c5a4fb8a11a998bec401999088b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aab48a13d1c4363ad8edd440c125d4a3</data>
      <data key="d2">Accessibility relates to the design of products and environments that enhance opportunities for Persons with Disabilities through the use of AI.&lt;SEP&gt;Efforts to improve accessibility are driven by the need to support individuals with disabilities in various environments.</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_132.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_142.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657841</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Distributor">
      <data key="d0">Distributor</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A distributor is a person in the supply chain who makes an AI system available on the Union market, not including the provider or importer.&lt;SEP&gt;A distributor is a third-party entity responsible for providing goods, which in this context refers to high-risk AI systems, and must adhere to legal obligations when placing them on the market.&lt;SEP&gt;A distributor is an individual or organization in the supply chain that makes AI systems available on the Union market.&lt;SEP&gt;Distributors are entities responsible for making high-risk AI systems available in the market and must notify relevant authorities of any non-compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6a8bd64d122f5a09e9e3859bf77c6931&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dbd41da6ea2a77fff5beb18c8e7c896&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a21678b36bef336bf18e091bdfdb68f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7d62750f1113d24ac155fcd2b2ef02c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_84.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_24.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657382</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Importer">
      <data key="d0">Importer</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">An importer is a person in the Union who places an AI system developed by a third country's entity onto the market.&lt;SEP&gt;An importer is an individual or organization in the Union that places AI systems from third countries on the market.&lt;SEP&gt;An importer is an organization or individual that brings goods into a country from abroad, and in this context, it refers to the importation of high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Importers are entities that bring high-risk AI systems into a market, responsible for ensuring compliance with local regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6a8bd64d122f5a09e9e3859bf77c6931&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dbd41da6ea2a77fff5beb18c8e7c896&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a21678b36bef336bf18e091bdfdb68f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7d62750f1113d24ac155fcd2b2ef02c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_84.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_24.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657382</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Trademark">
      <data key="d0">Trademark</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A trademark is a recognizable sign, design, or expression that distinguishes products or services of a particular source, relevant in the context of high-risk AI systems being attributed to a provider.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6a8bd64d122f5a09e9e3859bf77c6931</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_84.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657053</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Modification">
      <data key="d0">Modification</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Modification refers to changes made to existing high-risk AI systems, which can affect their compliance with legal obligations and classification.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6a8bd64d122f5a09e9e3859bf77c6931</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_84.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657053</data>
    </node>
    <node id="General-Purpose AI System">
      <data key="d0">General-Purpose AI System</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A general-purpose AI system is an AI technology that may not be initially classified as high-risk but can become one under certain modifications or intended uses.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6a8bd64d122f5a09e9e3859bf77c6931</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_84.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657053</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Trade Unions">
      <data key="d0">Trade Unions</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Trade Unions represent workers' rights and interests and may engage in the dialogue surrounding the development of AI systems and their impacts on labor.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0c14e1756e1d8d71ac3ba07125f122da</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_165.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657067</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Consumer Protection Organisations">
      <data key="d0">Consumer Protection Organisations</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Consumer Protection Organisations advocate for consumer rights and safety, often addressing concerns related to technology such as AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0c14e1756e1d8d71ac3ba07125f122da</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_165.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657067</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Research Organisations">
      <data key="d0">Research Organisations</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Research Organisations are entities that conduct studies and advancements in various fields, including AI, and contribute to the ethical development of such technologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0c14e1756e1d8d71ac3ba07125f122da</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_165.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657067</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Low-Risk AI Systems">
      <data key="d0">Low-Risk AI Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Low-Risk AI Systems are AI applications that do not pose significant risks and can operate under less stringent ethical requirements and oversight.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0c14e1756e1d8d71ac3ba07125f122da</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_165.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657078</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Voluntary Requirements">
      <data key="d0">Voluntary Requirements</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Voluntary Requirements are not mandatory standards that AI Providers may adopt to promote ethical practices in the development and use of their systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0c14e1756e1d8d71ac3ba07125f122da</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_165.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657078</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Key Performance Indicators">
      <data key="d0">Key Performance Indicators</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Key Performance Indicators are metrics used to measure the effectiveness and progress of AI Providers in achieving their ethical objectives.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0c14e1756e1d8d71ac3ba07125f122da</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_165.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657078</data>
    </node>
    <node id="business and civil society organisations">
      <data key="d0">business and civil society organisations</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Business and civil society organisations refer to various groups involved in societal and economic activities, contributing to the development of key performance indicators and other initiatives.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a811acaf13b6420a717f6aa21a6ed331</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_165.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657080</data>
    </node>
    <node id="academia">
      <data key="d0">academia</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Academia encompasses universities and research institutions, playing a vital role in developing knowledge and initiatives related to AI and data usage.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a811acaf13b6420a717f6aa21a6ed331</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_165.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657080</data>
    </node>
    <node id="research organisations">
      <data key="d0">research organisations</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Research organisations are entities focused on scientific investigation and analysis, contributing to the development of objectives and performance metrics for AI.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a811acaf13b6420a717f6aa21a6ed331</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_165.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1747657080</data>
    </node>
    <node id="trade unions">
      <data key="d0">trade unions</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Trade unions represent workers’ interests and are stakeholders in discussions related to economic policies and performance indicators.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a811acaf13b6420a717f6aa21a6ed331</data>
