    <edge source="Market Surveillance Authority" target="Member State">
      <data key="d6">59.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Market Surveillance Authority is an entity that operates within each Member State, tasked with overseeing the compliance of artificial intelligence (AI) systems in accordance with European Union (EU) regulations. Each Member State has its own dedicated Market Surveillance Authority, which is responsible for ensuring that market regulations are enforced, particularly concerning the testing of high-risk AI systems.

The primary role of the Market Surveillance Authority includes monitoring AI systems to ensure they comply with applicable regulations. This involves conducting compliance evaluations and reporting findings to the Member State, especially in cases where non-compliance could impact the national territory. The Market Surveillance Authority plays a crucial role in safeguarding public welfare by ensuring that AI technologies operate within the legal frameworks set forth by the EU and the respective Member States.</data>
      <data key="d8">authority,communication,compliance,enforcement,local governance,member compliance,national authority,national oversight,national regulation,oversight,regulatory authority,regulatory body,regulatory oversight</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-ff61ec794793cf787d4a0473487a06f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cb2802f1b508b813d06e58ae27a1f77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddb5ca2a2f12bb39286916d398b70ed9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa9e2916955e882c73231ed69851f6ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28daf57045ce50f0bd160cddd41ffc14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee6d94a5f64203f09d02387acbdb39c5</data>
      <data key="d10">./cached_docs/article_81.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_60.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_83.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_79.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1747657580</data>
    </edge>
