    <edge source="Market Surveillance Authority" target="Cross-Border Cases">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Market surveillance authorities must handle cross-border cases by cooperating and sharing information under established regulations.</data>
      <data key="d8">jurisdictional cooperation, regulatory challenges</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-0b90abf0636c26d546e9b6724e3224ae</data>
      <data key="d10">./cached_docs/recital_161.json</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Market Surveillance Authority" target="Commission">
      <data key="d6">65.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Commission and the Market Surveillance Authority work collaboratively to oversee the regulation and safety of AI systems within Member States. Market Surveillance Authorities are mandated to submit annual reports to the Commission detailing the usage of biometric systems and must also communicate their findings and objections regarding various measures for the Commission's evaluation and decision-making. The Commission plays a crucial role in consulting with the Market Surveillance Authority to assess the AI practices enacted by Member States, ensuring that these systems are safe for public use. Furthermore, the Market Surveillance Authority operates under the regulatory guidance of the Commission and is responsible for implementing or withdrawing the Commission's decisions regarding authorizations. Additionally, the Market Surveillance Authority must inform the Commission of any compliance issues and the measures taken to address them for AI systems. This systematic approach helps facilitate a thorough oversight process, promoting safety and compliance in AI technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;The Commission establishes implementing acts that market surveillance authorities must follow when approving AI testing plans.&lt;SEP&gt;The Market Surveillance Authority informs the Commission about the results of evaluations conducted on AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance,compliance evaluation,compliance reporting,enforcement,oversight,regulatory authority,regulatory communication,regulatory compliance,regulatory consultation,regulatory oversight,reporting</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-a64bfb94635a0df2f808b2f8a494bd3e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff61ec794793cf787d4a0473487a06f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2187eb3476528ac7c75b571eb3844f0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2440fb0070f3198e96bd1ad753ae3e0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13bd6c41d609ae7976a7b3ac4ab8e3fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee6d94a5f64203f09d02387acbdb39c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ad9c740a10a5c1577e578a593bd61fd</data>
      <data key="d10">./cached_docs/article_60.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_82.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_46.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_36.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_80.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_81.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_79.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1747658096</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Market Surveillance Authority" target="Health and Safety">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The authority ensures that AI systems do not compromise health and safety, addressing risks as mandated by regulation.</data>
      <data key="d8">health risks, safety measures</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-2440fb0070f3198e96bd1ad753ae3e0a</data>
