    <edge source="Regulation" target="Union">
      <data key="d6">53.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Regulation is a legislative framework enacted to govern activities related to AI systems within the Union. It applies to all operators operating within the Union, creating a unified approach to regulating AI technologies across its member states. The primary objective of the Regulation is to enforce rules that protect individuals' rights, ensuring that the usage of AI systems respects these rights within the context of the Union. The Union is tasked with the responsibility of adopting the Regulation in order to achieve overarching goals that cannot be fulfilled by individual Member States acting alone. Additionally, the Regulation outlines important guidelines concerning consumer protection and the responsible usage of AI within the Union.</data>
      <data key="d8">EU governance,compliance,governance,jurisdiction,legal framework,legal governance,organizational responsibility,protection of rights,regulatory framework</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-714d9f621f6eee9273625419653b083c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0455405f9e173535e78c4ea589745cf4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3d60cf6cbe0ae91a9793cb5c98a4a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63ef16386f45c7bc364061cc094254fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e78bce1eaa5df9c186492b5e1482218&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5928be36056ac91865bd3e4d596159e</data>
      <data key="d10">./cached_docs/recital_176.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_1.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_22.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_2.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_62.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_21.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1747464671</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Regulation" target="AI Systems">
      <data key="d6">156.0</data>
      <data key="d7">AI Systems are subject to comprehensive regulations that dictate their use, particularly for biometric identification in public spaces within law enforcement. The Regulation establishes a robust framework for overseeing and managing AI Systems, with a significant emphasis on high-risk categories necessitating thorough scrutiny. It categorizes AI systems into high-risk and non-high-risk classes based on their intended applications and use cases, thereby establishing targeted rules and requirements for their deployment and management.

Under the Regulation, AI Systems are mandated to comply with specific legal standards, which include safety and accountability measures aimed at protecting individuals in the Union. This compliance is crucial for AI systems placed on the market, ensuring they fulfill established obligations and legal requirements.

Moreover, the Regulation governs both the operational aspects of AI systems and their adaptation, particularly focusing on high-risk applications that may affect market continuity. It also delineates permissible uses of AI systems across military and civilian contexts, providing clear guidelines for governance and compliance.

Notably, the Regulation specifies that AI systems developed for scientific research are exempt from certain regulatory frameworks, which affects how research is conducted in this area. Additionally, high-risk AI Systems designated as medical devices must adhere to the Regulation to guarantee safety and efficacy.

Overall, the Regulation plays a critical role in defining the objectives and contextual operations of AI Systems, ensuring their responsible and secure deployment across various sectors, including public administration and law enforcement.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulations are put in place to govern the use of AI systems, ensuring they operate within ethical and fair guidelines.&lt;SEP&gt;High-risk AI Systems are subject to the Regulation intended to ensure their responsible use and compliance with legal frameworks.</data>
      <data key="d8">AI governance,AI usage,classification,compliance,compliance standards,ethical standards,governance,legal framework,legislation,operational standards,regulation,regulatory compliance,regulatory framework,regulatory provisions,regulatory standards,research exclusion,risk assessment,risk management,technology governance,technology oversight</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-907dfa7ec80255255b81cd50cd6a4494&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c1d05b847c03fe702172f787883fc33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b31c82fb046f107cbfab945a92431bbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ffd8df9d8eb9625dca23bc5f974e025&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc1203d6797827fbb6dbb7dc7c8d7d26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83f37d4143e19486af167d7acee5bee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7eb8204c84c6a7310e75effed716fcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40e75ee11aa912f1497b2a91ae655e7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e78bce1eaa5df9c186492b5e1482218&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b8c1122e1044e4445aa96d7fa6d5b6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1b92a727425c41637e16da3cb9ac9c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee1f186f5aed070bc8e6e813caed9967&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5981afe4b9fb547c64f49e76b1d9c0a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2315cd7abb88dee440f081de5430a32f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5928be36056ac91865bd3e4d596159e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cac929d0048fe34377179e8ecde4a5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b89491b02af0a00cbc13f9e8df827a6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8e23760d52ebfb589b4de63afe8ab83</data>
      <data key="d10">./cached_docs/recital_157.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_53.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_84.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_25.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_97.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_177.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_67.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_111.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_12.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_24.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_38.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_58.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_118.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_1.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_174.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_22.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1747657985</data>
    </edge>
