      <data key="d10">./cached_docs/article_2.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_137.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1747464663</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Union" target="Member States">
      <data key="d6">59.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Member States are integral constituents of the Union, playing a crucial role in the implementation and compliance with regulations set forth by the Union, particularly concerning AI systems. These Member States are required to align their policies and actions with common objectives established by the Union, ensuring that regulations governing AI systems and their deployment are duly observed. Furthermore, the Union collaborates with Member States to enforce compliance with various rights, including disability rights, and to promote equality across sectors.

The Union is formed by these Member States, which not only engage in the legislative process but also work together to ensure adherence to laws and regulations that protect workers and govern the use of AI technologies. This collaborative effort helps to create a coherent framework for SME regulations and AI governance, highlighting the importance of both cooperation and compliance in achieving shared goals.</data>
      <data key="d8">10,collaboration,legal compliance,legal framework,member collaboration,membership,policy alignment,policy enforcement,political collaboration,political organization,regulatory enforcement,regulatory oversight</data>
