    <edge source="Commission" target="European Parliament">
      <data key="d6">82.0</data>
      <data key="d7">"The Commission reports to the European Parliament regarding assessments and evaluations of regulations."}&lt;SEP&gt;The Commission and the European Parliament play crucial roles in the legislative process of the European Union, particularly concerning regulations on artificial intelligence (AI) systems. The Commission is responsible for ensuring that the European Parliament is actively involved in the preparation of delegated acts, providing documentation to the Parliament at the same time as it is shared with Member States' experts. Furthermore, the Commission is mandated to report to the European Parliament on the enforcement assessment of AI regulations, and it submits evaluation reports that are integral to shaping legislation related to AI.

Together, the European Parliament and the Commission collaborate to evaluate and implement regulations affecting AI systems, thereby influencing EU legislation. Importantly, the European Parliament holds the authority to revoke the powers granted to the Commission regarding delegated acts, emphasizing the Parliament's role in overseeing and regulating the Commission's activities in the legislative framework. Overall, this partnership is pivotal in shaping laws and regulations governing artificial intelligence in the EU.&lt;SEP&gt;The Commission collaborates with the European Parliament on legislation related to AI systems and metrology standards.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Parliament works alongside the Commission in legislative action, particularly in relation to the adoption of regulations like those governing standardisation.&lt;SEP&gt;The Commission works under the guidance of the European Parliament to implement directives like the Directive (EU) 2016/943."&lt;&lt;"institutional oversight, directive implementation</data>
