    <edge source="Commission" target="AI Office">
      <data key="d6">146.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The AI Office acts under the Commission's authority to monitor compliance and enforce rules for AI providers.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI Office and the Commission work closely together to oversee the regulation and compliance of AI model providers in accordance with established regulations. The Commission, which supervises and enhances the expertise of the AI Office, empowers it to monitor activities related to general-purpose AI models that pose systemic risks. The AI Office operates under the guidance of the Commission and is responsible for developing methodologies that aid in the assessment and evaluation of AI systems. These methodologies assist the Commission in its regulatory actions and proposals.

Within this collaborative framework, the Commission evaluates both the performance and resources of the AI Office to ensure the effective implementation of regulations. The AI Office is entrusted with specific tasks that uphold its organizational authority, including the responsibility to inform the Commission about risk assessments and measures regarding AI models. This reflects a hierarchy in their joint efforts to maintain safety and efficacy in AI technologies.

The AI Office also has the capacity to propose dialogues and commitments to the Commission concerning systemic risks associated with AI models. Through their cooperative dynamic, both entities are committed to fostering compliance and ensuring the responsible oversight of AI technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI Office can request updates from the Commission, denoting interaction between the two organizations.</data>
