    <edge source="European Parliament" target="Regulation (EU) 2024/1689">
      <data key="d6">106.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The European Parliament enacted Regulation (EU) 2024/1689, establishing a comprehensive legislative framework governing artificial intelligence (AI) within the European Union. This regulation sets forth rules and standards for the development and implementation of AI systems, significantly influencing existing regulations associated with AI technologies. The European Parliament played a pivotal role in the creation, discussion, and approval of this regulation, ensuring adherence to legislative processes throughout its development. 

Through its actions, the European Parliament has demonstrated its commitment to regulating emerging technologies by prioritizing both innovation and the protection of citizens' rights. Its involvement in the legislative process was essential for crafting and enacting the regulation, enabling it to effectively address the complexities and challenges posed by artificial intelligence. By adopting Regulation (EU) 2024/1689, the European Parliament reinforces its legislative authority and its intention to govern AI responsibly within the EU.</data>
      <data key="d8">AI governance,EU governance,governance,governance regulation,legislation,legislative authority,legislative body,legislative process,regulation adoption,regulation of AI,regulatory creation</data>
