    <edge source="Regulation (EU) 2019/1020" target="Market Surveillance Authorities">
      <data key="d6">62.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Market Surveillance Authorities are tasked with ensuring compliance with EU regulations under Regulation (EU) 2019/1020. They are required to report relevant information to the European Commission regarding this compliance, thereby playing a crucial role in monitoring and enforcing regulations concerning various products within the EU market. The activities and responsibilities of these authorities are defined by the guidelines and provisions laid out in Regulation (EU) 2019/1020, which outlines their powers and the framework within which they operate. Overall, Market Surveillance Authorities function to uphold market regulations and ensure that products meet the necessary compliance standards set by the EU.&lt;SEP&gt;Market surveillance authorities operate under the framework of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 to ensure compliance with AI regulations.</data>
      <data key="d8">7&lt;SEP&gt;9&lt;SEP&gt;legal enforcement, regulation&lt;SEP&gt;regulatory framework, compliance&lt;SEP&gt;regulatory framework, market compliance&lt;SEP&gt;regulatory framework, oversight&lt;SEP&gt;reporting, compliance</data>
