    <edge source="Market Surveillance Authorities" target="Member States">
      <data key="d6">45.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Market Surveillance Authorities operate under the regulations established by Member States to ensure compliance with AI testing standards. These authorities are designated by Member States to carry out enforcement roles as mandated by relevant regulations. Member States communicate with these authorities to share vital information regarding compliance with the testing standards of AI systems. Furthermore, they play a crucial role in facilitating coordination among Market Surveillance Authorities, ensuring that they effectively enforce Union harmonization legislation and adhere to regulatory requirements. This collaborative approach underscores the commitment of Member States to uphold stringent compliance and enforcement measures within the realm of AI regulation.</data>
      <data key="d8">7,compliance,cooperation,information sharing,law enforcement,organizational structure,regulatory collaboration,regulatory framework,regulatory oversight</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-c0711090702fd9b1787822998d5deac9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53fb2685a38836a165fa7637bbbadce2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f12c01099dadb1fc1008ce18c7d800e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc8a3a685818e1a12850434d4ddcb5cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4518ca313d8493e277775e1a9267b84d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43a1516ad8d48077af0d59fc01578f33</data>
