    <edge source="Member States" target="AI Office">
      <data key="d6">60.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Member States may be involved in discussions or initiatives led by the AI Office to align AI-related policies with their interests.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI Office and Member States work collaboratively to enhance the regulation and governance of artificial intelligence (AI) systems. Member States play a crucial role in facilitating the operations and tasks assigned to the AI Office by the Commission. This partnership is essential for enforcing regulations pertaining to general-purpose AI models. 

The AI Office assists Member States in implementing regulatory sandboxes, which allow for the testing of AI technologies within a controlled environment, while also supporting the development of necessary expertise in the field. Together, they focus on establishing and evolving comprehensive regulatory frameworks tailored to AI systems.

Moreover, the AI Office collaborates with Member States to create effective governance mechanisms for AI technologies, ensuring that the development of codes of conduct for these systems considers specific local interests and regulatory requirements. Through these efforts, the AI Office and Member States aim to promote a responsible and adaptable approach to AI regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI Office works collaboratively with Member States to facilitate the development and implementation of AI capabilities.</data>
      <data key="d8">collaboration,cooperation,governance,governance collaboration,policy alignment,regulatory framework,regulatory interaction,regulatory support,support</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-21c742eff7a2b610bb01c8c0ec233b62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-064e3e5273a81cd8d9a47da9a3f51240&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6579442a2f027e643cf907006333003a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40f3761e589fb7702938fd4fbbecfdcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-577494efd5ce842563e6974b0da9707b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00e7606a0fa9d588f18d67d02cfcf654&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e6a5cc59273abbe42c743808026477c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f892644f7a3eab6b024d8a386777f23</data>
