    <edge source="Member States" target="National Competent Authorities">
      <data key="d6">47.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Member States play a crucial role in the governance and regulatory framework related to artificial intelligence (AI) technologies within the European Union. They are responsible for appointing National Competent Authorities which are tasked with ensuring the effective implementation and enforcement of regulations. These authorities operate under the guidance and requirements set by the Member States to ensure adherence to regulatory standards concerning AI and data protection.

Additionally, Member States delegate the responsibility for establishing the necessary regulatory structures to these National Competent Authorities, thus facilitating effective governance of AI technologies. The Member States also play a pivotal role in overseeing the compliance with EU regulations by designating the National Competent Authorities that monitor AI Regulatory Sandboxes, further underscoring their importance in maintaining regulatory oversight and governance within the framework of AI technologies.</data>
      <data key="d8">7,8,authority function,compliance,government structure,national responsibilities,regulatory implementation,regulatory oversight</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-d42aaf56c15be020feabced14d2409d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0779dfb4a5c0f82f05a67985fe0224a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cdf1c7e7ad7fe2c6b1b8f1b0b12db35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dbe8a4749b15b91fcb1062fee4fa778&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-475967c83e624bc711a9ff13e8150163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97ee5867d3c03f24001b650ad752686d</data>
